{"parentUuid":"44124232-3ee1-494a-9b47-4066748f881c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJ6tSQdqUystAA3j6uhi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, nothing was published. The release PR #46 merged at 15:50:58 UTC, and \"Release & Publish\" (run 39808667033) failed in its first job, \"Identify a merged Callisto release PR\", 31 seconds later. One of its GitHub API calls returned an empty body, so the build and publish jobs were skipped.\n\nIt looks transient. I ran the job's three API calls just now and they all succeed:\n- the commit `a5a878f9` resolves\n- it's verified\n- it maps to exactly one merged release PR, #46 from `callisto/version-packages`\n\nSo re-running the failed run should go through. That would build and publish the packages; there may also be an approval step on \"Execute approved release\". Should I run `gh run rerun 39808667033 --failed`?\n\n**Separately (not your question):** my local test run is still going. The slow `compile_fail` test is rebuilding dependencies after a branch switch; nothing in the namespace re-export work has failed so far."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":695899,"output_tokens":403,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":89},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":794,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":403,"cache_read_input_tokens":695899,"cache_creation_input_tokens":794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":794},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a5da87fe-32ab-492c-9061-6c4b74a96786","