{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":981,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"a62336cd-8c0e-46a9-b52b-1b10cf250de2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJA1hgBwK3r2ToDKVzts","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4372,"cache_read_input_tokens":708679,"output_tokens":1246,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":497},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4372,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":708679,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4372},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":12851,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"01612878-a358-430a-831e-f9a7f33858dd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgJA1hKs3PwPs1b3CqzJ2","requestRef":"94d5ccaa-ad75-4ac7-b4e0-0e738b0020a8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6add5d4-d22a-4480-92d4-caafdc27d7b6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T23:38:23.401Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/namespace-reexports","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"a6add5d4-d22a-4480-92d4-caafdc27d7b6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJA1hgBwK3r2ToDKVzts","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Short answer: **trybuild is the standard when the compiler's error message is part of your product (proc-macro crates). For guarding a type's API, the idiom is a `compile_fail` doctest**, or no test at all when privacy already enforces the rule.\n\n| Tool | Typical use | Cost |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **trybuild** | Proc-macro crates: serde_derive, thiserror, tokio's macros, anything built on `syn`. It saves the expected compiler output in a `.stderr` file, because those error messages are what users see. | A separate test crate built against every dependency. Slow on the first build and whenever `Cargo.lock` changes. |\n| **`compile_fail` doctest** | API guarantees on ordinary types (\"this can't be constructed / called\"); the standard library and most crates. | Compiled against the already-built crate by `cargo test --doc`. Fast, no extra dependency. |\n| **`static_assertions`** | Trait facts (`Send`, `Sync`, \"does *not* implement X\"). | Checked at compile time, nothing runs. |\n\n**A correction to what I said earlier:** pinning a `compile_fail` doctest to an error code (`compile_fail,E0451`) works only on nightly, and the rustdoc docs say it's unlikely ever to be stabilized. On stable, a `compile_fail` doctest passes on *any* compile error, including a typo in the example. The usual way to cover that is a twin example that *does* compile with the allowed path. Here that's `ParsedProp::new(...)`, which proves the imports and names are right, so the failing example can only fail on the struct literal.\n\nFor Caliper, I'd use the doctest pair:\n\n- a `compile_fail` example building `ParsedProp { .. }`\n- a compiling example using `ParsedProp::new`\n- both on `ParsedProp`'s doc comment, with trybuild and `tests/compile_fail/` removed\n\nIt guards the same thing (the private `_seal` field) with no separate dependency build. michi's case is different: many of its checks are about non-exhaustive matches and `#[must_use]`, where the exact compiler message is worth keeping, so trybuild is a reasonable fit there.\n\nWant me to make that change in Caliper as a small separate PR?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4372,"cache_read_input_tokens":708679,"output_tokens":1246,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":497},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4372,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":708679,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4372},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"01612878-a358-430a-831e-f9a7f33858dd","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgJA1hKs3PwPs1b3CqzJ2","requestRef":"94d5ccaa-ad75-4ac7-b4e0-0e738b0020a8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7e005dff-95b7-4358-b026-3183a65e9721","timestamp":"2026-10-22T23:38:23.581Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/namespace-reexports","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
