{"parentUuid":"86c216b1-8fe4-4179-ae01-983762ec1a0f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJAZ319QKFztezhr2Uw3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The re-run got further but the release is now **half published**. The npm half needs a change on your npm account.\n\n**Published to crates.io, version 0.3.0:**\n- `caliper-docgen-core` at 23:43:59 UTC\n- `caliper-docgen` at 23:44:27 UTC\n\n**Not published to npm.** The first npm package, `caliper-docgen-darwin-arm64@0.3.0`, was rejected:\n\n> 403 Forbidden … Two-factor authentication is required to publish this package but an automation token was specified\n\nAll the npm packages are still at 0.2.1. All five platform builds succeeded, so only publishing is blocked.\n\n**Cause:** the npm packages are set to \"require two-factor authentication and disallow tokens\", while the workflow publishes with an `NPM_TOKEN` automation token. Only you can change that, on npmjs.com.\n\n**Two fixes:**\n1. **Quick:** on npmjs.com, for each npm package (`caliper-docgen`, `caliper-docgen-napi`, `caliper-docgen-vite-plugin` and the platform packages), go to **Settings → Publishing access** and choose \"Require two-factor authentication or an automation or granular access token\".\n2. **Better:** set up npm trusted publishing, so GitHub Actions publishes through its OIDC identity with no stored token. Each package gets a trusted-publisher entry for `orin-dx/caliper` and the release workflow on npmjs.com, and the workflow needs `id-token: write` with no `NPM_TOKEN`. I can make the workflow change once you've configured the packages.\n\n**Before re-running:** the crates are already at 0.3.0 on crates.io, and I haven't checked whether Callisto's release step skips versions that are already published. If it doesn't, a plain re-run will fail at crates.io before reaching npm. I can check how Callisto handles that while you change the npm setting.\n\n**Pending from earlier:** should I switch Caliper's compile-fail test to the doctest pair, as a separate PR?\n\nneeds input: Change the npm publishing-access setting on the caliper-docgen packages (fix 1), or set up trusted publishing (fix 2), then tell me which so I can re-run or adjust the workflow."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3301,"cache_read_input_tokens":718416,"output_tokens":1324,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":583},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3301,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1324,"cache_read_input_tokens":718416,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3301},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b927c271-3a90-4b34-a7cd-a7ca8a71639c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgJAZ2YcKGbhSs8hDLXWh","requestRef":"f1f3e8f1-16ae-41f7-bf8a-2249327b6643","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0bbcbe86-6a1e-44bb-8669-d4c48527e04b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T23:45:27.915Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/namespace-reexports","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
