{"parentUuid":"a299992f-87f5-4d35-b24c-796b5f4fbc69","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJFMWvfdu7KJYfU4pfhY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011cZbGr54PKVqqEuDfXvPqc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr_body_callisto.md","content":"Callisto 0.11 stops the release after each npm publish: it checks for the new version about 30 seconds later, npm hasn't listed it yet, and the job exits with E157. Releasing 0.3.0 took one re-run per npm package. 0.12.0 waits up to 6 minutes for npm (2 for Cargo), and the wait also applies to a re-run that finds the version already published.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `release.yml` and `ci.yml`: Callisto's actions pinned to `callisto@0.12.0` (`c3d524d3`, the commit the annotated tag points to); `setup-callisto` installs `callisto@0.12.0`.\n- `callisto.toml`: the pin comment.\n\n## Checked\n\n- The three actions' inputs are identical in 0.11.0 and 0.12.0 (`setup-callisto`, `callisto-action`, `callisto-validate`).\n- `callisto.toml` already uses the `ecosystem/name` form 0.12 requires (E316/E317), and its fixed groups pair separate packages, not one package under two names (E250).\n- `callisto status --check` with the 0.12.0 binary passes on this branch.\n\nThe in-flight 0.3.0 release keeps running on 0.11; re-runs use the workflow the run started with.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1442,"cache_read_input_tokens":747602,"output_tokens":1318,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":174},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1442,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1318,"cache_read_input_tokens":747602,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1442,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1442},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011cZbGr54PKVqqEuDfXvPqc":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr_body_callisto.md","content":"Callisto 0.11 stops the release after each npm publish: it checks for the new version about 30 seconds later, npm hasn't listed it yet, and the job exits with E157. Releasing 0.3.0 took one re-run per npm package. 0.12.0 waits up to 6 minutes for npm (2 for Cargo), and the wait also applies to a re-run that finds the version already published.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `release.yml` and `ci.yml`: Callisto's actions pinned to `callisto@0.12.0` (`c3d524d3`, the commit the annotated tag points to); `setup-callisto` installs `callisto@0.12.0`.\n- `callisto.toml`: the pin comment.\n\n## Checked\n\n- The three actions' inputs are identical in 0.11.0 and 0.12.0 (`setup-callisto`, `callisto-action`, `callisto-validate`).\n- `callisto.toml` already uses the `ecosystem/name` form 0.12 requires (E316/E317), and its fixed groups pair separate packages, not one package under two names (E250).\n- `callisto status --check` with the 0.12.0 binary passes on this branch.\n\nThe in-flight 0.3.0 release keeps running on 0.11; re-runs use the workflow the run started with.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e65b1176-5712-4605-b6e9-2d35b100109c","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CgJFMWMw43ZsJiHA4UPZQ","requestRef":"201eb0ac-79e7-49ae-a6f7-ca2d698afc2f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7dcefa0d-60ad-4edd-845e-62e2abc3fbaa","timestamp":"2026-10-23T00:48:24.037Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoin