{"parentUuid":"3b78e3b4-cd0f-4d9c-a716-ae61830f7a6c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJFZv24ysGpexApqU1zQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not usably yet. Callisto 0.13.0 is on crates.io, but its release didn't finish on GitHub: there's no `callisto@0.13.0` tag and no GitHub release. The newest of each is still 0.12.0.\n\n- **Why that blocks us:** our workflows install Callisto through `setup-callisto` with `verification: require`. That needs a GitHub release asset carrying an attestation, and pinning the actions needs the release tag. Neither exists for 0.13.0, so a pin to it would fail at setup.\n- **Likely cause:** 0.13.0 added two new release targets (Intel macOS, arm64 Linux), and Callisto merged \"fix(release): assemble every target build, not a list of three\" (#318) at 00:25 UTC today. That looks like its release job broke on the new targets.\n- **Callisto's next release:** release PR #316 for 0.14.0 is open.\n- **0.13 doesn't affect us:** its changes are a release-PR wording tweak for pre-1.0 minors, a `publish-timeout` setting, a repository-mismatch warning, and the two new binaries. The npm propagation fix we need is already in 0.12.0.\n\nSo #98 stays on 0.12.0, and I'll bump again once Callisto publishes a tagged, attested 0.14 release. #98's CI passes.\n\n**0.3.0 release:** the background loop is still re-running the release one npm package at a time; I'll report when it finishes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1608,"cache_read_input_tokens":754438,"output_tokens":779,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":295},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1608,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":779,"cache