{"parentUuid":"3b9eb10c-3346-43c9-8073-2fd4b77dfdd0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJFv4coKn4uv5yBq69FL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The release is 8 of 13 npm packages in, and both crates are on crates.io. Five npm packages are left:\n\n- the `caliper-docgen-napi` package\n- 3 of its 5 platform packages (`linux-arm64-gnu`, `linux-x64-gnu`, `win32-x64-msvc`)\n- `caliper-docgen-vite-plugin`\n\nIt's slow because Callisto 0.11 publishes one package per attempt, then stops when npm hasn't listed it yet. Each attempt costs about 3–4 minutes of job setup plus a publish. The run is on attempt 11 now, so at that rate it needs about 15–20 more minutes.\n\nThere's no clearly faster path. A fresh release run on 0.12 would publish all five in one go, but it starts from scratch, including the five platform builds, which likely costs as much as the remaining attempts. Publishing by hand would bypass CI's provenance signing. So I'm letting the loop finish. #98 (pin Callisto 0.12.0) fixes this for every future release, and its CI is green, so it's ready to merge whenever you like."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1250,"cache_read_input_tokens":760156,"output_tokens":765,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":399},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1250,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":760156,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1250},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"45e91ae3-7606-4302-a71d