{"parentUuid":"90783432-30bf-48ed-aff9-e5c486c64bf9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7db10f65-cef1-428a-b158-fcc358310258","timestamp":"2026-10-23T02:51:44.250Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/namespace-reexports","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"d35a888e2aff9886b8d0ce4097e69f8d15299f2009aa16b51006f2b09bc14d1a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Recommendation on the collapse rule: **apply it to dependency sources only, the way Storybook does, and don't collapse sources declared in the project. Fix chakra's size with in-memory sharing, and expose the rule as an option.** Reasons:\n\n- **Storybook parity.** react-component-meta, Storybook 11's default, collapses only sources inside `node_modules` (or `.d.ts`) with more than 30 props. Collapsing project sources would hide props Storybook shows.\n- **Who sees what.** In an app that *uses* chakra or Mantine, those style props come from `node_modules`, so they collapse anyway. Only in the design system's own repo are they project sources. There they're the library's own API, and its authors want them listed.\n- **The chakra blow-up is a cost problem, not a display one.** About 665 props per component cost 2.4 s and 3.4 GB because each component holds its own copy. Sharing resolved props in memory (step 3) fixes the cost, and #95's prop table already makes the output small. Hiding data to save memory would lose precision.\n- **An escape hatch:** a `collapseInheritedProps: \"dependencies\" | \"all\" | \"none\"` option with a threshold, defaulting to `\"dependencies\"`.\n\nI'll build it that way unless you say otherwise.\n\nPlan for the rest, as one stack so every PR's diff is only its own change:\n\n`main ← #94 ← #95 ← #97 ← namespace ← ComponentProps<typeof X> ← type-text fixes ← shared props ← loader`\n\nThe trybuild replacement and #98 stay independent off main, and I'll also look at the failing Dependabot PR #84. Starting by moving #97 onto #95:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KYNMWAVsrTaCAUUJTLwQXM","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Replace trybuild compile_fail test with a doctest pair","description":"compile_fail + compiling ParsedProp::new doctests on ParsedProp; remove trybuild dev-dep and tests/compile_fail. Independent PR off main."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018b7g2N5D3NjKof7f2HJKn4","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"ComponentProps<typeof X> resolves to X's props","description":"Direct props position (known::component_props) looks up component values (local, imported, namespace members) like extends' component_props_of. Stacked on namespace re-exports."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0138EnNWVbBoyKfRFVT3vts5","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Investigate failing Dependabot PR #84","description":"Find why CI fails on dependabot routine-npm PR #84 and fix or report."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012TtjeNHin9vQJY9ZNdL5sP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"/usr/bin/git switch -q fix/resolver-groundwork && /usr/bin/git merge -q origin/feat/interned-props --no-edit 2>&1 | tail -5; /usr/bin/git status --short | head","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
