{"parentUuid":"7ea5732b-f1ca-4502-96f7-e3e302512c8f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJRjwW4gVQLuau7etY54","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DibwMaaPe72wzJ3W8mxYEx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr_body_doctest.md","content":"`tests/compile_fail.rs` checked with trybuild that a `ParsedProp` struct literal doesn't compile outside the crate, so props go through `ParsedProp::new` (which makes a prop with a default optional). trybuild compiles a separate crate against the whole dependency graph in `target/tests/trybuild`; whenever `Cargo.lock` changed (a branch switch), that one test took minutes locally.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `ParsedProp`'s doc comment carries the guard as a doctest pair: a `compile_fail` example with the struct literal, and a compiling example with `ParsedProp::new` that proves the imports and names are right, so the failing one can only fail on the literal. `cargo test --doc` (already in `just test-rust` and CI) builds them against the crate already built.\n- Removed `tests/compile_fail.rs`, `tests/compile_fail/` and the `trybuild` dev-dependency.\n\nTrade-off: trybuild compared the exact compiler error text; a stable `compile_fail` doctest only requires that compilation fails (`compile_fail,E0451` is nightly-only). The compiling twin covers the realistic failure, a typo in the example.\n\n## Verify\n\n`cargo test -p caliper-docgen-core --doc` (both `ParsedProp` doctests pass), `just test-rust`, `just lint doc-check machete typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1558,"cache_read_input_tokens":799146,"output_tokens":1255,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1558,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":799146,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1558},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DibwMaaPe72wzJ3W8mxYEx":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr_body_doctest.md","content":"`tests/compile_fail.rs` checked with trybuild that a `ParsedProp` struct literal doesn't compile outside the crate, so props go through `ParsedProp::new` (which makes a prop with a default optional). trybuild compiles a separate crate against the whole dependency graph in `target/tests/trybuild`; whenever `Cargo.lock` changed (a branch switch), that one test took minutes locally.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `ParsedProp`'s doc comment carries the guard as a doctest pair: a `compile_fail` example with the struct literal, and a compiling example with `ParsedProp::new` that proves the imports and names are right, so the failing one can only fail on the literal. `cargo test --doc` (already in `just test-rust` and CI) builds them against the crate already built.\n- Removed `tests/compile_fail.rs`, `tests/compile_fail/` and the `trybuild` dev-dependency.\n\nTrade-off: trybuild compared the exact compiler error text; a stable `compile_fail` doctest only requires that compilation fails (`compile_fail,E0451` is nightly-only). The compiling twin covers the realistic failure, a typo in the example.\n\n## Verify\n\n`cargo test -p caliper-docgen-core --doc` (both `ParsedProp` doctests pass), `just test-rust`, `just lint doc-check machete typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6120558a-7b3b-4776-b89e-f2886164aff9","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgJRjw5G3vd6E6xovCC2e","request