return types lost (printed as `=> void`), the made-up `(e: void)` parameter, and handler types wrapped as a parameter (`(e: MouseEventHandler<…>) => void` instead of `MouseEventHandler<…>`). Find each family's cause in the resolver/extractor (start from type_families.py's family definitions and the examples it prints) and fix at the source, not by string rewriting.\n2. `fix/generic-defaults` — keep type parameters' default types (`<P = {}>`) in the extractor and use them in `build_substitution` when a reference omits arguments, instead of leaving the placeholder (spectrum `StyleString` keeping `P`) and warning GenericArgumentMismatch.\n3. `fix/alias-display` — when an alias's expansion would be printed as raw conditional/mapped type text (Opaque conditional/mapped), keep the alias name with its arguments (`StyleProp<MaxWidth<string | number>>`, `LucideIcon`) instead of the raw text. Keep real structural expansions (unions of literals for enum controls, objects) as they are. This is mostly Mantine's 15,866 \"alias expanded where RDT names it\" family.\n\nFor each PR:\n- Measure before/after on the five corpora with /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/review/type_families.py (family counts vs RDT; it takes a binary path; RDT dumps are in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-results) and report the family deltas and the exact-match rate vs RDT in the PR description. Also check no prop count / component count regressions on the installed corpora (/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/stage2/groundwork.py pattern, bins in tmp/perf/bins).\n- Tests that assert exact type text (assert content, not presence — AGENTS.md), fixture snapshots regenerated and reviewed (each changed line justified in the PR), `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi`, `just lint doc-check machete typos`. The trybuild `compile_fail` test is slow after lockfile changes; you may exclude it locally with `-E 'not test(parsed_prop_bare_struct_literal)'` (it's being replaced in #100), CI runs everything.\n- If the cache schema changes (SourceData shape, e.g. generic defaults), bump CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION and its golden.\n- A changeset per PR (.changeset/*.md, same frontmatter style as existing ones; patch unless output shape changes for consumers).\n- Commits: imperative subject, one or two sentences of why, attribution line `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`. PR body ends with `https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`. Non-draft PRs. `gh` and `git commit`/`push` need the sandbox disabled; use `/usr/bin/git`, one plain git command per call.\n- Never force-push, never push to main, never merge.\n\nIf a fix turns out not to be worth it (no measurable improvement or it makes RDT agreement worse), drop it and say so instead of opening that PR. Report: each PR number/URL, branch, base, the measured family deltas, snapshot changes, and anything left undone.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/af0f4556df8c16e76.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c104d9d-0e35-4df0-8edf-1f9a5d465116","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"docs/oxfmt-073-toml","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d3b0e41e-6742-416d-b1b0-62