{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-23T03:38:18.031Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af0f4556df8c16e76</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01R8ViwUYNDd3qRBsibsKTHD</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/af0f4556df8c16e76.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Type-text fixes as stacked PRs\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I opened two stacked PRs and dropped the generic-defaults fix, because it didn't improve agreement with RDT. Together the two PRs raise exact matches against RDT from 7,939 to 14,011 of 26,463 props (30.0% → 52.9%).\n\nThe stack runs #101 → #103 → #104. Both PRs are non-draft, and each has its measurements and snapshot notes in its description.\n\n### PR 1: #103, function types\n- **Link:** https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/103\n- **Branch / base:** `fix/function-type-text` → `feat/component-props-of-typeof` (#101)\n- **Commit:** `e7d416d1`\n- **What it fixes:**\n  - Callbacks keep their return type: \"callback return type lost\" went from 261 to 2.\n  - The made-up `(e: void)` parameter is gone (191 → 0).\n  - Handler types are no longer wrapped as a parameter (60 → 0).\n- **Measured:** exact 7,939 → 8,008; exact plus formatting-only 8,307 → 8,712 (31.4% → 32.9%). No exact match regressed.\n- **Corpus counts:** unchanged on all five installed corpora.\n- **Snapshots:** 8 changed. Handler props now print as `React.FocusEventHandler&lt;HTMLInputElement&gt;` and similar, and the mui `sx` and react_aria render callbacks get their real return types. The cache golden moves to schema 15.\n- **Breaking:** `EventHandler` (`kind: \"eventHandler\"`) becomes `Function` (`kind: \"function\"`), and `MultiParamFunction` is removed.\n\n### PR 2: generic defaults, dropped\n- Built and measured: exact moved by only +3, and 5 props that matched exactly stopped matching.\n- The regressions are Mantine components cast to a generic signature, where RDT keeps the parameter name (`Value[]` became `string[]`), plus a substituted conditional left as text like `false extends true ? …`.\n- The work is commit `87646dcc` on the local branch `fix/generic-defaults`, not pushed. It includes the extractor change, substitution and tests, and would need cache schema 16.\n\n### PR 3: #104, alias display\n- **Link:** https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/104\n- **Branch / base:** `fix/alias-display` → `fix/function-type-text`\n- **Commit:** `6178a4bb`\n- **What it fixes:** an alias whose expansion contains an unevaluated conditional or mapped type now prints as its name with its arguments as written, e.g. `StyleProp&lt;MantineSpacing&gt;`. Nested cases work too: once `MantineBreakpoint` keeps its name, `StyleProp&lt;…&gt;` does as well. Literal unions and objects still expand, so enum controls are unchanged.\n- **Measured:** exact 8,008 → 14,011 (30.3% → 52.9%); exact plus formatting-only 32.9% → 55.6%. \"Alias expanded\" fell from 15,868 to 2,429.\n- **Why \"other\" rose to 8,278:** every prop that moved there was already a mismatch. Most now read `StyleProp&lt;React.CSSProperties[\"maxWidth\"]&gt;` where RDT prints `StyleProp&lt;MaxWidth&lt;string | number&gt;&gt;`. No exact match regressed.\n- **Corpus counts and time:** prop and component counts are unchanged, and timing is unchanged.\n- **Snapshots:** none changed, because no fixture has this kind of alias; a new end-to-end test asserts the exact text instead. The cache shape is unchanged.\n\n### Checks\n- Each PR: `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi -E 'not test(parsed_prop_bare_struct_literal)'` passes (731 tests on PR 1, 732 on PR 3).\n- `just lint doc-check machete typos` is clean on both.\n- The `watch_process` tests fail inside the sandbox because they need a terminal, so I ran the suite outside it.\n- Two `tsc-client` timing tests failed once in a full run but passed when run alone.\n- Each PR has one changeset: `.changeset/function-types.md` and `.changeset/alias-display.md`.\n\n### Left undone\n- The remaining gap after PR 3 is argument text: we print an alias's arguments as written in source, and RDT prints TypeScript's evaluation of them. Closing it needs the type checker.\n- An empty object prints as `{  }` where RDT has `{}`. It affects one Mantine prop shape (233 props), and fixing it alone wouldn't make them exact.\n- For generic components, RDT shows the parameter's constraint (`Multiple` → `boolean`) rather than its default. That could be a follow-up if you want it.\n\nresult: Opened #103 (function types) and #104 (alias names) on top of #101; together they raise exact agreement with RDT from 30.0% to 52.9%, and the generic-defaults fix was dropped for not improving it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>239521</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>253</tool_uses><duration_ms>1793626</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-af0f4556df8c16e76</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-af0f4556df8c16e76</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
