{"parentUuid":"cf5e3cd2-bb1a-4ed1-925b-f62339b5aa15","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJULfhzquQoXRe5WS2Xm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#103 passed CI and #104's is running. Starting step 3, sharing resolved props in memory, stacked on #104:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4160,"cache_read_input_tokens":836098,"output_tokens":2434,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":542},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4160,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2434,"cache_read_input_tokens":836098,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4160},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b81eab54-c4eb-44be-8584-55b7f7e07236","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgJULfJwFTsz4h5FKzJjW","requestRef":"f5f06dc3-d992-430c-8048-c2c886b8ced7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fb1e33c0-9be5-4392-bde7-a5c7d9de76ea","timestamp":"2026-10-23T03:38:36.560Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/alias-display","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"fb1e33c0-9be5-4392-bde7-a5c7d9de76ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJULfhzquQoXRe5WS2Xm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W9gexwrkrdMN7JhsH7Mbp4","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Share resolved props in memory","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"You are the step-3 worker: share resolved props in memory, as one PR stacked on #104 (base branch `fix/alias-display`; create branch `perf/shared-props` from `origin/fix/alias-display`). The user asked to \"do all of the rest, commit appropriately and stack PRs\".\n\nProblem (measured in the exp/dependency-types experiment): each component resolves and owns its own copy of every inherited prop. Mantine already emits 19,506 props of which ~3,200 are distinct; with dependency loading chakra reached 398,910 props, 2.4 s and 3.4 GB, and a per-interface memo didn't help because copying a memoized chain cost about as much as resolving it (chakra 2.2 → 1.8 s at 3.4 → 6.8 GB; see the memo code on `exp/dependency-types`, resolver/mod.rs InterfaceMemo, and its CALIPER_MEMO note).\n\nGoal: resolved props are shared, not copied, so components inheriting the same interface reuse one resolution and one allocation.\n- Make resolved props cheap to share (e.g. `Arc<ParsedProp>` in `ComponentEntry.props`/`notable_inherited` and in `ResolvedChain`, copy-on-write via `Arc::make_mut` where a plugin hook or per-component step mutates). Keep the public JSON byte-identical (the interned output from ADR 0009 already dedups on the wire; its PropId hashing may be able to reuse identity — measure, don't assume).\n- Then a per-run memo of resolved interface chains keyed by everything resolution depends on (interface identity, type args, in-scope type params, html-attributes mode, depth class; read why the exp memo key needed `visited_added`, `in_scope_added`, `deps`, diagnostics replay) storing shared results; replay diagnostics and watch dependencies (`resolver/deps.rs`) exactly, so diagnostics and watch-equals-cold stay correct. If the memo can't be made provably correct, ship only the sharing and say why.\n- Watch mode: the memo must not survive across revisions for project types unless keyed safely; a per-revision memo is fine.\n\nVerify:\n- Output byte-identical before/after on all fixtures (snapshots unchanged) and on the five installed corpora (`/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus`, source dirs in `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-deps/env.sh`; compare `extract --json` output hashes, durationMs normalized).\n- Time and peak RSS before/after on the five corpora (hyperfine -N, warmup 2, 10 runs, min time and peak RSS), and the watch harness if relevant.\n- Also measure the effect with dependency loading: create a LOCAL scratch branch (never pushed) merging your branch with `exp/dependency-types`, and report chakra/shadcn/spectrum time and RSS with `CALIPER_LOAD_DEPENDENCIES=1` before vs after (the experiment's baseline is chakra 2,419 ms / 3.4 GB). Delete nothing that isn't yours.\n- Tests asserting sharing semantics (e.g. two components inheriting one interface share the Arc; a plugin mutating one component's prop doesn't affect another's) and that diagnostics/`affects` and watch parity are unchanged.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi` (the trybuild test may be excluded locally with `-E 'not test(parsed_prop_bare_struct_literal)'`; run outside the sandbox if watch_process tests need a terminal), `just lint doc-check machete typos`, NAPI build + `just test-integration` if the binding is touched.\n- Changeset (minor for core if the public Rust type changes; patch otherwise for packages). Commit(s) with imperative subjects and one or two sentences of why, attribution `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; PR body with measurements, ending with `https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`. Non-draft PR, base `fix/alias-display`. `gh`, commit and push need the sandbox disabled; `/usr/bin/git`, one plain command per call. Never force-push, push to main, or merge.\n\nReport: PR URL/branch/base, design chosen and why, byte-identity evidence, before/after tables (without and with dependency loading), and anything left out.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4160,"cache_read_input_tokens":836098,"output_tokens":2434,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":542},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4160,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2434,"cache_read_input_tokens":836098,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4160},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01W9gexwrkrdMN7JhsH7Mbp4":{"description":"Share resolved props in memory","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"You are the step-3 worker: share resolved props in memory, as one PR stacked on #104 (base branch `fix/alias-display`; create branch `perf/shared-props` from `origin/fix/alias-display`). The user asked to \"do all of the rest, commit appropriately and stack PRs\".\n\nProblem (measured in the exp/dependency-types experiment): each component resolves and owns its own copy of every inherited prop. Mantine already emits 19,506 props of which ~3,200 are distinct; with dependency loading chakra reached 398,910 props, 2.4 s and 3.4 GB, and a per-interface memo didn't help because copying a memoized chain cost about as much as resolving it (chakra 2.2 → 1.8 s at 3.4 → 6.8 GB; see the memo code on `exp/dep