{"parentUuid":"56b48f89-424d-4e70-9412-03efed25eb88","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7bfab3ec-0a5e-493a-b3d8-c0fbc5d66600","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W9gexwrkrdMN7JhsH7Mbp4","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a5e5cfedce67ab662 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a5e5cfedce67ab662', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a5e5cfedce67ab662.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"475e0150-ccf3-4ef0-b5ad-7bbb8e932b4d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T03:38:54.468Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a5e5cfedce67ab662","description":"Share resolved props in memory","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","prompt":"You are the step-3 worker: share resolved props in memory, as one PR stacked on #104 (base branch `fix/alias-display`; create branch `perf/shared-props` from `origin/fix/alias-display`). The user asked to \"do all of the rest, commit appropriately and stack PRs\".\n\nProblem (measured in the exp/dependency-types experiment): each component resolves and owns its own copy of every inherited prop. Mantine already emits 19,506 props of which ~3,200 are distinct; with dependency loading chakra reached 398,910 props, 2.4 s and 3.4 GB, and a per-interface memo didn't help because copying a memoized chain cost about as much as resolving it (chakra 2.2 → 1.8 s at 3.4 → 6.8 GB; see the memo code on `exp/dependency-types`, resolver/mod.rs InterfaceMemo, and its CALIPER_MEMO note).\n\nGoal: resolved props are shared, not copied, so components inheriting the same interface reuse one resolution and one allocation.\n- Make resolved props cheap to share (e.g. `Arc<ParsedProp>` in `ComponentEntry.props`/`notable_inherited` and in `ResolvedChain`, copy-on-write via `Arc::make_mut` where a plugin hook or per-component step mutates). Keep the public JSON byte-identical (the interned output from ADR 0009 already dedups on the wire; its PropId hashing may be able to reuse identity — measure, don't assume).\n- Then a per-run memo of resolved interface chains keyed by everything resolution depends on (interface identity, type args, in-scope type params, html-attributes mode, depth class; read why the exp memo key needed `visited_added`, `in_scope_added`, `deps`, diagnostics replay) storing shared results; replay diagnostics and watch dependencies (`resolver/deps.rs`) exactly, so diagnostics and watch-equals-cold stay correct. If the memo can't be made provably correct, ship only the sharing and say why.\n- Watch mode: the memo must not survive across revisions for project types unless keyed safely; a per-revision memo is fine.\n\nVerify:\n- Output byte-identical before/after on all fixtures (snapshots unchanged) and on the five installed corpora (`/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus`, source dirs in `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-deps/env.sh`; compare `extract --json` output hashes, durationMs normalized).\n- Time and peak RSS before/after on the five corpora (hyperfine -N, warmup 2, 10 runs, min time and peak RSS), and the watch harness if relevant.\n- Also measure the effect with dependency loading: create a LOCAL scratch branch (never pushed) merging your branch with `exp/dependency-types`, and report chakra/shadcn/spectrum time and RSS with `CALIPER_LOAD_DEPENDENCIES=1` before vs after (the experiment's baseline is chakra 2,419 ms / 3.4 GB). Delete nothing that isn't yours.\n- Tests asserting sharing semantics (e.g. two components inheriting one interface share the Arc; a plugin mutating one component's prop doesn't affect another's) and that diagnostics/`affects` and watch parity are unchanged.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi` (the trybuild test may be excluded locally with `-E 'not test(parsed_prop_bare_struct_literal)'`; run outside the sandbox if watch_process tests need a terminal), `just lint doc-check machete typos`, NAPI build + `just test-integration` if the binding is touched.\n- Changeset (minor for core if the public Rust type changes; patch otherwise for packages). Commit(s) with imperative subjects and one or two sentences of why, attribution `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; PR body with measurements, ending with `https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`. Non-draft PR, base `fix/alias-display`. `gh`, commit and push need the sandbox disabled; `/usr/bin/git`, one plain command per call. Never force-push, push to main, or merge.\n\nReport: PR URL/branch/base, design chosen and why, byte-identity evidence, before/after tables (without and with dependency loading), and anything left out.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a5e5cfedce67ab662.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b81eab54-c4eb-44be-8584-55b7f7e07236","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"docs/oxfmt-073-toml","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"56b48f89-424d-4e70-9412-03efed25eb88","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/alias-display","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"475e0150-ccf3-4ef0-b5ad-7bbb8e932b4d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Agent","toolUseID":"toolu_01W9gexwrkrdMN7JhsH7Mbp4","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Agent\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":48},"type":"attachment","uuid":"66665be5-69d4-40c2-a33f-9f1465a54c4e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T03:38:54.451Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"fix/alias-display","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"66665be5-69d4-40c2-a33f-9f1465a54c4e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"sandbox_instructions","content":"## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a limit below is not enforced. Commands can reach more than that — credentials and keys elsewhere on this machine, the user's other projects and configuration, sockets that control this machine or other workloads, cloud metadata endpoints — but being reachable does not make them provided; those are the user's, not the task's, unless the user's request calls for them. If the task cannot be finished with what you were given, do what you can and tell the user plainly what is missing instead of finding another way to it; that report is a complete answer.\n\nHow the sandbox is configured in this session:\nFilesystem: {\"read\":{\"denyOnly\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/ide\",\"./.entire/metadata\"],\"allowWithinDeny\":[]},\"write\":{\"allowOnly\":[\"/dev/stdout\",\"/dev/stderr\",\"/dev/null\",\"/dev/tty\",\"/dev/dtracehelper\",\"/dev/autofs_nowait\",\"/tmp/claude\",\"/private/tmp/claude\",\"/Users/gabe/.npm/_logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/debug\",\".\",\"$TMPDIR\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.git\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a5e5cfedce67ab662\"],\"denyWithinAllow\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.d\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/local\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/daemon\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/shell-snapshots\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/session-env\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/workflows\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/commands\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/agents\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/routines\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/rules\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/output-styles\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/launch.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/CLAUDE.md\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/daemon.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.signature-iat.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/policy-limits.json.stamp.json\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/backups\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/loop.md\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/cowork_plugins\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/dev-mods\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/mcp-skill-archives\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/mcp-discovery-cache\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/shares\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/todos\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/statsig\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/access-audit\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/remote-settings-helper-consent\",\"... and 95 more (truncated for prompt size)\"]}}\n\n - You should always default to running commands within the sandbox. Do NOT attempt to set `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` unless:\n  - The user *explicitly* asks you to bypass sandbox\n  - A specific command just failed and you see evidence of sandbox restrictions causing the failure. Note that commands can fail for many reasons unrelated to the sandbox (missing files, wrong arguments, network issues, etc.).\n - Evidence of sandbox-caused failures includes:\n  - \"Operation not permitted\" errors for file/network operations\n  - Access denied to specific paths outside allowed directories\n  - Network connection failures to non-whitelisted hosts\n  - Unix socket connection errors\n - When you see evidence of sandbox-caused failure:\n  - Retry with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` directly rather than asking in prose first — the retry itself goes through the permission gate (a user prompt, or the auto-mode classifier when auto mode is active)\n  - Briefly explain what sandbox restriction likely caused the failure. Be sure to mention that the user can use the `/sandbox` command to manage restrictions.\n - A sandbox denial on a credential, a file or a host that the task does not involve is the boundary above at work: tell the user rather than retrying with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`.\n - Treat each command you execute with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true` individually. Even if you have recently run a command with this setting, you should default to running future commands within the sandbox.\n - Do not suggest adding sensitive paths like ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc, ~/.ssh/*, or credential files to the sandbox allowlist.\n - Network egress goes through a filtering proxy. Attempt requests and read the error rather than predicting whether a host is reachable; denied connections are reported in a `<sandbox_violations>` block explaining the reason.\n - If a command fails to bind or listen on a local port with \"Operation not permitted\" (EPERM), local port binding is off in this sandbox. Treat it as the sandbox-caused failure described above, and tell the user that `sandbox.network.allowLocalBinding: true` in their settings (it applies without a restart) allows it without leaving the sandbox.\n - Opening an app, file or URL with `open`, or scripting another app with `osascript`, is blocked inside this sandbox (macOS Launch Services and Apple Events are off) and fails with errors such as -10822 (kLSServerCommunicationErr), -54, -600 or \"LSOpenURLsWithRole() failed\". That failure is the sandbox, not a problem with what you built; do not retry it with `dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true`. Tell the user the sandbox blocked it and give them the exact command to run themselves.\n - For temporary files, always use the `$TMPDIR` environment variable. TMPDIR is automatically set to the correct sandbox-writable directory in sandbox mode. Do NOT use `/tmp` directly - use `$TMPDIR` instead.\n - If a clipboard utility such as `pbcopy`, `xclip`, or `wl-copy` fails inside the sandbox and the user wants the text on their clipboard, put the text in a fenced code block in your response and tell them to run `/copy` (it copies from outside the sandbox; when the picker appears they can select just that block), rather than writing a file for them to copy manually."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"64d14221-23ac-49d3-b614-93ca0b516813","timestamp":"2026-10-23T03:38:54.509Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a l