{"parentUuid":"6d734ebc-b9dd-4699-b368-611657abafdf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7baa1fc8-94fc-4849-80e5-6573cde7eb2f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A5chU6nCxoPbuPxPSmUqX4","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a75c51be5bf7193ae (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a75c51be5bf7193ae', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a75c51be5bf7193ae.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"5c1b3fb9-b76d-4831-85bd-542241b17bcc","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:19:55.176Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a75c51be5bf7193ae","description":"Dependency loader behind a flag","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","prompt":"You are the step-5 worker: land name-driven dependency type loading, behind a flag (off by default), as PRs stacked on #105 (base branch `perf/shared-props`). The user asked to \"do all of the rest, commit appropriately and stack PRs\", and approved: collapse of large inherited sources applies to dependency sources only by default (react-component-meta parity), with an option.\n\nSource material: the experiment branch `exp/dependency-types` (worktree /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a1bf012dd9d3d2112; `crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs` + tests, layer fallbacks in named_type_index.rs/import_map.rs, resolver wiring in resolver/mod.rs, import.rs, precedence.rs, chain.rs, extends.rs, pipeline/revision.rs, CLI flags), the stage-1 prototype (/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/loader-proto, its recommendations on index format/keying/work queue), and the stack's already-landed pieces: #97 resolver groundwork (ModuleResolvers, tsconfig discovery, customConditions, resolve_dts retries — the experiment's own versions must NOT be re-added), #99 namespace re-exports, #101 ComponentProps<typeof X>, #103/#104 type text, #105 shared props + interface memo (the experiment's CALIPER_MEMO memo must not be ported). Port, don't copy blindly: re-derive against the current stack.\n\nSplit into stacked PRs (each base = previous branch), for reviewability:\n1. ADRs only (`docs/adr/0010-…`, `0011-…`, index lines in docs/adr/README.md, following its rules and banned words): (a) load dependency declarations by name before resolution into a shared dependency layer, precedence project > known shortcut > dependency declaration > builtin, dependency components only in a non-emitted value index, dependency enums never public; (b) the per-package export index persisted next to the cache dir, keyed by package realpath + resolver config hash, validated by package.json mtime+size, and why the msgpack DtsCache is not used for dependencies (measured slower than re-parsing); (c) display: `collapseInheritedProps: \"dependencies\" | \"all\" | \"none\"` (default \"dependencies\") with threshold 30, react-component-meta parity, collapsed sources kept as an InheritedLayer with total_props and curated notable props. Put the measurements (stage 1/2 numbers already in the conversation) in Context. Branch `docs/adr-dependency-types`.\n2. The loader + dependency layer + precedence + value index + leak guards + watch demand diff (`Revision::next` loads new names into a new layer version; watch-equals-cold cases: new package import, removed import, local shadowing), diagnostics for every unresolved demand reason attached to the referencing component, `PipelineOptions.load_dependencies` (default false), CLI `--load-dependencies`, config `loadDependencies`, NAPI option, Vite plugin option. Branch `feat/load-dependency-types`.\n3. The collapse option (`collapseInheritedProps` across PipelineOptions/CLI/config/NAPI/Vite) applied before resolving. Branch `feat/collapse-inherited-props`.\nIf (2) is too large to review, split it further (e.g. layer+index first, then watch), still stacked.\n\nRequirements for each PR:\n- Flag off: output byte-identical to the base on fixtures and the five installed corpora (/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus; source dirs/tsconfigs in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-deps/env.sh), `durationMs` normalized.\n- Flag on: measure per corpus — unresolved type diagnostics, components with no props, props, output size, time and peak RSS (hyperfine -N warmup 2, 10 runs) cold and warm index, vs flag off and vs RDT with dependencies (bench-deps results); determinism at RAYON_NUM_THREADS 1/4/18; leak checks (no node_modules component or enum in output); watch timings for an edit adding a package import and one not. Put the tables in the PR.\n- Tests: loader unit tests (index flattening incl. star cycles, determinism), precedence (cva VariantProps keeps its shortcut with cva loaded), leak guards, value index (shadcn-style `ComponentProps<typeof DialogPrimitive.Content>` through a package), watch parity cases, collapse option on fixtures. Assert exact content (AGENTS.md).\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi` (trybuild test may be excluded locally with `-E 'not test(parsed_prop_bare_struct_literal)'`; run outside the sandbox when watch tests need a terminal), `just lint doc-check machete typos`, NAPI build + `just test-integration` when the binding/plugin changes, docs (`docs/architecture/*`, STATUS.md's overstated \"cross-package .d.ts resolution\" claim) updated, changesets.\n- Commits: imperative subject, one or two sentences of why, `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`. PR bodies end with `https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`. Non-draft. `gh`/commit/push need the sandbox disabled; `/usr/bin/git`, one plain command per call. Never force-push, push to main, or merge.\n\nReport: each PR URL/branch/base, deviations and why, measurement tables, correctness findings (including wrong results vs RDT on a sample), and what remains before turning the flag on by default.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a75c51be5bf7193ae.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"fee9baee-ca50-4c3f-a22f-a79cd873f2d8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"docs/oxfmt-073-toml","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6d734ebc-b9dd-4699-b368-611657abafdf","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af