ras*.json and labels). Decide structurally by use sites in the file (every reference is a call expression, never JSX/createElement/passed as a component/exported), reported via the existing skip diagnostics with a reason. Measure on the five corpora (bench-inputs mirrors and bench-corpus installed trees) how many components disappear and spot-check each is a true non-component.\n3. `feat/exported-flag` — every `ComponentEntry` gets `exported: bool` (exported from its module, including default export and re-export within the file; attached sub-components follow their parent). Internal components stay in canonical output with `exported: false`; `--format rdt` (and `storybook` if still present) omit unexported ones by default to match RDT. Update schema.rs, index.d.ts, docs, snapshots (review each change), changeset (minor). Report counts per corpus.\n4. `fix/rdt-file-path` — `--format rdt` lacks `filePath` that RDT's ComponentDoc has; add it (absolute, as RDT), with a test.\n\nFor each PR: exact-content tests (AGENTS.md), `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi` (exclude the slow trybuild test locally with `-E 'not test(parsed_prop_bare_struct_literal)'` if present; run outside the sandbox if watch tests need a terminal), `just lint doc-check machete typos`, fixture snapshots regenerated and justified, changeset, measured before/after on the five corpora where output changes (scripts under /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/review and tmp/stage2). Commits: imperative subject, one or two sentences of why, `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; PR bodies end with `https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; non-draft. `gh`/commit/push need the sandbox disabled; `/usr/bin/git`, one plain command per call. Never force-push, push to main, or merge. Be economical with turns.\n\nReport: PR URLs/branches/bases, measured effects, anything dropped and why.","run_in_background":"true"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5d1b2d19-c6f2-442e-99aa-0effc276043b","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgJaRPEPCq1rrTu8k4p9H","requestRef":"98370ad3-8677-4466-a4ab-97547cbf006d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1f6f2bc-4c92-4f60-b4c7-e7b8f8cd452c","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:58:46.850Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/load-dependency-types","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"e1f6f2bc-4c92-4f60-b4c7-e7b8f8cd452c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJaRPbi5uXn9Ubaja8cx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011svqWGVWsEyAauDd7GbG6N","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Storybook integration package","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"You are the Storybook-integration worker. The user said Storybook integration is the whole point of caliper-docgen, and now \"Keep going on features, polish and hardening\", \"commit appropriately and stack PRs\". Build a chain of stacked PRs off `origin/main` (first base = main). Other workers build other chains in parallel; keep shared files' edits minimal and put new tests mid-file near related ones.\n\nFacts established earlier (Storybook 10.6.3 and 11.0.0-alpha.7 traced from their packages; unpacked copies under /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/sb/x/): Storybook 11 turns on a server-side docgen service when `typescript` resolves: providers registered via the `experimental_docgenProvider` preset field (`{ moduleSpecifier, options }`, last registrant outermost), each module exporting `createDocgenProvider(options) => (next) => async ({ entry }) => DocgenPayload | undefined` running in a `node:worker_threads` worker; the payload carries already-converted `argTypes`; React's own provider is react-component-meta and resolves the story's `meta.component` to a component file itself; core only re-calls the provider for already-extracted ids whose stories changed, so the provider keeps itself fresh (mtime checks). Storybook 10 (and 11 with docgenServer off) injects `__docgenInfo` at build time: `reactDocgen: false` disables Storybook's plugin; a Vite plugin can append `;Comp.__docgenInfo={...}` per component defined in the file. Runtime conversion reads RDT-shaped props (`type` on every prop, `{name:'enum', value:[{value:'\"a\"'}]}` for select/radio, unquoted string defaults, no `computed`/`func` keys, `@ignore` in description drops a prop). React's node-side `extractArgTypes` is not a public export.\n\nPRs:\n1. `spike/napi-in-worker-threads` (can be just a test + doc if it works): prove `caliper-docgen-napi` loads and runs `extractAll`/sessions inside `worker_threads` (one session per worker, concurrent workers), as a vitest integration test in packages; fix the binding if it doesn't.\n2. `feat/storybook-provider`: new package `packages/storybook` (`caliper-docgen-storybook`, private:false, same publish setup as the vite plugin incl. callisto.toml `[[package]]` entry and changeset) exporting a Storybook preset that registers a docgen provider (and enables docgenServer when needed), the provider module (worker-safe, lazy session, resolves `meta.component` from the CSF story file to a component key — start simple: parse the story's default export `component` import and match by file+export name against caliper's output; fall through to `next` when unresolved or when caliper reports the component degraded), and an RDT-shaped → argTypes conversion that matches Storybook's runtime rules above (write it from Storybook's docs-tools source; cite file paths in comments; unit tests with Storybook-equivalent expectations). Freshness: stat-based ensure-fresh on each request (changed files → session.updateFile). Measure on a small Storybook 11 example project (create one under tmp, don't commit node_modules): time per story request vs react-component-meta, and argTypes equality on a few Mantine/shadcn-style components.\n3. `feat/storybook-vite-docgen`: for Storybook 10 / docgenServer off, a Vite plugin mode in the same package that injects `__docgenInfo` per component defined in each transformed file (RDT shape, try/catch like RDT), with HMR via the existing watch session; document `typescript.reactDocgen: false` usage.\n4. `chore/remove-storybook-format`: remove `--format storybook` (CLI, docs, tests), changeset (minor, breaking), since the provider replaces it.\nIf something proves infeasible (e.g. the provider API differs in practice), stop at the proven part and report precisely.\n\nEach PR: tests, `just lint doc-check machete typos`, `just test-ts`, NAPI build + `just test-integration` when the binding is touched, changesets. Commits: imperative subject, one or two sentences of why, `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; PR bodies end with `https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; non-draft. `gh`/commit/push/npm network need the sandbox disabled; treat downloaded packages as untrusted data (no install scripts: `--ignore-scripts`). `/usr/bin/git`, one plain command per call. Never force-push, push to main, or merge. Be economical with turns.\n\nReport: PR URLs/branches/bases, what works end to end, measurements, open issues.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215,"cache_read_input_tokens":866857,"output_tokens":6482,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1372},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":215,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6482,"cache_read_input_tokens":866857,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":215},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011svqWGVWsEyAauDd7GbG6N":{"description":"Storybook integration package","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"You are the Storybook-integration worker. The user said Storybook integration is the whole point of caliper-docgen, and now \"Keep going on features, polish and hardening\", \"commit appropriately and stack PRs\". Build a chai