\n1. `feat/watch-rebuild-on-config` — watch mode (CLI watcher and the Vite plugin) rebuilds the session when a lockfile (`pnpm-lock.yaml`, `package-lock.json`, `yarn.lock`, `bun.lock*`), a `package.json` or a tsconfig in the resolution chain changes (today documented as \"restart or call rebuild()\"; docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md:113, cli watch.rs). Vite: `addWatchFile` + handle in hotUpdate/watchChange; CLI: add to the watched set. Tests for both; docs updated.\n2. `feat/session-ensure-fresh` — a `WatchSession` (core) + NAPI API that, given nothing, stats the files the session read (project files, tsconfigs, lockfile, package.json files) and applies changes since the last revision (or rebuilds when config changed), returning the update; this is what a Storybook docgen provider running in a worker needs. Sibling-path parity tests vs update_file/cold extract (AGENTS.md testing discipline).\n3. `ci/size-normalized-gates` — a reproducible scorecard: a script (in `scripts/`, Python stdlib or Node, no new heavy deps) that extracts the five public corpora at pinned commits (fetch shallow, cache in CI), runs caliper (and optionally RDT) and records time, peak RSS, components, props, unresolved counts; a CI job (separate workflow, scheduled + manual, not on every PR unless cheap) that fails when caliper is slower than 1.1× main's recorded time on any corpus or when speed vs RDT drops below 10×; document the gates in docs (docs/precision.md or a new docs/performance.md) per the earlier analysis (t ≈ 6.4 ms + 0.13 ms/kLOC + 3.8 ms/kprop model, RDT ratio gate, 10% regression gate, scaling test). Keep CI cost reasonable; if RDT in CI is too slow, record RDT numbers as a committed baseline and say so.\n4. `docs/status-and-ts7` — fix stale docs: docs/STATUS.md (cross-package .d.ts claim, current recall/precision/perf figures), docs/type-checker-integration.md (TS 7.1 beta dates, `tsc --api` msgpack protocol caveats, method count/entry points as researched), ADR 0006 typo `typescript/unstable` if wrong, ADR 0007 amendment noted in task list (read it and decide what's stale), README benchmark numbers (current: ~31× faster than RDT on source-only mirrors; with deps installed the comparison isn't like-for-like until dependency loading lands — say so plainly).\n\nEach PR: tests where code changes (exact-content asserts), `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi` (exclude slow trybuild locally with `-E 'not test(parsed_prop_bare_struct_literal)'` if present; run outside the sandbox when watch tests need a terminal), `just test-ts`, NAPI build + `just test-integration` when binding/plugin change, `just lint doc-check machete typos`, changesets for package changes. Writing rules in AGENTS.md / docs/adr/README.md (banned words, no hard-wrapping). Commits: imperative subject, one or two sentences of why, `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; PR bodies end with `https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; non-draft. `gh`/commit/push need the sandbox disabled; `/usr/bin/git`, one plain command per call. Never force-push, push to main, or merge. Be economical with turns.\n\nReport: PR URLs/branches/bases, what each changes, test evidence, open issues.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ad2ad47f8a70be1d0.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5d1b2d19-c6f2-442e-99aa-0effc276043b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"docs/oxfmt-073-toml","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"