{"parentUuid":"e1f6f2bc-4c92-4f60-b4c7-e7b8f8cd452c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d1299072-5d8d-4b6c-8667-1c51025790cb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013TW2YzkLjiELsj9ZRaZgTX","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: ac4ffd0d81fe4e197 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'ac4ffd0d81fe4e197', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ac4ffd0d81fe4e197.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"cf71f46c-394a-468d-8f05-af7dc5601ccb","timestamp":"2026-10-23T04:59:20.867Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"ac4ffd0d81fe4e197","description":"Precision and detection fixes","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","prompt":"You are the precision/detection worker. The user said \"Keep going on features, polish and hardening\" and earlier \"commit appropriately and stack PRs\". Build a chain of small stacked PRs off `origin/main` (first base = main, each next base = previous branch). Other workers are building other chains in parallel; put new tests in the middle of shared test files (near related tests), never appended at the end, to avoid merge conflicts.\n\nPRs, in order (drop one only if measurement shows it doesn't help, and say why):\n1. `fix/factory-payload-props` — Mantine `OverflowList` gets its factory payload keys (`props`, `ref`, `signature`, `stylesNames`, `vars`) as props: `extractor/wrapper.rs` `payload_props` rejects a `props:` member with type arguments (`OverflowListProps<any>`), then `select_wrapper_props` falls back to the Factory alias itself because it's declared in the same file. Accept `props: X<…>` (carry the args), never use a payload alias as the props type, and emit a diagnostic when no props are found (never silent).\n2. `fix/called-helpers-are-not-components` — PascalCase functions that are only *called* (e.g. `IndexedAccess(type)`, `ObjectType(type)`, a `(props, ref)` render callback passed to something) were reported as components (the 3 false positives in the extras sample: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/review/precision/extras*.json and labels). Decide structurally by use sites in the file (every reference is a call expression, never JSX/createElement/passed as a component/exported), reported via the existing skip diagnostics with a reason. Measure on the five corpora (bench-inputs mirrors and bench-corpus installed trees) how many components disappear and spot-check each is a true non-component.\n3. `feat/exported-flag` — every `ComponentEntry` gets `exported: bool` (exported from its module, including default export and re-export within the file; attached sub-components follow their parent). Internal components stay in canonical output with `exported: false`; `--format rdt` (and `storybook` if still present) omit unexported ones by default to match RDT. Update schema.rs, index.d.ts, docs, snapshots (review each change), changeset (minor). Report counts per corpus.\n4. `fix/rdt-file-path` — `--format rdt` lacks `filePath` that RDT's ComponentDoc has; add it (absolute, as RDT), with a test.\n\nFor each PR: exact-content tests (AGENTS.md), `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi` (exclude the slow trybuild test locally with `-E 'not test(parsed_prop_bare_struct_literal)'` if present; run outside the sandbox if watch tests need a terminal), `just lint doc-check machete typos`, fixture snapshots regenerated and justified, changeset, measured before/after on the five corpora where output changes (scripts under /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/review and tmp/stage2). Commits: imperative subject, one or two sentences of why, `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; PR bodies end with `https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; non-draft. `gh`/commit/push need the sandbox disabled; `/usr/bin/git`, one plain command per call. Never force-push, push to main, or merge. Be economical with turns.\n\nReport: PR URLs/branches/bases, measured effects, anything dropped and why.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ac4ffd0d81fe4e197.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5d1b2d19-c6f2-442e-99aa-0effc276043b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"docs/oxfmt-073-toml","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e1f6f2bc-4c92-