e model, it fails if extracting two copies of Mantine takes more than 2.2× as long as one. The model (t ≈ 6.4 ms + 0.13 ms/kLOC + 3.8 ms/kprop) is reported but not gated: it was within 2× on every corpus but ranged from 0.45× to 1.6×, so a gate on it would flake.\n- **No committed baseline:** react-docgen-typescript takes 1 to 2 s per corpus, so CI times it live.\n- **Local results:** 34–81 ms per corpus, 17–39× faster than react-docgen-typescript, scaling 1.77×, all gates pass. Documented in `docs/performance.md`.\n\n**#118 – stale docs.**\n- **`STATUS.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md`:** the cross-package claim was wrong. Main only reads `@types/react`, TypeScript's lib files and files inside source directories. Test counts, recall, precision and speed figures are updated.\n- **`docs/type-checker-integration.md`:** checked against the 7.1 beta package. The beta was planned for 2026-10-06 but published to npm on 2026-10-20. The doc now has all the launch flags and entry points, the msgpack caveats, and 177 API methods (up from 157).\n- **ADR 0006:** left unchanged. Its `typescript/unstable` wording was right for the nightly it cites, and the ADR rules forbid editing history.\n- **ADR 0007:** left unchanged. Its decisions are not yet implemented rather than outdated. The one stale line (\"`update_file` must notify\") is now covered in the integration doc, which names both update paths.\n- **README speed claim:** I wrote 17–39× (median 22×), not \"about 31×\". That's what the reproducible scorecard measures; the earlier 29–42× in #107 timed react-docgen-typescript with dependencies installed. The README also says the comparison with dependencies installed isn't like for like until dependency loading lands.\n\n**Open issues:**\n- The scorecard workflow hasn't run in Actions. A manual run only becomes possible once the file is on `main`.\n- The shadcn and spectrum source directories differ from the old unrecorded mirrors. Even the whole spectrum repo gives 7.4k props, against 32.8k in #107, so the old figure can't be reproduced.\n- The terminal-signal test flake above.\n- Merge in order #111 → #114 → #116 → #118, and retarget each child to `main` when its parent merges.\n\n**Paths changed:**\n- #111: `crates/core/src/pipeline/{watch.rs,revision.rs,watch/tests.rs}`, `crates/cli/src/commands/watch.rs`, `crates/binding/src/lib.rs`, `packages/vite-plugin/{src/index.ts,tests/unit/plugin.test.ts,README.md}`, `packages/napi/{binding.d.ts,index.js}`, `docs/architecture/{pipeline-orchestration,cli-commands}.md`, `.changeset/watch-rebuild-on-config.md`\n- #114: `crates/core/src/pipeline/{discover.rs,revision.rs,watch.rs,watch/tests.rs}`, `crates/binding/src/lib.rs`, `packages/napi/{binding.d.ts,index.js}`, `docs/architecture/{napi-binding,pipeline-orchestration}.md`, `.changeset/session-ensure-fresh.md`\n- #116: `scripts/scorecard.py`, `scripts/scorecard-rdt.mjs`, `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml`, `docs/performance.md`, `docs/benchmarks.md`, `.gitignore`\n- #118: `docs/STATUS.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `README.md`, `docs/type-checker-integration.md`\n\nresult: Stacked PRs #111 → #114 → #116 → #118 are open; tests and lint pass, the scorecard workflow hasn't run in Actions, and one terminal test flaked once</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>309034</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>261</tool_uses><duration_ms>2178743</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-ad2ad47f8a70be1d0</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-ad2ad47f8a70be1d0</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"3445ebce-ab2c-4dca-8ccc-7fb7e10667d9","timestamp":"2026-10-23T05:35:41.659Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mvki3198-1a748947"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":99,"turnIndex":141},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Pro