{"parentUuid":"a4d9dab9-1e01-4c81-bebd-f3b61b2c4730","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:TaskUpdate","toolUseID":"toolu_013yLG4fgDesUoTfxaxwKHfS","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"TaskUpdate\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":42},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c0c18d3f-3d65-412f-966f-128e26a52ad9","timestamp":"2026-10-23T05:50:12.158Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/remove-storybook-format","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"c0c18d3f-3d65-412f-966f-128e26a52ad9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJeNYRvQMAeRguBwyT86","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FFWDEp62YtC8N1uwkHZ99x","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Bug batch from Storybook and loader findings","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","prompt":"You are the bug-batch worker. The user said \"Keep going on features, polish and hardening\" and \"commit appropriately and stack PRs\". Fix correctness bugs found by the Storybook and loader tracks, as small stacked PRs on top of the main stack tip: first base = `feat/collapse-inherited-props` (#109), each next base = previous branch. Put new tests mid-file near related ones.\n\nBugs (one PR each; reproduce with a failing exact-content test first; drop one only if it's already fixed on the base, and say so):\n1. `fix/jsdoc-one-line-function` — a JSDoc comment above a one-line `function X(props: { a: string; b: number }) { … }` is attached to the first prop instead of the component (and the prop gets the component's description).\n2. `fix/render-prop-return-type` — a function prop with one parameter returning ReactNode (render prop, e.g. `renderItem: (item: T) => React.ReactNode`) is printed as `=> void`; check against #103's function-type fixes on the base and fix the remaining path.\n3. `fix/dom-handler-overwrite` — with dependency loading on (`--load-dependencies`), recharts' own event-handler props overwrite the DOM handler of the same name: shadcn `ChartLegendContent.onTimeUpdate` comes out `(data: any, index: number, event: …) => void | string` where RDT has `ReactEventHandler<SVGSVGElement>`. Work out TypeScript's actual rule for that component's props (intersection/extends order, Omit, which declaration wins) and make the merge follow it; verify against RDT's type on shadcn (/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus/shadcn-ui/apps/v4; RDT runner in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-deps).\n4. `fix/zod-infer-unwrap` — with dependency loading on, `z.infer<typeof schema>` becomes `typeof schema[\"_output\"]`; make it stop one level earlier (keep `z.infer<typeof schema>` as a name, like the alias-display rule in #104) unless it can be evaluated structurally.\n\nEach PR: flag-off output byte-identical on the five installed corpora except where the fix intends a change (state which), measured effect, snapshots reviewed, changeset, `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi` (run outside the sandbox when watch/terminal tests need it), `just lint doc-check machete typos`. Commits: imperative subject, one or two sentences of why, `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; PR bodies end with `https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`; non-draft. `gh`/commit/push need the sandbox disabled; `/usr/bin/git`, one plain command per call. Never force-push, push to main, or merge. Be economical with turns: batch edits, don't re-read files you've read.\n\nReport: PR URLs/branches/bases, root cause and fix per bug, measured effects, anything dropped.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2447,"cache_read_input_tokens":905000,"output_tokens":1946,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":627},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2447,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1946,"cache_read_input_tokens":905000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2447},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FFWDEp62YtC8N1uwk