{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":981,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"c8723f45-6a51-435c-bd53-6868b04aaf89","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJeQ1aawkUxfcfZxyDiS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Track B (Storybook) is done: four stacked PRs off main, all passing CI: `#108 ← #117 ← #119 ← #120`.\n\n- **#108:** the native binding works inside `worker_threads`, including several workers at once.\n- **#117, `caliper-docgen-storybook`:** a Storybook 11 docgen provider package. It finds the story's `meta.component`, converts props with `@storybook/react`'s own argTypes converter, checks for changed files on every request, and hands anything it can't document to React's docgen (react-component-meta).\n- **#119:** an `injectDocgenInfo` mode in the Vite plugin for Storybook 10 (or 11 with the docgen server off), with hot reload when a shared types file changes.\n- **#120:** removes `--format storybook`.\n\n**Verified with real Storybook builds** in both modes, against react-component-meta:\n\n| | caliper | react-component-meta |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| First request | 33–43 ms | 504 ms |\n| Later requests | 0.4–0.6 ms | 0.7–1.5 ms |\n| After an edit | 3.9 ms, edit included | edit not seen |\n\n19 of 26 argTypes are identical. Five of the seven differences are string-default quote style: we print `\"md\"`, React prints the source text `'md'`.\n\n**Decision for you:** should string defaults keep their source text (`'md'`)? That matches Storybook's React docgen but changes our canonical output. Default is to leave them as they are.\n\n**Now running:** a bug batch stacked on #109:\n1. A JSDoc comment on a one-line function is attached to the first prop instead of the component.\n2. Render props print as `=> void`.\n3. recharts' event handlers overwrite the DOM ones.\n4. `z.infer<typeof schema>` is unwrapped one level too far.\n\n**Open PRs, for merging:**\n- Main stack: `#97 ← #99 ← #101 ← #103 ← #104 ← #105 ← #106 ← #107 ← #109`\n- Track A: `#110 ← #112 ← #113 ← #115`\n- Track C: `#111 ← #114 ← #116 ← #118`\n- Track B: `#108 ← #117 ← #119 ← #120`\n- Independent: #98, #100, #102 (then `@dependabot rebase` on #84)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5366,"cache_read_input_tokens":907447,"output_tokens":784,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5366,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":784,"cache_read_input_tokens":907447,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5366},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"694b4dbd-d142-4df9-98c3-ca69514ec511","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgJeQ164v8QXqgCTw7nEC","requestRef":"6017ffed-815c-43ae-ad89-28109b0b4696","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e8cbab74-40f0-429f-bb2e-9c1116e0dc16","timestamp":"2026-10-23T05:50:30.519Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/remove-storybook-format","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
