{"parentUuid":"aef58104-3449-4e8e-a2a9-4ff8e1cc0dbd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb563e85-80fa-4200-bf18-7a747f7a254b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R1KTLvhzxSStteexCXjo8c","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --cc docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md\nindex d8a4ccec,9314e3a4..00000000\n--- a/docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md\n+++ b/docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md\n@@@ -110,6 -112,8 +112,12 @@@ Cross-referencing `docs/edge-cases.md` \n  \n  **Still open** (deliberately deferred, not oversights):\n  \n++<<<<<<< HEAD\n +- **Watch mode does not observe `node_modules`.** A change to a tsconfig, jsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above a source directory (`WatchSession::is_resolution_config`) does reach `update_file`, which rebuilds the session from scratch (`Revision::rebuilt`) and returns the full delta; watchers add those files with `resolution_config_files()`. A package edited in place without a lockfile change still needs `rebuild()`.\n++=======\n+ - **The dependency layer only grows during a watch session.** A demand an edit removes leaves its declarations loaded; they change no output (a name nothing references is never looked up), and `rebuild()` starts from a fresh layer.\n+ \n+ - **Watch mode does not observe `tsconfig.json`, `package.json` or `node_modules` changes.** They change module resolution for every component; restart the session (or call `rebuild()`) after editing them.\n++>>>>>>> fix/rdt-file-path\n  - **`watch --out` write failures are silently discarded** and writes are non-atomic (`docs/edge-cases.md` line 72-73; `docs/root-cause-analysis.md` line 139). This is CLI-layer (`cli/commands/watch.rs`), outside this subsystem's scope (`crates/core` non-negotiable #6 doesn't reach the CLI), but it directly affects how trustworthy `WatchSession`'s output is once it leaves this module.\n  - **LSP `Content-Length` header has no upper bound before allocation** (`docs/edge-cases.md` P1-2) — CLI-layer (`cli/commands/lsp.rs`), noted here only because it's adjacent to watch-mode's session lifecycle, not because it's part of this subsystem.\ndiff --cc packages/vite-plugin/README.md\nindex dc4a16d7,ca0f901a..00000000\n--- a/packages/vite-plugin/README.md\n+++ b/packages/vite-plugin/README.md\n@@@ -37,9 -37,9 +37,15 @@@ import.meta.hot?.on\n  )\n  ```\n  \n++<<<<<<< HEAD\n +A change to a tsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above `srcDirs` (installing a package, editing `paths`) re-extracts everything and arrives as an ordinary update event.\n +\n +In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs`, or to that configuration, triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n++=======\n+ Pass `loadDependencies: true` to resolve the types your props import from installed packages; by default they stay named references.\n+ \n+ In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs` triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n++>>>>>>> fix/rdt-file-path\n  \n  Extraction runs on OXC through [`caliper-docgen-napi`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/caliper-docgen-napi), so a single-file update takes about 2ms. Requires Vite 7 or 8. The module uses the canonical output format, not the `react-docgen-typescript` shape.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d502267a-593d-407f-a455-a82b6abb1592","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:00:00.394Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"diff --cc docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md\nindex d8a4ccec,9314e3a4..00000000\n--- a/docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md\n+++ b/docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md\n@@@ -110,6 -112,8 +112,12 @@@ Cross-referencing `docs/edge-cases.md` \n  \n  **Still open** (deliberately deferred, not oversights):\n  \n++<<<<<<< HEAD\n +- **Watch mode does not observe `node_modules`.** A change to a tsconfig, jsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above a source directory (`WatchSession::is_resolution_config`) does reach `update_file`, which rebuilds the session from scratch (`Revision::rebuilt`) and returns the full delta; watchers add those files with `resolution_config_files()`. A package edited in place without a lockfile change still needs `rebuild()`.\n++=======\n+ - **The dependency layer only grows during a watch session.** A demand an edit removes leaves its declarations loaded; they change no output (a name nothing references is never looked up), and `rebuild()` starts from a fresh layer.\n+ \n+ - **Watch mode does not observe `tsconfig.json`, `package.json` or `node_modules` changes.** They change module resolution for every component; restart the session (or call `rebuild()`) after editing them.\n++>>>>>>> fix/rdt-file-path\n  - **`watch --out` write failures are silently discarded** and writes are non-atomic (`docs/edge-cases.md` line 72-73; `docs/root-cause-analysis.md` line 139). This is CLI-layer (`cli/commands/watch.rs`), outside this subsystem's scope (`crates/core` non-negotiable #6 doesn't reach the CLI), but it directly affects how trustworthy `WatchSession`'s output is once it leaves this module.\n  - **LSP `Content-Length` header has no upper bound before allocation** (`docs/edge-cases.md` P1-2) — CLI-layer (`cli/commands/lsp.rs`), noted here only because it's adjacent to watch-mode's session lifecycle, not because it's part of this subsystem.\ndiff --cc packages/vite-plugin/README.md\nindex dc4a16d7,ca0f901a..00000000\n--- a/packages/vite-plugin/README.md\n+++ b/packages/vite-plugin/README.md\n@@@ -37,9 -37,9 +37,15 @@@ import.meta.hot?.on\n  )\n  ```\n  \n++<<<<<<< HEAD\n +A change to a tsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above `srcDirs` (installing a package, editing `paths`) re-extracts everything and arrives as an ordinary update event.\n +\n +In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs`, or to that configuration, triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n++=======\n+ Pass `loadDependencies: true` to resolve the types your props import from installed packages; by default they stay named references.\n+ \n+ In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs` triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n++>>>>>>> fix/rdt-file-path\n  \n  Extraction runs on OXC through [`caliper-docgen-napi`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/caliper-docgen-napi), so a single-file update takes about 2ms. Requires Vite 7 or 8. The module uses the canonical output format, not the `react-docgen-typescript` shape.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e8219786-1f0c-41b7-9d15-5c1739afc23e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"feat/watch-rebuild-on-config","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":112,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aef58104-3449-4e8e-a2a9-4ff8e1cc0dbd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/watch-rebuild-on-config","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumo