{"parentUuid":"1bf5e135-e317-49f2-ae58-98df9879d346","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb563e85-80fa-4200-bf18-7a747f7a254b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K2jCJZNBSSheCSxhfAVPWa","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"78d3a405-3ff4-46f6-a39a-7d19f784794b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:00:13.311Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md","oldString":"<<<<<<< HEAD\n- **Watch mode does not observe `node_modules`.** A change to a tsconfig, jsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above a source directory (`WatchSession::is_resolution_config`) does reach `update_file`, which rebuilds the session from scratch (`Revision::rebuilt`) and returns the full delta; watchers add those files with `resolution_config_files()`. A package edited in place without a lockfile change still needs `rebuild()`.\n=======\n- **The dependency layer only grows during a watch session.** A demand an edit removes leaves its declarations loaded; they change no output (a name nothing references is never looked up), and `rebuild()` starts from a fresh layer.\n\n- **Watch mode does not observe `tsconfig.json`, `package.json` or `node_modules` changes.** They change module resolution for every component; restart the session (or call `rebuild()`) after editing them.\n>>>>>>> fix/rdt-file-path","newString":"- **The dependency layer only grows during a watch session.** A demand an edit removes leaves its declarations loaded; they change no output (a name nothing references is never looked up), and a rebuild (a configuration change below, or `rebuild()`) starts from a fresh layer.\n\n- **Watch mode does not observe `node_modules`.** A change to a tsconfig, jsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above a source directory (`WatchSession::is_resolution_config`) does reach `update_file`, which rebuilds the session from scratch (`Revision::rebuilt`) and returns the full delta; watchers add those files with `resolution_config_files()`. A package edited in place without a lockfile change still needs `rebuild()`.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":112,"oldLines":12,"newStart":112,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," **Still open** (deliberately deferred, not oversights):"," ","-<<<<<<< HEAD","-- **Watch mode does not observe `node_modules`.** A change to a tsconfig, jsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above a source directory (`WatchSession::is_resolution_config`) does reach `update_file`, which rebuilds the session from scratch (`Revision::rebuilt`) and returns the full delta; watchers add those files with `resolution_config_files()`. A package edited in place without a lockfile change still needs `rebuild()`.","-=======","-- **The dependency layer only grows during a watch session.** A demand an edit removes leaves its declarations loaded; they change no output (a name nothing references is never looked up), and `rebuild()` starts from a fresh layer.","+- **The dependency layer only grows during a watch session.** A demand an edit removes leaves its declarations loaded; they change no output (a name nothing references is never looked up), and a rebuild (a configuration change below, or `rebuild()`) starts from a fresh layer."," ","-- **Watch mode does not observe `tsconfig.json`, `package.json` or `node_modules` changes.** They change module resolution for every component; restart the session (or call `rebuild()`) after editing them.","->>>>>>> fix/rdt-file-path","+- **Watch mode does not observe `node_modules`.** A change to a tsconfig, jsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above a source directory (`WatchSession::is_resolution_config`) does reach `update_file`, which rebuilds the session from scratch (`Revision::rebuilt`) and returns the full delta; watchers add those files with `resolution_config_files()`. A package edited in place without a lockfile change still needs `rebuild()`."," - **`watch --out` write failures are silently discarded** and writes are non-atomic (`docs/edge-cases.md` line 72-73; `docs/root-cause-analysis.md` line 139). This is CLI-layer (`cli/commands/watch.rs`), outside this subsystem's scope (`crates/core` non-negotiable #6 doesn't reach the CLI), but it directly affects how trustworthy `WatchSession`'s output is once it leaves this module."," - **LSP `Content-Length` header has no upper bound before allocation** (`docs/edge-cases.md` P1-2) — CLI-layer (`cli/commands/lsp.rs`), noted here only because it's adjacent to watch-mode's session lifecycle, not because it's part of this subsystem."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1bf5e135-e317-49f2-ae58-98df9879d346","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/watch-rebuild-on-config","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"78d3a405-3ff4-46f6-a39a-7d19f784794b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01K2jCJZNBSSheCSxhfAVPWa","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Edit\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":39},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b1bb7706-efc3-4e3f-983c-d25bdeec633d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:00:13.310Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/watch-rebuild-on-config","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"30e813b2-a2ab-4f9a-8e4d-5888f513662c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb563e85-80fa-4200-bf18-7a747f7a254b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NpEDj9aMRo2fQzb58uB7xf","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/packages/vite-plugin/README.md has been updated successfully. (note: the file had been modified on disk since you last read it — the edit applied cleanly, but the file contains other changes not in your context. Read it before edits that depend on surrounding content.)"}]},"uuid":"072dac44-a073-40f4-84a0-d1116a65bc1e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:00:13.376Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/packages/vite-plugin/README.md","oldString":"<<<<<<< HEAD\nA change to a tsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above `srcDirs` (installing a package, editing `paths`) re-extracts everything and arrives as an ordinary update event.\n\nIn `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs`, or to that configuration, triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n=======\nPass `loadDependencies: true` to resolve the types your props import from installed packages; by default they stay named references.\n\nIn `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs` triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n>>>>>>> fix/rdt-file-path","newString":"A change to a tsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above `srcDirs` (installing a package, editing `paths`) re-extracts everything and arrives as an ordinary update event.\n\nPass `loadDependencies: true` to resolve the types your props import from installed packages; by default they stay named references.\n\nIn `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs`, or to that configuration, triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.","originalFile":"# caliper-docgen-vite-plugin\n\nA Vite plugin that exposes your React components' props on a virtual module and updates it through HMR as you edit.\n\n```bash\nnpm install --save-dev caliper-docgen-vite-plugin\n```\n\n```ts\n// vite.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'\nimport { caliperDocgen } from 'caliper-docgen-vite-plugin'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react(), caliperDocgen({ srcDirs: ['src'] })],\n})\n```\n\n```ts\nimport docgen from 'virtual:caliper-docgen'\n\n// A component maps each prop name to an id; each distinct prop is written once, in `docgen.props`.\nconst label = docgen.props[docgen.components['Button'].props.label]\n```\n\nOn every change the virtual module reloads with the same output a fresh extraction would give, including removed components, enums and diagnostics. To apply changes yourself, listen for the update event:\n\n```ts\nimport.meta.hot?.on(\n  'caliper-docgen:update',\n  ({ updatedKeys, updatedComponents, props, removedKeys, diagnostics, removedDiagnostics }) => {\n    // Events arrive in revision order, each a delta from the one before: delete removedKeys, set updatedKeys[i] to\n    // updatedComponents[i], merge props into docgen.props, drop removedDiagnostics and add diagnostics. Props no\n    // component refers to any more can be dropped.\n  },\n)\n```\n\n<<<<<<< HEAD\nA change to a tsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above `srcDirs` (installing a package, editing `paths`) re-extracts everything and arrives as an ordinary update event.\n\nIn `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs`, or to that configuration, triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n=======\nPass `loadDependencies: true` to resolve the types your props import from installed packages; by default they stay named references.\n\nIn `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs` triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n>>>>>>> fix/rdt-file-path\n\nExtraction runs on OXC through [`caliper-docgen-napi`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/caliper-docgen-napi), so a single-file update takes about 2ms. Requires Vite 7 or 8. The module uses the canonical output format, not the `react-docgen-typescript` shape.\n\nDocs and benchmarks: [orin-dx.com/tools/caliper](https://orin-dx.com/tools/caliper/). Source: [github.com/orin-dx/caliper](https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper).\n\n## License\n\nFSL-1.1-MIT. Each version becomes MIT two years after its release.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":37,"oldLines":15,"newStart":37,"newLines":11,"lines":[" )"," ```"," ","-<<<<<<< HEAD"," A change to a tsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above `srcDirs` (installing a package, editing `paths`) re-extracts everything and arrives as an ordinary update event."," ","-In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs`, or to that configuration, triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.","-======="," Pass `loadDependencies: true` to resolve the types your props import from installed packages; by default they stay named references."," ","-In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs` triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.","->>>>>>> fix/rdt-file-path","+In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs`, or to that configuration, triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails."," "," Extraction runs on OXC through [`caliper-docgen-napi`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/caliper-docgen-napi), so a single-file update takes about 2ms. Requires Vite 7 or 8. The module uses the canonical output format, not the `react-docgen-typescript` shape."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"staleRecovered":true,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30e813b2-a2ab-4f9a-8e4d-5888f513662c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/watch-rebuild-on-config","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
