{"parentUuid":"43036042-99f6-41a1-9854-987f10b345f4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Detection precision: render evidence, non-destructive renames, wrapper evidence","description":"Typed function/arrow/HOC-arg and function declarations require render evidence (JSX/createElement/children/null body or React return type); declare function with JSX return accepted; wrapper first-arg evidence (render fn, tag + element type arg, PascalCase reference); reject createContext; diagnostic for rejected recorded candidates; remove empty-props guard (dropped 84 real Chakra comps); renames never delete an exported base. Negative families in shapes.rs; fix tests that pinned silent drops.","activeForm":"Fixing detection precision","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Type-text P0s: quoted substitution, Infinity/NaN, Required extends, key sets, typeof props, generic alias in prop, cache bump","description":"Done in #72 (structured args, typeof props, Required extends, quoted substitution, Infinity) and #73 (key sets). Generic alias in prop position moved to task 5 with the memo.","activeForm":"Fixing type-text defects","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Discovery and small correctness: relative excludes, export-default misses, Required unwrap, PropsWithChildren children","description":"Match .test./.stories. excludes relative to src dir; detect export default arrow/memo/forwardRef/class; stop treating Required<P> as transparent; children from PropsWithChildren.","activeForm":"Fixing discovery and small correctness issues","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Watch revision model shared with cold path, Vite plugin and CLI watch fixes","description":"One immutable Revision, single writer, assemble shared with extract(), real dependency edges (barrels, ../, aliases, .js), deltas with removals, seeded diagnostics, filters/plugins in watch; Vite: removals, keys, invalidation, build --watch, build errors; CLI: write --out at start, r re-extracts. Gate: snapshot()==extract() property test.","activeForm":"Building the watch revision model","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"5","subject":"Diagnostics identity and dedup, resolution memoization, cache fingerprint","description":"Dedup by (code,file,span,subject) with affected components; memoize type resolution per run; cache keyed on crate version + extractor fingerprint with versioned payload; diagnostics on cache decode failure.","activeForm":"Reworking diagnostics and cache","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Docs, DX and ADR 0007 amendment; restate #64 figures","description":"Docs, DX and the semantic merge contract (Codex #4): ADR amending 0007 with component identity, field-level precedence (structural identity, checker props), diagnostic retirement, provenance and disagreement handling; triggers that do not rely only on visible incompleteness; schemaVersion vs mode/provenance fields. One reproducible scorecard (recall own/any, hand-labelled precision, prop type/required/default/description agreement, time, RSS, watch parity, with and without deps). Reconcile benchmarks.md, STATUS.md and roadmap figures; CLI DX items.","activeForm":"Fixing docs and DX","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"7","subject":"Replace name-based special cases with structural rules","description":"Revised per Codex: symbol origin (not every @types declaration terminal, record why resolution stopped); wrapper detection from callee signature where structural data permits, else labelled inferred and measured; library shortcuts need a type-resolution adapter boundary before moving out of core; finite keyof/mapped evaluator within a stated budget with opaque diagnostics; React tables from installed @types/react only when requested, curated fallback. Blocked by symbol precedence and the precision gate.","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"8","subject":"Delta contract: every changed key and diagnostic in IncrementalUpdate","description":"Codex #3. updated_keys must include kept components whose key or entry changed (name-collision key shifts on delete/create); add removed diagnostics; Vite drops updates older than the newest revision across files. Test: apply every emitted delta to the previous output and assert it equals snapshot(), including collisions, diagnostic disappearance and cross-file reordering.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"9","subject":"Symbol precedence: resolve the binding before builtin or utility names","description":"Codex #1. named.rs checks React builtins and chain.rs checks TS utilities before source lookup, so a local ReactNode/Partial is misread. Resolve the binding first; apply builtin meaning only when the origin is React/TS lib, or as a reported fallback when resolution fails. Tests with local ReactNode, CSSProperties, Partial, Required.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"10","subject":"Render evidence: count only returned JSX and resolved element types; precision gate","description":"Codex #2. JSX must be in a returned expression, not any nested callback; element return annotations resolve their origin; wrapper/rename name heuristics frozen. Add a hand-labelled precision sample per detection family (roadmap 95% gate) before any detector expansion.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"11","subject":"Silent degradations: tsconfig parsing, RenderProps shortcut, cache size bound","description":"Codex #5/#6. Parse tsconfig with a JSONC-aware parser and report read/parse failures; RenderProps keeps the function form or reports opacity; bound the DTS cache file size before decoding. Silence list records why resolution stopped.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"12","subject":"Interned props: ADR 0009","description":"Write docs/adr/0009 for the canonical output's prop table (content-hash ids, update carries referenced entries, rdt stays expanded) and index it.","activeForm":"Writing ADR 0009","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"13","subject":"Interned props: Rust serialization","description":"Custom Serialize/Deserialize for ExtractionOutput and IncrementalUpdate writing a top-level props table and prop ids in components (props and notableInherited). FNV-1a 64 of compact prop JSON; collision is a serialization error. Snapshots stay expanded. Tests: round-trip, id stability, collision, update table completeness. Update schema command.","activeForm":"Implementing interned serialization","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"14","subject":"Interned props: JS consumers and docs","description":"Update packages/napi/index.d.ts types, Vite plugin update payload (props), apps/validate normalize, docs describing the canonical format; measure size and time on corpora; open stacked PR on perf/output-path.","activeForm":"Updating JS consumers","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"15","subject":"Prove dependency loading: stage 1 loader prototype","description":"Standalone scratch Rust prototype (outside the repo) of name-driven dependency .d.ts loading with a per-package export index and work-queue overlap with project parsing. Measure files touched, cold vs warm-index time, overlap gain, watch new-import cost on the 5 installed corpora.","activeForm":"Prototyping the dependency loader","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"16","subject":"Prove dependency loading: stage 2 end-to-end on an experimental branch","description":"Experimental caliper branch (local, behind a flag) plugging the loader into a shared dependency layer before resolve; measure resolved types, output change, leaks, display-filter-before-resolve and session memo, timings cold/warm/watch vs today and RDT.","activeForm":"Measuring dependency loading end to end","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"17","subject":"Dependency types 1: resolver groundwork PR","description":"tsconfig auto-discovery, customConditions, .d.mts/.d.cts, the two resolve_dts retries (@types fallback for .js exports; types-only conditions retry), one shared ResolveOptions builder. PR against main, ported from exp/dependency-types without the loader.","activeForm":"Building resolver groundwork","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"18","subject":"Dependency types 2: namespace re-exports","description":"Extractor promotion of `import * as ns; export { ns as N }` and named-import namespace members in resolve_to_canonical.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"19","subject":"Dependency types 3: share resolved props in memory","description":"Arc-shared resolved props across components so large inherited sources (chakra) don't copy per component; then the session memo.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"20","subject":"Dependency types 4: type-text fixes","description":"Keep alias names when expansion is conditional/mapped, generic defaults, handler types, callback return types, fake (e: void).","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"21","subject":"Dependency types 5: loader + dependency layer behind a flag, with ADRs","description":"Persisted per-package index, fallback indexes, precedence, value index, leak guards, watch demand diff; ADR for loading and for replacing DtsCache for dependencies.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"22","subject":"Replace trybuild compile_fail test with a doctest pair","description":"compile_fail + compiling ParsedProp::new doctests on ParsedProp; remove trybuild dev-dep and tests/compile_fail. Independent PR off main.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"23","subject":"ComponentProps<typeof X> resolves to X's props","description":"Direct props position (known::component_props) looks up component values (local, imported, namespace members) like extends' component_props_of. Stacked on namespace re-exports.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"24","subject":"Investigate failing Dependabot PR #84","description":"Find why CI fails on dependabot routine-npm PR #84 and fix or report.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"25","subject":"Track A: precision and detection PR chain","description":"Factory payload props, called-only helpers, exported flag, rdt filePath — stacked off main.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"26","subject":"Track B: Storybook integration PR chain","description":"NAPI in worker_threads, Storybook 11 docgen provider package, Storybook 10 Vite __docgenInfo mode, remove --format storybook.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"27","subject":"Track C: hardening, gates and docs PR chain","description":"Watch rebuild on config changes, ensure-fresh session API, size-normalized CI gates + scorecard, stale docs (covers task #6).","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":27},"type":"attachment","uuid":"18a406b3-70b0-45b9-87b1-e155a922a19e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:02:38.186Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n\nHere are the existing tasks:\n\n#1. [completed] Detection precision: render evidence, non-destructive renames, wrapper evidence\n#2. [completed] Type-text P0s: quoted substitution, Infinity/NaN, Required extends, key sets, typeof props, generic alias in prop, cache bump\n#3. [completed] Discovery and small correctness: relative excludes, export-default misses, Required unwrap, PropsWithChildren children\n#4. [completed] Watch revision model shared with cold path, Vite plugin and CLI watch fixes\n#5. [completed] Diagnostics identity and dedup, resolution memoization, cache fingerprint\n#6. [completed] Docs, DX and ADR 0007 amendment; restate #64 figures\n#7. [pending] Replace name-based special cases with structural rules\n#8. [completed] Delta contract: every changed key and diagnostic in IncrementalUpdate\n#9. [completed] Symbol precedence: resolve the binding before builtin or utility names\n#10. [completed] Render evidence: count only returned JSX and resolved element types; precision gate\n#11. [completed] Silent degradations: tsconfig parsing, RenderProps shortcut, cache size bound\n#12. [completed] Interned props: ADR 0009\n#13. [completed] Interned props: Rust serialization\n#14. [completed] Interned props: JS consumers and docs\n#15. [completed] Prove dependency loading: stage 1 loader prototype\n#16. [completed] Prove dependency loading: stage 2 end-to-end on an experimental branch\n#17. [completed] Dependency types 1: resolver groundwork PR\n#18. [completed] Dependency types 2: namespace re-exports\n#19. [completed] Dependency types 3: share resolved props in memory\n#20. [completed] Dependency types 4: type-text fixes\n#21. [completed] Dependency types 5: loader + dependency layer behind a flag, with ADRs\n#22. [completed] Replace trybuild compile_fail test with a doctest pair\n#23. [completed] ComponentProps<typeof X> resolves to X's props\n#24. [completed] Investigate failing Dependabot PR #84\n#25. [completed] Track A: precision and detection PR chain\n#26. [completed] Track B: Storybook integration PR chain\n#27. [completed] Track C: hardening, gates and docs PR chain\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/w