s\nM  crates/cli/tests/cmd/extract_help.trycmd\nM  crates/cli/tests/cmd/schema.trycmd\nM  crates/core/Cargo.toml\nM  crates/core/src/cache.rs\nM  crates/core/src/cache/snapshots/caliper_docgen_core__cache__golden__source_data_bytes_are_stable_for_the_current_schema_version.snap\nA  crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs\nA  crates/core/src/dependency_types/tests.rs\nM  crates/core/src/extractor/interface.rs\nM  crates/core/src/extractor/jsdoc.rs\nM  crates/core/src/extractor/mod.rs\nM  crates/core/src/extractor/tests.rs\nA  crates/core/src/extractor/uses.rs\nM  crates/core/src/extractor/visit.rs\nM  crates/core/src/extractor/wrapper.rs\nM  crates/core/src/import_map.rs\nM  crates/core/src/known.rs\nM  crates/core/src/lib.rs\nM  crates/core/src/nam\n... (truncated because it exceeds 2k characters. If you need more information, run \"git status\" using Bash)\n\nRecent commits:\n2e2dcd8a style: name the provider's lazy session promise apart from the session\n24426b2a fix: load the native binding on the first docgen request\n823a2ba3 feat: add a Storybook 11 docgen provider backed by a caliper session\n824dd11d fix: match Storybook's React docgen in the RDT projection\nd1fe1d42 feat: expose react-docgen-typescript docgen for session components to Node"}},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fd6beda6-c75a-45cd-9ca7-407069f74a60","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:03:42.854Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# userEmail\nThe user's email address is gabe@techworx.dev. Use it only to identify the user, such as for authorship, attribution, or filtering their own work. Never send it to an unrelated service, such as in a request header, URL, or payload, unless the user explicitly asks.\n# gitStatus\nThis is the git status at the start of the conversation. Note that this status is a snapshot in time, and will not update during the conversation.\n\nCurrent branch: feat/storybook-provider\n\nMain branch (you will usual