{"parentUuid":"9b4b34e3-6a84-43e2-b9a4-171ef23f068a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb563e85-80fa-4200-bf18-7a747f7a254b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, EnterWorktree, Grep, Read, ReadNotifications, SendMessage, Skill, TaskCreate, TaskStop, TaskUpdate, ToolSearch, WebSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Main thread:** improve caliper-docgen (Rust/OXC React props extractor; Storybook integration is \"the whole point\") via stacked, non-draft PRs.\n   - **Dependency types (this phase):** \"Let's explore and prove it out first\"; then \"Let's get going on this work now\".\n   - **Approved order:** resolver groundwork → namespace re-exports → shared props → type-text fixes → loader behind a flag, with ADRs.\n   - \"Yes, replace trybuild, help me decide if the collapse inherited props applies locally too. Do all of the rest, commit appropriatelly and stack PRs\".\n     - I recommended collapse for dependency sources only (react-component-meta parity) as the default, with a `collapseInheritedProps` option.\n   - \"Keep going on features, polish and hardening\".\n   - **Latest:** \"Let's stack and cleanup the PRs appropriately\" — put all open PRs into one linear stack in merge order, resolve conflicts, and clean up worktrees and branches.\n   - **Release-related:**\n     - User: \"yes rerun it\" (release); \"Fixed the forbidden issue\".\n     - User: \"We need to bump to the latest Callisto\" — done in #98.\n     - User: \"Callisto doesn't support OIDC yet\" — keep the NPM_TOKEN step.\n     - User: \"But GH is setup for it\" — `id-token: write` is already present.\n   - User asked for the Rust best practice on compile-fail tests (answered: trybuild for proc-macro diagnostics; compile_fail doctests for type invariants; error codes are nightly-only).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Dependency loading:**\n     - Name-driven loading of `.d.ts` files before resolution, into a shared Arc dependency layer.\n     - A per-package export index keyed by realpath + resolver config hash, validated by `package.json` mtime+size.\n     - Precedence: project > known shortcut > dependency > builtin.\n     - A value index for `ComponentProps<typeof X>`.\n     - Leak guards (no dependency components or enums in output).\n     - A watch demand diff.\n     - ADRs 0010–0012.\n     - `--load-dependencies` is off by default.\n     - `collapseInheritedProps: dependencies|all|none`, threshold 30.\n   - **ModuleResolvers (#97):**\n     - tsconfig auto-discovery: `resolve_file`/`resolve_dts` take the importing file, not its directory.\n     - `customConditions` read via json-strip-comments.\n     - `.d.mts`/`.d.cts` and extension aliases.\n     - Retries: `types_first` conditions, then `@types/<name>`.\n     - A declaration path must exist.\n   - Shared `Arc<ParsedProp>` with a per-run interface memo (#105).\n   - Canonical JSON prop interning, ADR 0009 (shipped).\n   - **Storybook 11:** server-side docgen provider (`experimental_docgenProvider`, `createDocgenProvider`, worker_threads, argTypes payload).\n   - **Storybook 10:** Vite `__docgenInfo` injection.\n   - Cache schema version bumps: #103 → 15, #107 → 16, merged with #113 → 17.\n   - **Callisto:** 0.12 waits up to 6 minutes for npm; 0.13 is on crates.io but has no tag or GitHub release; there's no OIDC support yet.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (latest-relevant):\n   - **`/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/restack.py`** — the restack driver. `ORDER` (index: PR branch):\n     - 0: #98 `ci/callisto-0.12`\n     - 1: #102 `docs/oxfmt-073-toml`\n     - 2: #100 `test/doctest-seal`\n     - 3: #97 `fix/resolver-groundwork`\n     - 4: #99 `feat/namespace-reexports`\n     - 5: #101 `feat/component-props-of-typeof`\n     - 6: #103 `fix/function-type-text`\n     - 7: #104 `fix/alias-display`\n     - 8: #105 `perf/shared-props`\n     - 9: #106 `docs/adr-dependency-types`\n     - 10: #107 `feat/load-dependency-types`\n     - 11: #109 `feat/collapse-inherited-props`\n     - 12: #121 `fix/jsdoc-one-line-function`\n     - 13: #122 `fix/dom-handler-overwrite`\n     - 14: #123 `fix/zod-infer-unwrap`\n     - 15: #110 `fix/factory-payload-props`\n     - 16: #112 `fix/called-helpers-are-not-components`\n     - 17: #113 `feat/exported-flag`\n     - 18: #115 `fix/rdt-file-path`\n     - 19: #111 `feat/watch-rebuild-on-config`\n     - 20: #114 `feat/session-ensure-fresh`\n     - 21: #116 `ci/size-normalized-gates`\n     - 22: #118 `docs/status-and-ts7`\n     - 23: #108 `spike/napi-in-worker-threads`\n     - 24: #117 `feat/storybook-provider`\n     - 25: #119 `feat/storybook-vite-docgen`\n     - 26: #120 `chore/remove-storybook-format`\n\n     Behaviour:\n     - Per index it runs `checkout -B branch origin/branch`, stopping if the local branch has unpushed commits.\n     - It then runs `merge --no-edit` of the predecessor (`origin/main` for index 0), stopping on conflict with exit 2.\n     - On success it pushes if anything changed, then `gh pr edit --base`, skipping when the base already matches.\n     - After a manual resolution: commit, push the branch manually, then rerun from that index.\n   - **`/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/resolve_one_sided.py`** — keeps the non-empty side of a conflict block. It didn't help here: every #117 conflict is two-sided.\n   - **`crates/core/src/cache.rs`** (resolved on #113):\n     ```rust\n     /// 16: `LexedExport::LocalDeclaration` gained `declared_as`.\n     /// 17: component mappings record whether they are exported.\n     const CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION: u32 = 17;\n     ```\n     The golden snapshot was regenerated with `INSTA_UPDATE=always`.\n   - **`docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md`** and **`packages/vite-plugin/README.md`** (resolved on #111): both sides' bullets and paragraphs combined.\n   - **`docs/STATUS.md`** (resolved on #118): combined paragraph about types from other packages and `--load-dependencies`.\n   - **Current conflicts on #117** (in the worktree, merge in progress):\n     - **`crates/core/src/pipeline/rdt.rs`** (from #117) has `type_json` (enum with `raw`), `omits`, `docgen_info(entry)` (keeps children), private `component_doc(entry, keep)` and `pub fn serialize(output: &ExtractionOutput)`. It needs to gain `filePath` in `component_doc` and `serialize(output, include_unexported: bool)` filtering on `entry.exported`. `entry.props` is now `Arc<ParsedProp>`, so `keep(prop)` may need `&**prop`.\n     - **`crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs`** — the conflict at line 81 should be replaced with:\n       ```rust\n       /// `--format rdt`: react-docgen-typescript's shape, shared with the NAPI binding. Like react-docgen-typescript, only\n       /// exported components unless asked.\n       pub fn serialize_rdt(\n           output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n           include_unexported: bool,\n       ) -> serde_json::Result<String> {\n           caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::rdt::serialize(output, include_unexported)\n       }\n\n       /// The components a compatibility format writes: like react-docgen-typescript, only exported ones unless asked.\n       fn compat_components(\n           output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n           include_unexported: bool,\n       ) -> impl Iterator<Item = (&String, &caliper_docgen_core::types::ComponentEntry)> {\n           output.components.iter().filter(move |(_, entry)| include_unexported || entry.exported)\n       ```\n       The closing `}` follows the marker. `serialize_storybook(output, include_unexported)` still exists and uses `compat_components`; #120 removes it later.\n     - **`crates/cli/src/commands/extract/tests.rs`**: keep both `docgen_info_keeps_undocumented_children_for_storybook` (HEAD) and `compat_formats_omit_unexported_components_unless_asked` (theirs), adjusting the closing brace.\n     - **`crates/core/src/pipeline/watch.rs`**: keep both HEAD's `current_output()` method and theirs (`is_resolution_config`, `resolution_config_files`). Ours lacks its closing `    }`; insert `    }\\n\\n` between.\n     - **`crates/binding/src/lib.rs`**: keep both HEAD's `session_docgen_info` and theirs (`ensure_fresh`, `resolution_config_files`, `is_resolution_config`); insert `}\\n\\n` between.\n     - **`packages/napi/binding.d.ts`**: keep both (`sessionDocgenInfo`, and `resolutionConfigFiles` with a `/**` opener between).\n     - **`packages/napi/index.js`**: keep both export lines.\n     - **`crates/core/src/types/output.rs`**: take theirs (`PropType::Function` printing) and drop HEAD's `EventHandler` arms, since #103 removed `EventHandler`.\n     - **`crates/core/src/types/output/tests.rs`**: take theirs (`an_operand_is_parenthesized_where_typescript_needs_it`) and drop HEAD's `EventHandler` test.\n     - **`docs/architecture/napi-binding.md`** (2 blocks) and **`docs/architecture/serialization-formats.md`** (1 block): combine.\n   - **Earlier PR content** (for reference):\n     - #97 ModuleResolvers in `resolver/mod.rs` and `react.rs`.\n     - #99 `ReExportNamespace` promotion in `extractor/mod.rs`, `import_map.rs`, `import.rs`.\n     - #101 chain.rs step 0.6 calling `extends::component_props_of`.\n     - #100 doctest pair on `ParsedProp`, trybuild removed.\n     - #102 oxfmt 0.73 TOML formatting in `docs/archive`.\n     - #98 Callisto pin `c3d524d3aba359f5e767007ea76d229e8a291dc3`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Worktree guard:** it blocks complex shell commands (computed values, loops, `git -C`, inline Python heredocs). Use simple commands, Write+python scripts or the Edit tool. The most recent block hit an inline Python edit of `extract.rs`.\n   - **`gh pr edit` GraphQL transient error:** the script now skips the edit when the base already matches.\n   - **trybuild slowness:** it was the slow test locally; replaced in #100.\n   - **Flaky tests:**\n     - `watch_process a_signal_restores_the_terminal_mode_the_session_changed` failed once and passed on rerun. Track C also reported it as flaky; a fix is still pending.\n     - `tsc-client` timing tests flake under load.\n   - **`extract_help.trycmd` after the merge:** only option order changed; regenerated with `TRYCMD=overwrite`.\n   - **My grep filter hid HEAD lines** in the combined diff, which made me misread the conflicts as one-sided. Fix: view the full conflict blocks.\n   - **Release:**\n     - Transient API error, then npm 403 (automation token; the user fixed the package setting).\n     - Callisto 0.11's npm visibility check needed repeated re-runs; loop script `tmp/release_loop.sh`. 0.3.0 fully released.\n   - **I wrongly attempted an OIDC workflow change;** the user said Callisto doesn't support OIDC, so I reverted it and deleted the branch.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Restack progress:** done through index 23 (#108 merged and pushed). Conflicts resolved and verified at #113, #111 and #118. On #113 the full suite passed: 761 tests, lint clean. On #111: 766 Rust tests and 44 TypeScript tests.\n   - **Cleanup:** agent worktrees removed (`agent-a5e5…`, `a75c…`, `aad4…`, `ac4f…`, `ad20…`, `ad2a…`, `af0f…`, `a1bf…`); branches kept.\n   - **Local-only branches to keep:**\n     - `exp/dependency-types`\n     - `fix/generic-defaults` (dropped work)\n     - `scratch/shared-props-deps`\n     - `scratch/shared-props-deps-before`\n   - **Still to clean up:** remote branches of merged PRs (e.g. `perf/output-path`, `feat/interned-props`, `fix/silent-degradations` and older ones).\n\n6. All user messages (this phase and the most recent):\n   - \"What's next?\" (after the earlier summary)\n   - \"Yes, replace trybuild, help me decide if the collapse inherited props applies locally too. Do all of the rest, commit appropriatelly and stack PRs\"\n   - \"Did the release succeed?\"\n   - \"yes rerun it\"\n   - \"Is that slow test required? HOw do michi and callisto do it?\"\n   - \"What is the best practice in rust-land??\"\n   - \"Fixed the forbidden issue\"\n   - \"I'll have Callisto take a look\"\n   - \"We need to bump to the latest Callisto, this is fixed already\"\n   - \"Isn't 0.13 out?\"\n   - \"This is taking forever\"\n   - \"I've setup trusted publishing\"\n   - \"Callisto doesn't support OIDC yet\"\n   - \"But GH is setup for it\"\n   - \"What's next?\"\n   - \"Keep going on features, polish and hardening\"\n   - \"Let's stack and cleanup the PRs appropriately\"\n   - Earlier this phase:\n     - \"First let's think about the problem structurally and comprehensively…\"\n     - \"Does this all account for dev/watch mode?\"\n     - \"Is there a better, more clever way… Can parallelism help?\"\n     - \"Let's explore and prove it out first. I like that\"\n     - \"Let's get going on this work now\"\n     - \"Stack has conflicts\"\n     - \"Still working on it?\"\n     - \"Ok, sounds good\"\n     - \"RDT allows for exclusions to speed-up parsing right?\"\n     - \"why isn't caliper reading the node_modules types? Does storybook normaly recommend not reading all the node_modules?\"\n     - \"Let's make sure that each have node_modules here\"\n     - \"It's important to resolve dependencies\"\n     - \"Is it stuck?\"\n     - \"What is our average performance compared to RDT now?\"\n     - \"Why is this CI taking 3 hrs?? … This is fucking ridiculous and you must be doing some crazy stuff with the workflows\"\n   - **Standing constraints, which remain in effect:**\n     - Stack PRs, non-draft.\n     - Never push to main, force-push or merge.\n     - The user merges releases.\n     - Keep the NPM_TOKEN step (Callisto has no OIDC yet).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Finish restacking:**\n     - Resolve #117's conflicts, run tests and lint, commit, push `feat/storybook-provider`.\n     - Rerun `restack.py 24` for #119 and #120, resolving any further conflicts.\n     - Verify all PR bases and CI.\n   - **Cleanup:**\n     - Delete remote branches of already-merged PRs (confirm each is merged first).\n     - Optionally fix the flaky terminal-signal test.\n   - **Pending user decisions:**\n     - String default quote style (`'md'` vs `\"md\"`).\n     - Whether chakra-style project sources collapse by default.\n     - An ADR 0010 amendment so curated mode loads React's attribute declarations (handler merge).\n     - When to make `--load-dependencies` the default.\n   - Task #7 (structural rules replacing name-based shortcuts) remains pending.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - **Task:** restacking all open PRs into one linear stack, following \"Let's stack and cleanup the PRs appropriately\".\n   - **Where it stopped:** `restack.py` stopped at index 24:\n     `[24] #117 feat/storybook-provider: CONFLICT merging spike/napi-in-worker-threads: ['crates/binding/src/lib.rs', 'crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs', 'crates/cli/src/commands/extract/tests.rs', 'crates/core/src/pipeline/watch.rs', 'crates/core/src/types/output.rs', 'crates/core/src/types/output/tests.rs', 'docs/architecture/napi-binding.md', 'docs/architecture/serialization-formats.md', 'packages/napi/binding.d.ts', 'packages/napi/index.js']`\n   - **State:** the worktree (`release-0.2.0`) is on `feat/storybook-provider` with the merge in progress. All conflicts are two-sided. My inline-Python attempt to rewrite the `extract.rs` conflict was refused by the worktree guard, so none of these 10 files is resolved yet.\n   - **Planned resolution** (detailed in section 3):\n     - Extend `core/pipeline/rdt.rs` with `filePath` and an `include_unexported` parameter on `serialize`.\n     - CLI wrapper plus `compat_components`.\n     - Keep both sides in the binding, `watch.rs`, d.ts, index.js and the extract tests.\n     - Take theirs (`Function`) in `output.rs` and its tests.\n     - Combine the docs.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   1. Resolve #117's merge conflicts with the Edit tool,