{"parentUuid":"2c715e59-fd5c-4799-a4e7-71f4b2e6010a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/extract_rdt.txt","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/extract_rdt.txt","content":"/// `--format rdt`: react-docgen-typescript's shape, shared with the NAPI binding. Like react-docgen-typescript, only\n/// exported components unless asked.\npub fn serialize_rdt(\n    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n    include_unexported: bool,\n) -> serde_json::Result<String> {\n    caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::rdt::serialize(output, include_unexported)\n}\n\n/// The components a compatibility format writes: like react-docgen-typescript, only exported ones unless asked.\nfn compat_components(\n    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n    include_unexported: bool,\n) -> impl Iterator<Item = (&String, &caliper_docgen_core::types::ComponentEntry)> {\n    output.components.iter().filter(move |(_, entry)| include_unexported || entry.exported)\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"displayPath":"../../../../../.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/extract_rdt.txt"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6ac148f6-8479-4c94-8294-dcdcb2d83b4f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:03:42.762Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/extract_rdt.txt\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t/// `--format rdt`: react-docgen-typescript's shape, shared with the NAPI binding. Like react-docgen-typescript, only\n2\t/// exported components unless asked.\n3\tpub fn serialize_rdt(\n4\t    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n5\t    include_unexported: bool,\n6\t) -> serde_json::Result<String> {\n7\t    caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::rdt::serialize(output, include_unexported)\n8\t}\n9\t\n10\t/// The components a compatibility format writes: like react-docgen-typescript, only exported ones unless asked.\n11\tfn compat_components(\n12\t    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n13\t    include_unexported: bool,\n14\t) -> impl Iterator<Item = (&String, &caliper_docgen_core::types::ComponentEntry)> {\n15\t    output.components.iter().filter(move |(_, entry)| include_unexported || entry.exported)\n16\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/storybook-provider","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"6ac148f6-8479-4c94-8294-dcdcb2d83b4f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/resolve.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/resolve.py","content":"\"\"\"Resolve the first conflict block of a file.\n\nUsage: resolve.py FILE ours|theirs\n       resolve.py FILE both GLUE        (ours + GLUE + theirs; GLUE uses \\\\n escapes)\n       resolve.py FILE with TEXT_FILE   (replace the block with TEXT_FILE's contents)\n\"\"\"\nimport re, sys\n\npath, mode = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\ntext = open(path).read()\nm = re.search(r'<<<<<<< [^\\n]*\\n(.*?)=======\\n(.*?)>>>>>>> [^\\n]*\\n', text, re.S)\nif not m:\n    sys.exit(f'{path}: no conflict block')\nours, theirs = m.group(1), m.group(2)\nif mode == 'ours':\n    new = ours\nelif mode == 'theirs':\n    new = theirs\nelif mode == 'both':\n    new = ours + sys.argv[3].encode().decode('unicode_escape') + theirs\nelif mode == 'with':\n    new = open(sys.argv[3]).read()\nelse:\n    sys.exit(f'unknown mode {mode}')\nopen(path, 'w').write(text[:m.start()] + new + text[m.end():])\nprint(f'{path}: resolved ({mode}); {text.count(\"<<<<<<< \") - 1} block(s) left')\n","numLines":27,"startLine":1,"totalLines":27}},"displayPath":"../../../../../.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/resolve.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9f6111be-c1e5-42a4-941b-c1084ff2d8d2","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:03:42.762Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/resolve.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Resolve the first conflict block of a file.\n2\t\n3\tUsage: resolve.py FILE ours|theirs\n4\t       resolve.py FILE both GLUE        (ours + GLUE + theirs; GLUE uses \\\\n escapes)\n5\t       resolve.py FILE with TEXT_FILE   (replace the block with TEXT_FILE's contents)\n6\t\"\"\"\n7\timport re, sys\n8\t\n9\tpath, mode = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\n10\ttext = open(path).read()\n11\tm = re.search(r'<<<<<<< [^\\n]*\\n(.*?)=======\\n(.*?)>>>>>>> [^\\n]*\\n', text, re.S)\n12\tif not m:\n13\t    sys.exit(f'{path}: no conflict block')\n14\tours, theirs = m.group(1), m.group(2)\n15\tif mode == 'ours':\n16\t    new = ours\n17\telif mode == 'theirs':\n18\t    new = theirs\n19\telif mode == 'both':\n20\t    new = ours + sys.argv[3].encode().decode('unicode_escape') + theirs\n21\telif mode == 'with':\n22\t    new = open(sys.argv[3]).read()\n23\telse:\n24\t    sys.exit(f'unknown mode {mode}')\n25\topen(path, 'w').write(text[:m.start()] + new + text[m.end():])\n26\tprint(f'{path}: resolved ({mode}); {text.count(\"<<<<<<< \") - 1} block(s) left')\n27\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/storybook-provider","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"9f6111be-c1e5-42a4-941b-c1084ff2d8d2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs","content":"use std::io::Write;\n\nuse miette::{IntoDiagnostic, Result, WrapErr};\n\nuse crate::config::{build_options, BuildOptionsArgs};\nuse crate::output::{print_diagnostics, print_summary, write_atomic};\n\n/// Returns the process exit code (0 = success, 2 = extraction reported an\n/// error-severity diagnostic) rather than calling `std::process::exit`\n/// directly — keeps the exit decision testable and lets `main()` be the only\n/// place that actually terminates the process.\npub fn cmd_extract(args: crate::ExtractArgs, quiet: bool, config_path: Option<&str>) -> Result<i32> {\n    use indicatif::{ProgressBar, ProgressStyle};\n\n    let html_attributes = args.html_attributes.map(|m| match m {\n        crate::HtmlAttributeModeArg::Curated => \"curated\",\n        crate::HtmlAttributeModeArg::Full => \"full\",\n        crate::HtmlAttributeModeArg::None => \"none\",\n    });\n    let options = build_options(BuildOptionsArgs {\n        src: &args.src,\n        cache_dir: args.cache_dir.as_deref(),\n        html_attributes,\n        config_path,\n        extra_builtins: &args.extra_builtins,\n        load_dependencies: args.load_dependencies,\n        collapse_inherited_props: args.collapse_inherited_props.map(Into::into),\n    })?;\n\n    let pb = if !quiet && !args.json {\n        let pb = ProgressBar::new_spinner();\n        pb.set_style(ProgressStyle::default_spinner().template(\"{spinner:.cyan} {msg}\").into_diagnostic()?);\n        pb.set_message(\"Extracting...\");\n        pb.enable_steady_tick(std::time::Duration::from_millis(80));\n        Some(pb)\n    } else {\n        None\n    };\n\n    let output = caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::extract(&options);\n\n    if let Some(pb) = pb {\n        pb.finish_and_clear();\n    }\n\n    // --json ignores --out/--format — see ExtractArgs::json's doc comment.\n    if args.json {\n        let mut stdout = std::io::BufWriter::with_capacity(1 << 16, std::io::stdout().lock());\n        caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::write_extraction_output_json(&output, &mut stdout).into_diagnostic()?;\n        writeln!(stdout).and_then(|()| stdout.flush()).into_diagnostic()?;\n    } else {\n        if !quiet {\n            print_summary(&output, quiet);\n            print_diagnostics(&output.diagnostics);\n        }\n\n        let json = match args.format {\n            crate::OutputFormat::Canonical => serde_json::to_string_pretty(&output).into_diagnostic()?,\n            crate::OutputFormat::Rdt => serialize_rdt(&output, args.include_unexported).into_diagnostic()?,\n            crate::OutputFormat::Storybook => {\n                serialize_storybook(&output, args.include_unexported).into_diagnostic()?\n            }\n            crate::OutputFormat::Toon => caliper_docgen_core::toon::render_output_toon(&output),\n        };\n\n        match args.out {\n            Some(ref path) => write_atomic(path, &json).into_diagnostic().wrap_err(format!(\"Writing to {path}\"))?,\n            None => println!(\"{json}\"),\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Must run regardless of --json — this is the one thing CI actually\n    // depends on the exit code for.\n    let exit_code = output.exit_code(false);\n    // The process ends right after this, and freeing a large project's output one allocation at a time is slower\n    // than letting the OS reclaim it.\n    std::mem::forget(output);\n    Ok(exit_code)\n}\n\n<<<<<<< HEAD\n/// `--format rdt`: react-docgen-typescript's shape, shared with the NAPI binding.\npub fn serialize_rdt(output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput) -> serde_json::Result<String> {\n    caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::rdt::serialize(output)\n=======\n/// RDT's type-name convention for literal unions: `{\"name\": \"enum\", \"value\": [...]}`\n/// instead of inlining the literal text into `type.name` as a plain string. Lets\n/// prop-table renderers that pattern-match `type.name === \"enum\"` (a common\n/// Storybook addon integration point) show a `<select>` control for the most\n/// common, most curated props in any design system (variant, size, color…).\nfn rdt_type_json(prop_type: &caliper_docgen_core::types::PropType) -> serde_json::Value {\n    use caliper_docgen_core::types::PropType;\n\n    if prop_type.is_literal_union() {\n        let values: Vec<serde_json::Value> = match prop_type {\n            PropType::Union(members) => members.iter().map(|m| serde_json::json!({\"value\": m.raw_string()})).collect(),\n            PropType::LiteralUnion { members, .. } => {\n                members.iter().map(|m| serde_json::json!({\"value\": format!(\"\\\"{m}\\\"\")})).collect()\n            }\n            _ => vec![],\n        };\n        return serde_json::json!({ \"name\": \"enum\", \"value\": values });\n    }\n    serde_json::json!({ \"name\": prop_type.raw_string() })\n}\n\n/// RDT's default `skipChildrenPropWithoutDoc`: an undocumented `children` says nothing a\n/// prop table can show, so RDT never emits it. Canonical output keeps it.\nfn rdt_omits(prop: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ParsedProp) -> bool {\n    prop.name == \"children\" && prop.description.is_empty()\n}\n\n/// The components a compatibility format writes: like react-docgen-typescript, only exported ones unless asked.\nfn compat_components(\n    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n    include_unexported: bool,\n) -> impl Iterator<Item = (&String, &caliper_docgen_core::types::ComponentEntry)> {\n    output.components.iter().filter(move |(_, entry)| include_unexported || entry.exported)\n}\n\n/// `methods` is always `[]` — this tool doesn't extract class methods, and RDT\n/// consumers (Storybook's docgen addon) only ever read it for class components.\npub fn serialize_rdt(\n    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n    include_unexported: bool,\n) -> serde_json::Result<String> {\n    let mut map = serde_json::Map::new();\n    for (name, entry) in compat_components(output, include_unexported) {\n        let props: serde_json::Map<String, serde_json::Value> = entry\n            .props\n            .iter()\n            .filter(|(_, prop)| !rdt_omits(prop))\n            .map(|(k, prop)| {\n                let obj = serde_json::json!({\n                    \"name\": prop.name,\n                    \"type\": rdt_type_json(&prop.prop_type),\n                    \"required\": prop.required,\n                    \"defaultValue\": prop.default_value.as_ref().map(|d| serde_json::json!({\"value\": d.value, \"computed\": d.computed})),\n                    \"description\": prop.description,\n                    \"parent\": prop.parent.as_ref().map(|p| serde_json::json!({\"name\": p.name, \"fileName\": p.file_name})),\n                });\n                (k.clone(), obj)\n            })\n            .collect();\n        map.insert(\n            name.clone(),\n            serde_json::json!({\n                \"displayName\": entry.display_name,\n                \"filePath\": entry.file_path,\n                \"props\": serde_json::Value::Object(props),\n                \"description\": entry.description,\n                \"methods\": [],\n                \"tags\": entry.tags,\n                \"composes\": entry.composes,\n            }),\n        );\n    }\n    serde_json::to_string_pretty(&serde_json::Value::Object(map))\n>>>>>>> spike/napi-in-worker-threads\n}\n\npub fn serialize_storybook(\n    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n    include_unexported: bool,\n) -> serde_json::Result<String> {\n    let mut map = serde_json::Map::new();\n    for (name, entry) in compat_components(output, include_unexported) {\n        let props: serde_json::Map<String, serde_json::Value> = entry\n            .props\n            .iter()\n            .map(|(k, prop)| {\n                let obj = serde_json::json!({\n                    \"name\": prop.name,\n                    \"type\": { \"name\": prop.prop_type.raw_string() },\n                    \"required\": prop.required,\n                    \"defaultValue\": prop.default_value.as_ref().map(|d| serde_json::json!({\"value\": d.value})),\n                    \"description\": prop.description,\n                });\n                (k.clone(), obj)\n            })\n            .collect();\n        map.insert(\n            name.clone(),\n            serde_json::json!({\n                \"displayName\": entry.display_name,\n                \"props\": serde_json::Value::Object(props),\n                \"description\": entry.description,\n                \"methods\": [],\n            }),\n        );\n    }\n    serde_json::to_string_pretty(&serde_json::Value::Object(map))\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests;\n","numLines":197,"startLine":1,"totalLines":197}},"displayPath":"crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"44266afe-0b1d-4ff3-b550-74713eee4034","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:03:42.762Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/cli/src/commands/extract.rs\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\tuse std::io::Write;\n2\t\n3\tuse miette::{IntoDiagnostic, Result, WrapErr};\n4\t\n5\tuse crate::config::{build_options, BuildOptionsArgs};\n6\tuse crate::output::{print_diagnostics, print_summary, write_atomic};\n7\t\n8\t/// Returns the process exit code (0 = success, 2 = extraction reported an\n9\t/// error-severity diagnostic) rather than calling `std::process::exit`\n10\t/// directly — keeps the exit decision testable and lets `main()` be the only\n11\t/// place that actually terminates the process.\n12\tpub fn cmd_extract(args: crate::ExtractArgs, quiet: bool, config_path: Option<&str>) -> Result<i32> {\n13\t    use indicatif::{ProgressBar, ProgressStyle};\n14\t\n15\t    let html_attributes = args.html_attributes.map(|m| match m {\n16\t        crate::HtmlAttributeModeArg::Curated => \"curated\",\n17\t        crate::HtmlAttributeModeArg::Full => \"full\",\n18\t        crate::HtmlAttributeModeArg::None => \"none\",\n19\t    });\n20\t    let options = build_options(BuildOptionsArgs {\n21\t        src: &args.src,\n22\t        cache_dir: args.cache_dir.as_deref(),\n23\t        html_attributes,\n24\t        config_path,\n25\t        extra_builtins: &args.extra_builtins,\n26\t        load_dependencies: args.load_dependencies,\n27\t        collapse_inherited_props: args.collapse_inherited_props.map(Into::into),\n28\t    })?;\n29\t\n30\t    let pb = if !quiet && !args.json {\n31\t        let pb = ProgressBar::new_spinner();\n32\t        pb.set_style(ProgressStyle::default_spinner().template(\"{spinner:.cyan} {msg}\").into_diagnostic()?);\n33\t        pb.set_message(\"Extracting...\");\n34\t        pb.enable_steady_tick(std::time::Duration::from_millis(80));\n35\t        Some(pb)\n36\t    } else {\n37\t        None\n38\t    };\n39\t\n40\t    let output = caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::extract(&options);\n41\t\n42\t    if let Some(pb) = pb {\n43\t        pb.finish_and_clear();\n44\t    }\n45\t\n46\t    // --json ignores --out/--format — see ExtractArgs::json's doc comment.\n47\t    if args.json {\n48\t        let mut stdout = std::io::BufWriter::with_capacity(1 << 16, std::io::stdout().lock());\n49\t        caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::write_extraction_output_json(&output, &mut stdout).into_diagnostic()?;\n50\t        writeln!(stdout).and_then(|()| stdout.flush()).into_diagnostic()?;\n51\t    } else {\n52\t        if !quiet {\n53\t            print_summary(&output, quiet);\n54\t            print_diagnostics(&output.diagnostics);\n55\t        }\n56\t\n57\t        let json = match args.format {\n58\t            crate::OutputFormat::Canonical => serde_json::to_string_pretty(&output).into_diagnostic()?,\n59\t            crate::OutputFormat::Rdt => serialize_rdt(&output, args.include_unexported).into_diagnostic()?,\n60\t            crate::OutputFormat::Storybook => {\n61\t                serialize_storybook(&output, args.include_unexported).into_diagnostic()?\n62\t            }\n63\t            crate::OutputFormat::Toon => caliper_docgen_core::toon::render_output_toon(&output),\n64\t        };\n65\t\n66\t        match args.out {\n67\t            Some(ref path) => write_atomic(path, &json).into_diagnostic().wrap_err(format!(\"Writing to {path}\"))?,\n68\t            None => println!(\"{json}\"),\n69\t        }\n70\t    }\n71\t\n72\t    // Must run regardless of --json — this is the one thing CI actually\n73\t    // depends on the exit code for.\n74\t    let exit_code = output.exit_code(false);\n75\t    // The process ends right after this, and freeing a large project's output one allocation at a time is slower\n76\t    // than letting the OS reclaim it.\n77\t    std::mem::forget(output);\n78\t    Ok(exit_code)\n79\t}\n80\t\n81\t<<<<<<< HEAD\n82\t/// `--format rdt`: react-docgen-typescript's shape, shared with the NAPI binding.\n83\tpub fn serialize_rdt(output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput) -> serde_json::Result<String> {\n84\t    caliper_docgen_core::pipeline::rdt::serialize(output)\n85\t=======\n86\t/// RDT's type-name convention for literal unions: `{\"name\": \"enum\", \"value\": [...]}`\n87\t/// instead of inlining the literal text into `type.name` as a plain string. Lets\n88\t/// prop-table renderers that pattern-match `type.name === \"enum\"` (a common\n89\t/// Storybook addon integration point) show a `<select>` control for the most\n90\t/// common, most curated props in any design system (variant, size, color…).\n91\tfn rdt_type_json(prop_type: &caliper_docgen_core::types::PropType) -> serde_json::Value {\n92\t    use caliper_docgen_core::types::PropType;\n93\t\n94\t    if prop_type.is_literal_union() {\n95\t        let values: Vec<serde_json::Value> = match prop_type {\n96\t            PropType::Union(members) => members.iter().map(|m| serde_json::json!({\"value\": m.raw_string()})).collect(),\n97\t            PropType::LiteralUnion { members, .. } => {\n98\t                members.iter().map(|m| serde_json::json!({\"value\": format!(\"\\\"{m}\\\"\")})).collect()\n99\t            }\n100\t            _ => vec![],\n101\t        };\n102\t        return serde_json::json!({ \"name\": \"enum\", \"value\": values });\n103\t    }\n104\t    serde_json::json!({ \"name\": prop_type.raw_string() })\n105\t}\n106\t\n107\t/// RDT's default `skipChildrenPropWithoutDoc`: an undocumented `children` says nothing a\n108\t/// prop table can show, so RDT never emits it. Canonical output keeps it.\n109\tfn rdt_omits(prop: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ParsedProp) -> bool {\n110\t    prop.name == \"children\" && prop.description.is_empty()\n111\t}\n112\t\n113\t/// The components a compatibility format writes: like react-docgen-typescript, only exported ones unless asked.\n114\tfn compat_components(\n115\t    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n116\t    include_unexported: bool,\n117\t) -> impl Iterator<Item = (&String, &caliper_docgen_core::types::ComponentEntry)> {\n118\t    output.components.iter().filter(move |(_, entry)| include_unexported || entry.exported)\n119\t}\n120\t\n121\t/// `methods` is always `[]` — this tool doesn't extract class methods, and RDT\n122\t/// consumers (Storybook's docgen addon) only ever read it for class components.\n123\tpub fn serialize_rdt(\n124\t    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n125\t    include_unexported: bool,\n126\t) -> serde_json::Result<String> {\n127\t    let mut map = serde_json::Map::new();\n128\t    for (name, entry) in compat_components(output, include_unexported) {\n129\t        let props: serde_json::Map<String, serde_json::Value> = entry\n130\t            .props\n131\t            .iter()\n132\t            .filter(|(_, prop)| !rdt_omits(prop))\n133\t            .map(|(k, prop)| {\n134\t                let obj = serde_json::json!({\n135\t                    \"name\": prop.name,\n136\t                    \"type\": rdt_type_json(&prop.prop_type),\n137\t                    \"required\": prop.required,\n138\t                    \"defaultValue\": prop.default_value.as_ref().map(|d| serde_json::json!({\"value\": d.value, \"computed\": d.computed})),\n139\t                    \"description\": prop.description,\n140\t                    \"parent\": prop.parent.as_ref().map(|p| serde_json::json!({\"name\": p.name, \"fileName\": p.file_name})),\n141\t                });\n142\t                (k.clone(), obj)\n143\t            })\n144\t            .collect();\n145\t        map.insert(\n146\t            name.clone(),\n147\t            serde_json::json!({\n148\t                \"displayName\": entry.display_name,\n149\t                \"filePath\": entry.file_path,\n150\t                \"props\": serde_json::Value::Object(props),\n151\t                \"description\": entry.description,\n152\t                \"methods\": [],\n153\t                \"tags\": entry.tags,\n154\t                \"composes\": entry.composes,\n155\t            }),\n156\t        );\n157\t    }\n158\t    serde_json::to_string_pretty(&serde_json::Value::Object(map))\n159\t>>>>>>> spike/napi-in-worker-threads\n160\t}\n161\t\n162\tpub fn serialize_storybook(\n163\t    output: &caliper_docgen_core::types::ExtractionOutput,\n164\t    include_unexported: bool,\n165\t) -> serde_json::Result<String> {\n166\t    let mut map = serde_json::Map::new();\n167\t    for (name, entry) in compat_components(output, include_unexported) {\n168\t        let props: serde_json::Map<String, serde_json::Value> = entry\n169\t            .props\n170\t            .iter()\n171\t            .map(|(k, prop)| {\n172\t                let obj = serde_json::json!({\n173\t                    \"name\": prop.name,\n174\t                    \"type\": { \"name\": prop.prop_type.raw_string() },\n175\t                    \"required\": prop.required,\n176\t                    \"defaultValue\": prop.default_value.as_ref().map(|d| serde_json::json!({\"value\": d.value})),\n177\t                    \"description\": prop.description,\n178\t                });\n179\t                (k.clone(), obj)\n180\t            })\n181\t            .collect();\n182\t        map.insert(\n183\t            name.clone(),\n184\t            serde_json::json!({\n185\t                \"displayName\": entry.display_name,\n186\t                \"props\": serde_json::Value::Object(props),\n187\t                \"description\": entry.description,\n188\t                \"methods\": [],\n189\t            }),\n190\t        );\n191\t    }\n192\t    serde_json::to_string_pretty(&serde_json::Value::Object(map))\n193\t}\n194\t\n195\t#[cfg(test)]\n196\tmod tests;\n197\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/storybook-provider","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"44266afe-0b1d-4ff3-b550-74713eee4034","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/resolve_one_sided.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/resolve_one_sided.py","content":"\"\"\"Resolve conflict blocks where one side is empty by keeping the other; report files with two-sided blocks left.\"\"\"\nimport re, sys\n\nBLOCK = re.compile(r'<<<<<<< [^\\n]*\\n(.*?)=======\\n(.*?)>>>>>>> [^\\n]*\\n', re.S)\nfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n    text = open(path).read()\n    left = []\n\n    def keep(m):\n        ours, theirs = m.group(1), m.group(2)\n        if not ours.strip():\n            return theirs\n        if not theirs.strip():\n            return ours\n        left.append(m.group(0))\n        return m.group(0)\n\n    text = BLOCK.sub(keep, text)\n    open(path, 'w').write(text)\n    print(f'{path}: {\"resolved\" if not left else f\"{len(left)} two-sided block(s) left\"}')\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}},"displayPath":"../../../../../.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/resolve_one_sided.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3c66c89a-cc5d-477c-8f75-d7d1248d490b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:03:42.762Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/resolve_one_sided.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Resolve conflict blocks where one side is empty by keeping the other; report files with two-sided blocks left.\"\"\"\n2\timport re, sys\n3\t\n4\tBLOCK = re.compile(r'<<<<<<< [^\\n]*\\n(.*?)=======\\n(.*?)>>>>>>> [^\\n]*\\n', re.S)\n5\tfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n6\t    text = open(path).read()\n7\t    left = []\n8\t\n9\t    def keep(m):\n10\t        ours, theirs = m.group(1), m.group(2)\n11\t        if not ours.strip():\n12\t            return theirs\n13\t        if not theirs.strip():\n14\t            return ours\n15\t        left.append(m.group(0))\n16\t        return m.group(0)\n17\t\n18\t    text = BLOCK.sub(keep, text)\n19\t    open(path, 'w').write(text)\n20\t    print(f'{path}: {\"resolved\" if not left else f\"{len(left)} two-sided block(s) left\"}')\n21\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/storybook-provider","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"3c66c89a-cc5d-477c-8f75-d7d1248d490b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/STATUS.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/STATUS.md","content":"# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-10-22\n\nCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are fully tested. Config file loading, watch mode (including rebuilds on config changes and polling with `ensure_fresh`), plugin architecture, TOON token-optimized output format, JSON schema export, LSP server scaffold, and bounded atomic DTS caching are implemented and verified.\n\n**Types from other packages.** Imports resolve to any file under a source directory, `.d.ts` included, so a monorepo whose packages are all source directories resolves across them. By default, from `node_modules` only `@types/react` and TypeScript's own lib files are read, and a prop whose type comes from any other installed package stays a named reference with an `UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT` warning. `--load-dependencies` (config, NAPI and Vite `loadDependencies`) loads the declarations those names point to; it is off by default while its output is checked against RDT (ADR 0010).\n\n## Numbers\n\n- 745 Rust tests (729 workspace tests under `cargo nextest`, 16 NAPI binding tests) and 46 vitest (41 unit with a mocked binding, 5 integration against the real native binding), all green\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean with `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` enforced workspace-wide\n- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)\n- **Recall** against `react-docgen-typescript`, own props, five source-only mirrors with no dependencies installed (`docs/projects/architecture-roadmap.md`, after #69): components found Mantine 93%, Chakra 92%, Ant Design 97%, shadcn/ui 98%, react-spectrum 99%; share of RDT's props reported 92%, 85%, 95%, 94%, 97%.\n- **Precision** per detection rule (`docs/precision.md`, 2026-10-21): 1 component that isn't one in 154 sampled, `functionDeclaration` 96% and every other rule 100%. 25 samples per rule can't yet establish the 95% gate.\n- **Speed** on five pinned public corpora (`docs/performance.md`, 2026-10-22): 34 to 81 ms wall time and 66 to 153 MB peak RSS for 41 to 490 kLOC, 17 to 39 times faster than `react-docgen-typescript` on the same files. CI fails on a 10% regression against main or a ratio under 10×.\n\n## Features and improvements\n\n- **Testing Stack** — `cargo-nextest` process runner, `rstest` parameterized spec tables, `insta` snapshots, and `trycmd` executable Markdown CLI specs.\n- **Plugin system** (`DocgenPlugin` / `PluginRegistry`) — Extensible AST and component resolution hooks in `crates/core/src/plugin.rs`.\n- **TOON output format** (`--format toon` / `toon.rs`) — Token-optimized format for LLM agents, cutting context window token usage by ~65-75%.\n- **JSON schema export** (`caliper-docgen schema`) — Machine-readable Draft-07 JSON Schema export for component metadata validation.\n- **Atomic & Bounded DTS cache** (`cache.rs`) — Atomic temp-file swap writes, dirty flag tracking, and 5,000 entry eviction cap.\n- **LSP server scaffold** (`caliper-docgen lsp`) — bounded framing plus initialize/shutdown/exit lifecycle. It currently advertises `hoverProvider: false` and does not serve component prop hovers yet.\n- **Strict Safe Rust** — `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` via `[workspace.lints]`, active across all three crates (`core`, `cli`, `binding`) — none currently use `unsafe`, including the NAPI FFI boundary (napi-rs's `#[napi]` macros generate the glue without user-visible `unsafe`).\n\n## Known gaps that won't get fixed without a type checker\n\nSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all need real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs.\n\nAn opt-in TypeScript 7 semantic backend is designed (ADR 0006) but not implemented. Accuracy is verified against real RDT — 0 missing/extra props on 13 hand-picked components, and re-verified against the full 44-file fixture corpus (5,508/5,522 `required` matches, 5,265/5,522 type-string matches; the gap is explained noise, not a resolver bug) — and the RDT oracle that comparison depends on now runs on its own `typescript@6` install, separate from the semantic probe's `typescript@next`. Lifecycle (crash/restart/timeout handling for the `tsc --api` process) hasn't started; see `type-checker-integration.md`'s Gates table.\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- **Edge cases, failure modes, and gaps not yet fixed** → `edge-cases.md` — comprehensive audit of crash/hang risks, silent data loss, and silent correctness bugs across every subsystem, prioritized. Update it as findings get fixed or new ones turn up.\n- **Why those gaps happened, and the plan to fix them** → `root-cause-analysis.md` — the edge-case findings collapsed into 11 mechanism-level root causes with concrete fix proposals, plus a Phase 1 task breakdown.\n- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.\n- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, panic containment, the TypeScript 7 semantic backend. Write a new one when you make a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`).\n- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/architecture/` for per-subsystem invariants and known gaps (moved from `.claude/semantic-model/` so every coding agent can read it, not just Claude Code — `AGENTS.md` is now this repo's shared instructions file, with per-tool mirrors under `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, `.gemini/`, `.github/`, `.opencode/`).\n- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`\n- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** → `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}},"displayPath":"docs/STATUS.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4ec5a379-57f5-42d0-b56a-ed2397aef445","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:03:42.762Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/STATUS.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# Status\n2\t\n3\t**Updated:** 2026-10-22\n4\t\n5\tCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are fully tested. Config file loading, watch mode (including rebuilds on config changes and polling with `ensure_fresh`), plugin architecture, TOON token-optimized output format, JSON schema export, LSP server scaffold, and bounded atomic DTS caching are implemented and verified.\n6\t\n7\t**Types from other packages.** Imports resolve to any file under a source directory, `.d.ts` included, so a monorepo whose packages are all source directories resolves across them. By default, from `node_modules` only `@types/react` and TypeScript's own lib files are read, and a prop whose type comes from any other installed package stays a named reference with an `UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT` warning. `--load-dependencies` (config, NAPI and Vite `loadDependencies`) loads the declarations those names point to; it is off by default while its output is checked against RDT (ADR 0010).\n8\t\n9\t## Numbers\n10\t\n11\t- 745 Rust tests (729 workspace tests under `cargo nextest`, 16 NAPI binding tests) and 46 vitest (41 unit with a mocked binding, 5 integration against the real native binding), all green\n12\t- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean with `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` enforced workspace-wide\n13\t- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)\n14\t- **Recall** against `react-docgen-typescript`, own props, five source-only mirrors with no dependencies installed (`docs/projects/architecture-roadmap.md`, after #69): components found Mantine 93%, Chakra 92%, Ant Design 97%, shadcn/ui 98%, react-spectrum 99%; share of RDT's props reported 92%, 85%, 95%, 94%, 97%.\n15\t- **Precision** per detection rule (`docs/precision.md`, 2026-10-21): 1 component that isn't one in 154 sampled, `functionDeclaration` 96% and every other rule 100%. 25 samples per rule can't yet establish the 95% gate.\n16\t- **Speed** on five pinned public corpora (`docs/performance.md`, 2026-10-22): 34 to 81 ms wall time and 66 to 153 MB peak RSS for 41 to 490 kLOC, 17 to 39 times faster than `react-docgen-typescript` on the same files. CI fails on a 10% regression against main or a ratio under 10×.\n17\t\n18\t## Features and improvements\n19\t\n20\t- **Testing Stack** — `cargo-nextest` process runner, `rstest` parameterized spec tables, `insta` snapshots, and `trycmd` executable Markdown CLI specs.\n21\t- **Plugin system** (`DocgenPlugin` / `PluginRegistry`) — Extensible AST and component resolution hooks in `crates/core/src/plugin.rs`.\n22\t- **TOON output format** (`--format toon` / `toon.rs`) — Token-optimized format for LLM agents, cutting context window token usage by ~65-75%.\n23\t- **JSON schema export** (`caliper-docgen schema`) — Machine-readable Draft-07 JSON Schema export for component metadata validation.\n24\t- **Atomic & Bounded DTS cache** (`cache.rs`) — Atomic temp-file swap writes, dirty flag tracking, and 5,000 entry eviction cap.\n25\t- **LSP server scaffold** (`caliper-docgen lsp`) — bounded framing plus initialize/shutdown/exit lifecycle. It currently advertises `hoverProvider: false` and does not serve component prop hovers yet.\n26\t- **Strict Safe Rust** — `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` via `[workspace.lints]`, active across all three crates (`core`, `cli`, `binding`) — none currently use `unsafe`, including the NAPI FFI boundary (napi-rs's `#[napi]` macros generate the glue without user-visible `unsafe`).\n27\t\n28\t## Known gaps that won't get fixed without a type checker\n29\t\n30\tSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all need real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs.\n31\t\n32\tAn opt-in TypeScript 7 semantic backend is designed (ADR 0006) but not implemented. Accuracy is verified against real RDT — 0 missing/extra props on 13 hand-picked components, and re-verified against the full 44-file fixture corpus (5,508/5,522 `required` matches, 5,265/5,522 type-string matches; the gap is explained noise, not a resolver bug) — and the RDT oracle that comparison depends on now runs on its own `typescript@6` install, separate from the semantic probe's `typescript@next`. Lifecycle (crash/restart/timeout handling for the `tsc --api` process) hasn't started; see `type-checker-integration.md`'s Gates table.\n33\t\n34\t## Where to look next\n35\t\n36\t- **Edge cases, failure modes, and gaps not yet fixed** → `edge-cases.md` — comprehensive audit of crash/hang risks, silent data loss, and silent correctness bugs across every subsystem, prioritized. Update it as findings get fixed or new ones turn up.\n37\t- **Why those gaps happened, and the plan to fix them** → `root-cause-analysis.md` — the edge-case findings collapsed into 11 mechanism-level root causes with concrete fix proposals, plus a Phase 1 task breakdown.\n38\t- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.\n39\t- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, panic containment, the TypeScript 7 semantic backend. Write a new one when you make a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`).\n40\t- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/architecture/` for per-subsystem invariants and known gaps (moved from `.claude/semantic-model/` so every coding agent can read it, not just Claude Code — `AGENTS.md` is now this repo's shared instructions file, with per-tool mirrors under `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, `.gemini/`, `.github/`, `.opencode/`).\n41\t- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n42\t- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`\n43\t- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** → `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference\n44\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/storybook-provider","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
