{"parentUuid":"0f66c964-f21f-49f5-994d-dee2b3f0116b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01FfwiSN6gqH3dHDDQYtNG9C","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk grep -n -B3 -A30 '^<<<<<<<' packages/vite-plugin/README.md packages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts packages/vite-plugin/tests/unit/plugin.test.ts | head -300\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":22},"type":"attachment","uuid":"64ab057a-258c-4fcc-8c7b-03cec07a04da","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:06:31.846Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/storybook-vite-docgen","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"0f66c964-f21f-49f5-994d-dee2b3f0116b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb563e85-80fa-4200-bf18-7a747f7a254b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FfwiSN6gqH3dHDDQYtNG9C","type":"tool_result","content":"packages/vite-plugin/README.md-37-)\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-38-```\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-39-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md:40:<<<<<<< HEAD\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-41-## Storybook without the docgen server\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-42-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-43-On Storybook 10, or Storybook 11 with `features.docgenServer: false`, Storybook reads each component's `__docgenInfo`. With `injectDocgenInfo`, the plugin assigns it from the session, in react-docgen-typescript's shape, and an edit re-transforms every module whose components it changed. Turn off Storybook's own docgen plugin so it doesn't overwrite the assignments:\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-44-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-45-```ts\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-46-// .storybook/main.ts\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-47-import type { StorybookConfig } from '@storybook/react-vite'\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-48-import { caliperDocgen } from 'caliper-docgen-vite-plugin'\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-49-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-50-const config: StorybookConfig = {\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-51-  framework: '@storybook/react-vite',\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-52-  stories: ['../src/**/*.stories.tsx'],\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-53-  typescript: { reactDocgen: false },\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-54-  viteFinal: (config) => ({\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-55-    ...config,\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-56-    plugins: [...(config.plugins ?? []), caliperDocgen({ srcDirs: ['src'], injectDocgenInfo: true })],\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-57-  }),\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-58-}\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-59-export default config\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-60-```\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-61-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-62-Each assignment sits in a `try`, so a component the module can't reach by name (an anonymous default export) keeps no docs instead of failing. On Storybook 11 with the docgen server on, use `caliper-docgen-storybook` instead.\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-63-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-64-In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs` triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-65-=======\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-66-A change to a tsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above `srcDirs` (installing a package, editing `paths`) re-extracts everything and arrives as an ordinary update event.\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-67-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-68-Pass `loadDependencies: true` to resolve the types your props import from installed packages; by default they stay named references.\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-69-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-70-In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs`, or to that configuration, triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n--\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-13-  srcDirs: string[]\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-14-  exclude?: string[]\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-15-  skipHtmlProps?: boolean\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts:16:<<<<<<< HEAD\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-17-  /** Assign each component its react-docgen-typescript docs as `__docgenInfo`, for Storybook without a docgen server. */\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-18-  injectDocgenInfo?: boolean\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-19-=======\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-20-  /** Load the type declarations your props reference from installed packages. Off by default. */\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-21-  loadDependencies?: boolean\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-22-  /**\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-23-   * Which inherited sources of more than 30 props to list as one inherited layer instead of prop by prop: those from\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-24-   * loaded dependencies (the default), every inherited source, or none.\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-25-   */\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-26-  collapseInheritedProps?: 'dependencies' | 'all' | 'none'\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-27->>>>>>> feat/storybook-provider\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-28-}\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-29-\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-30-/**\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-31- * What `caliper-docgen:update` carries to the client. Events arrive in `revision` order; each is a delta from the one\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-32- * before. Delete `removedKeys`, set `updatedKeys[i]` to `updatedComponents[i]`, merge `props` into the output's\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-33- * `props`, drop `removedDiagnostics` and add `diagnostics`, and the client holds the same output the virtual module\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-34- * serves, less any props no component refers to any more.\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-35- */\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-36-export interface CaliperDocgenUpdate {\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-37-  file: string\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-38-  revision: number\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-39-  updatedKeys: string[]\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-40-  updatedComponents: IncrementalUpdate['updatedComponents']\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-41-  /** Every prop `updatedComponents` refer to, by id. */\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-42-  props: IncrementalUpdate['props']\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-43-  removedKeys: string[]\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-44-  /** Diagnostics this revision added. */\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-45-  diagnostics: IncrementalUpdate['diagnostics']\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-46-  /** Diagnostics this revision 