-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-50-const config: StorybookConfig = {\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-51-  framework: '@storybook/react-vite',\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-52-  stories: ['../src/**/*.stories.tsx'],\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-53-  typescript: { reactDocgen: false },\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-54-  viteFinal: (config) => ({\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-55-    ...config,\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-56-    plugins: [...(config.plugins ?? []), caliperDocgen({ srcDirs: ['src'], injectDocgenInfo: true })],\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-57-  }),\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-58-}\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-59-export default config\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-60-```\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-61-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-62-Each assignment sits in a `try`, so a component the module can't reach by name (an anonymous default export) keeps no docs instead of failing. On Storybook 11 with the docgen server on, use `caliper-docgen-storybook` instead.\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-63-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-64-In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs` triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-65-=======\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-66-A change to a tsconfig, `package.json` or lockfile in or above `srcDirs` (installing a package, editing `paths`) re-extracts everything and arrives as an ordinary update event.\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-67-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-68-Pass `loadDependencies: true` to resolve the types your props import from installed packages; by default they stay named references.\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-69-\npackages/vite-plugin/README.md-70-In `vite build --watch`, a change to any file under `srcDirs`, or to that configuration, triggers a rebuild, even one no bundle module imports. A build fails if extraction fails.\n--\npackages/vite-plugin/src/index.ts-13-  srcDirs: s