{"parentUuid":"d5ce699e-b3a5-465b-8844-db1701348d98","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb563e85-80fa-4200-bf18-7a747f7a254b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vr4rGrV3Fi8mwDeHbuGYxf","type":"tool_result","content":"crates/cli/src/main.rs:100:    /// Keep components their module doesn't export in `--format rdt` and `--format storybook`, which omit them by\ncrates/cli/src/commands/extract/tests.rs:423:fn docgen_info_keeps_undocumented_children_for_storybook() {\ndocs/architecture/serialization-formats.md:19:RDT and Storybook output hold only components with `exported: true`, unless `--include-unexported` is passed. react-docgen-typescript documents only a module's exports, so a file-local helper component would otherwise appear in RDT-shaped output where RDT never puts one.\ndocs/architecture/serialization-formats.md:21:Each RDT component carries `filePath`, the absolute path of its source file, as RDT's `ComponentDoc` does. Storybook format leaves it out.\ndocs/architecture/serialization-formats.md:82:### `methods: []` — always empty, and why RDT/Storybook both still carry the field\ndocs/architecture/cli-commands.md:63:**`extract --json` intentionally ignores `--out`/`--format`.** `ExtractArgs::json`'s doc comment (`main.rs:103-107`) states this precisely: `--json` is \"the canonical schema, compact, always to stdout, ignoring --out/--format (which govern the human/RDT/Storybook paths below), and suppresses the human-readable summary/diagnostics.\" This is a deliberate two-mode split (machine-readable canonical vs. human/RDT/Storybook-formatted), not an oversight where `--json --out foo.json` should have written to the file — it never will, by design.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7e45d909-039b-4d0c-ac3c-2f5f46e77a4c","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:08:10.075Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"crates/cli/src/main.rs:100:    /// Keep components their module doesn't export in `--format rdt` and `--format storybook`, which omit them by\ncrates/cli/src/commands/extract/tests.rs:423:fn docgen_info_keeps_undocumented_children_for_storybook() {\ndocs/architecture/serialization-formats.md:19:RDT and Storybook output hold only components with `exported: true`, unless `--include-unexported` is passed. react-docgen-typescript documents only a module's exports, so a file-local helper component would otherwise appear in RDT-shaped output where RDT never puts one.\ndocs/architecture/serialization-formats.md:21:Each RDT component carries `filePath`, the absolute path of its source file, as RDT's `ComponentDoc` does. Storybook format leaves it out.\ndocs/architecture/serialization-formats.md:82:### `methods: []` — always empty, and why RDT/Storybook both still carry the field\ndocs/architecture/cli-commands.md:63:**`extract --json` intentionally ignores `--out`/`--format`.** `ExtractArgs::json`'s doc comment (`main.rs:103-107`) states this precisely: `--json` is \"the canonical schema, compact, always to stdout, ignoring --out/--format (which govern the human/RDT/Storybook paths below), and suppresses the human-readable summary/diagnostics.\" This is a deliberate two-mode split (machine-readable canonical vs. human/RDT/Storybook-formatted), not an oversight where `--json --out foo.json` should have written to the file — it never will, by design.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"81493357-34c6-441b-a9b5-00c2b0806b8d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"chore/remove-storybook-format","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":128,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d5ce699e-b3a5-465b-8844-db1701348d98","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/remove-storybook-format","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
