{"parentUuid":"ec4b8361-289c-492f-b4c8-c7c1d25351db","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKY5jBQmjY3pQZJNqYHo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UDEorc3PfVZy4aVjX9k7Ug","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/serialization-formats.md","offset":76,"limit":12},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2093,"cache_read_input_tokens":146751,"output_tokens":401,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":95},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2093,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":401,"cache_read_input_tokens":146751,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2093,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2093},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UDEorc3PfVZy4aVjX9k7Ug":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/serialization-formats.md","offset":76,"limit":12}},"serverClassifierRequest":"cfe155c9-89c6-4be7-9cea-531ff7628842","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgKY5is3s3DWF4y96wd6F","requestRef":"8561a1b6-82eb-4757-95fd-e2ac9899644d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"86368027-13ff-4522-afe7-9bd129fb2fe1","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:08:13.785Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/remove-storybook-format","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"86368027-13ff-4522-afe7-9bd129fb2fe1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb563e85-80fa-4200-bf18-7a747f7a254b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UDEorc3PfVZy4aVjX9k7Ug","type":"tool_result","content":"76\t### `ref`/`key`: deliberate omission, not a bug, not relocated\n77\t\n78\tRDT lists React's `ref` and `key` reconciliation props alongside a component's real props. This tool does not. `docs/benchmarks.md` documents this precisely: of components with any prop-count mismatch against real RDT, \"the other 24 (0.9%, spread across 12 of the other 23 components) are **100% `ref`/`key`**... Worth being precise about that one: it's an omission, not a relocation — this tool doesn't surface forwardRef/ref-type metadata anywhere else either (checked `ComponentEntry`'s full field list — no such field exists), so 'we chose not to add it' is accurate, but 'the same info lives elsewhere' isn't.\"\n79\t\n80\t**Invariant 5:** Neither `ref` nor `key` appears in `props`, in any other `ComponentEntry` field, or in any of the serialization formats in this document. If a future change adds `ref`-as-prop support (React 19's `function Button({ ref, ...props })` pattern — see `docs/rdt-coverage.md`'s \"React 19 `ref`-as-prop\" note, already investigated and found to already work structurally when `ref` is an explicit member of the props type), that is a change to what the _resolver_ extracts, not a serialization-format decision — this document's job is only to record that today, none of the formats invent `ref`/`key` entries that the canonical `ExtractionOutput` doesn't already contain.\n81\t\n82\t### `methods: []` — always empty, and why RDT/Storybook both still carry the field\n83\t\n84\t**Locked design decision:** `rdt::docgen_info` hardcodes `\"methods\": []` unconditionally rather than omitting the field or computing it. This tool does not extract class component methods — \"this tool doesn't extract class methods, and RDT consumers (Storybook's docgen addon) only ever read it for class components\". Since class components are explicitly out of scope for this project (`docs/rdt-coverage.md`'s Component patterns table: `Class component | ❌ | out of scope (modern React only)`), the field is kept present-but-empty rather than dropped, because RDT/Storybook consumers may assume the key always exists on a valid RDT-shaped component entry — dropping it risks a `TypeError` on `.methods.length` in a consumer that doesn't defensively check for the key's presence, whereas an empty array is always safe to iterate.\n85\t\n86\t## TOON format (`crates/core/src/toon.rs`)\n87\t"}]},"uuid":"99727698-85f7-450b-bf4e-125c0b2a46e0","timestamp":"2026-10-23T17:08:13.855Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/serialization-formats.md","content":"### `ref`/`key`: deliberate omission, not a bug, not relocated\n\nRDT lists React's `ref` and `key` reconciliation props alongside a component's real props. This tool does not. `docs/benchmarks.md` documents this precisely: of components with any prop-count mismatch against real RDT, \"the other 24 (0.9%, spread across 12 of the other 23 components) are **100% `ref`/`key`**... Worth being precise about that one: it's an omission, not a relocation — this tool doesn't surface forwardRef/ref-type metadata anywhere else either (checked `ComponentEntry`'s full field list — no such field exists), so 'we chose not to add it' is accurate, but 'the same info lives elsewhere' isn't.\"\n\n**Invariant 5:** Neither `ref` nor `key` appears in `props`, in any other `ComponentEntry` field, or in any of the serialization formats in this document. If a future change adds `ref`-as-prop support (React 19's `function Button({ ref, ...props })` pattern — see `docs/rdt-coverage.md`'s \"React 19 `ref`-as-prop\" note, already investigated and found to already work structurally when `ref` is an explicit member of the props type), that is a change to what the _resolver_ extracts, not a serialization-format decision — this document's job is only to record that today, none of the formats invent `ref`/`key` entries that the canonical `ExtractionOutput` doesn't already contain.\n\n### `methods: []` — always empty, and why RDT/Storybook both still carry the field\n\n**Locked design decision:** `rdt::docgen_info` hardcodes `\"methods\": []` unconditionally rather than omitting the field or computing it. This tool does not extract class component methods — \"this tool doesn't extract class methods, and RDT consumers (Storybook's docgen addon) only ever read it for class components\". Since class components are explicitly out of scope for this project (`docs/rdt-coverage.md`'s Component patterns table: `Class component | ❌ | out of scope (modern React only)`), the field is kept present-but-empty rather than dropped, because RDT/Storybook consumers may assume the key always exists on a valid RDT-shaped component entry — dropping it risks a `TypeError` on `.methods.length` in a consumer that doesn't defensively check for the key's presence, whereas an empty array is always safe to iterate.\n\n## TOON format (`crates/core/src/toon.rs`)\n","numLines":12,"startLine":76,"totalLines":166}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"86368027-13ff-4522-afe7-9bd129fb2fe1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"chore/remove-storybook-format","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
