{"parentUuid":"a894aa3e-5a99-4a41-aced-4c76462f31a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKickNsHofj4jcocArT5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Next is merging the stack: all 27 PRs are green and waiting on you. After that, I'd work on recognizing components created through wrapper functions, which is now the biggest accuracy gap.\n\n**1. Merge the stack and release**\n- Merge from the bottom up, starting at #98 and ending at #120. When a PR merges, its child has to be retargeted to `main` before the parent's branch is deleted, or GitHub closes the child. I can do the retargeting as you go.\n- Then cut 0.4.0 with the changesets that have built up.\n\n**2. Components created through wrapper functions (recommended next feature)**\n- Compared with react-docgen-typescript, caliper finds only 29% of Mantine's components and 9% of Chakra's.\n- About 72% of the misses look like `const Button = factory<ButtonFactory>(...)` or Chakra's `withContext<El, Props>(...)`, where the props come from a type argument.\n- Recognizing that pattern generally, without hardcoding library names, is the largest recall gain available and matters most for Storybook users of those libraries.\n- It also covers task #7 (replace name-based special cases with structural rules).\n- The earlier research gives a starting point. I'd write an ADR, then stack 2–3 PRs, each measured against the 5-project benchmark.\n\n**3. Decisions waiting on you**\n\n| Decision | My default |\n|---|---|\n| Should `--load-dependencies` become the default? | Yes, once it's checked against react-docgen-typescript on the 20 fixture libraries, in 0.5.0 |\n| Should project sources with more than 30 inherited props collapse, as Chakra-style libraries would need? | No; keep `dependencies` as the default |\n| Amend ADR 0010 so curated mode loads React's attribute declarations (the event-handler merge)? | Yes |\n| Quote style for string defaults: `'md'` or `\"md\"`? | Keep the source's quotes, as react-docgen-typescript does |\n\n**4. Small cleanup**\n- `a_signal_restores_the_terminal_mode_the_session_changed` still fails on macOS under parallel test load. It's a timing problem in the test, about 30 minutes to fix.\n- The branch-deletion command from my last message is still pending.\n\nTell me to start on #2, or answer any of the decisions in #3."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":282626,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1071,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":300},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":282626,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1071,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":282626,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":282626},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}},"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d0827c15-bf93-420e-a1f1-501922023055","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgKicjz4Fx8bVLqZTgUBS","requestRef":"20700277-1b54-464e-ace9-2b8f723e6751","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bb41a06f-a42d-473d-86b8-6461f1079b69","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:26:31.175Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"scratch/watch-idl