{"parentUuid":"c6a4627d-fb43-449c-8978-8c8856b8b7ac","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MnBjz7uMn5dhpFSB4VQpoj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Research report: detecting and resolving wrapper-declared React components\n2\t\n3\tQuestion: how should caliper-docgen detect and resolve components declared through wrapper calls, without hardcoding library names, while preserving the architecture, the semantic models and the TS 7.1 semantic backend (ADR 0006)? Confidence: medium. Sources: four reader reports (architecture docs, code, real library shapes, prior art) and the five-project benchmark. Every claim below is \"confirmed\" unless marked (inferred) or (assumed).\n4\t\n5\t## 1. Recommendation\n6\t\n7\tDetect by declaration shape, in layers. No library names except React builtins.\n8\t\n9\t1. **Extractor** (`visit.rs:229-234`, owned records only, no AST escapes, no cross-file knowledge): add a typed-arrow and function-expression detector, generalize `try_hoc_wrapped` to the first function-valued argument at any position, and record a new owned `WrapperCall` candidate for PascalCase bindings initialized by a call with type arguments or an untyped callback.\n10\t2. **Pipeline promotion pass** after merge (cross-file, per item inside `contain_panic`): tier 1 resolves the callee declaration (aliases, imports, barrels, destructure-from-call) and reads where its type parameters flow into the props position, which gives the type-argument index and payload-versus-props without any name. Tier 2 (no callee declaration) picks the type argument that resolves to a source object type, low confidence. Tier 3 emits nothing and keeps the Info `SkippedCandidate`.\n11\t3. **Resolver fixes** so detected components carry props: accept indexed access as a props base (`resolver/alias.rs:245`), select members from object-literal type arguments, substitute generic interface type arguments (`chain.rs:201`), fix multi-hop barrels after a minimal repro, defer identifier-alias renames to `finish()`.\n12\t4. **Provenance:** a new `non_exhaustive` `DiagnosticCode` (for example `InferredComponent`), Info severity, with line, column and the rule used. No `ComponentEntry` field (it has no schema version). A new `SourceData` or `ComponentMapping` field forces `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` 4 to 5.\n13\t5. **Escape hatch:** a `/** @component */` leading comment first (syntax-only, no options plumbing, react-docgen precedent). A declarative `docgen.config.ts` list only if wanted, since `parse_file(path, source)` takes no options today.\n14\t6. **Semantic backend:** write ADR 0007 allowing the opt-in `tsc --api` backend to discover components (RDT's call-signature rule), handle opaque factories and generics, and keep structural as default and fallback.\n15\t\n16\tFalsifiable claim (inferred from miss counts, not measured): after stages 0 to 3, component recall against RDT's plausible set reaches Mantine at least 85% and Chakra at least 80%, with no regression elsewhere and under 5% of newly emitted components outside RDT's set. If new-emission false positives exceed 5%, or Mantine prop recall stays under 30% after stage 3, the type-shape heuristic is refuted and callee-signature resolution or the checker becomes mandatory.\n17\t\n18\t## 2. Baseline\n19\t\n20\t| Project | RDT components with own props | Caliper found | Component recall | Prop recall |\n21\t| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n22\t| mantine | 354 | 103 | 29% | 2% |\n23\t| chakra | 484 | 47 | 9% | 13% |\n24\t| antd | 149 | 132 | 88% | 81% |\n25\t| shadcn | 323 | 317 | 98% | 93% |\n26\t| spectrum | 962 | 947 | 98% | 97% |\n27\t\n28\tCaliper runs in 30 to 141ms and 34 to 78MB, against 0.5 to 2s and 300 to 590MB for react-docgen and react-docgen-typescript (10 to 37 times faster).\n29\t\n30\t## 3. Declaration shapes\n31\t\n32\tLayer: E = extractor, R = pipeline or resolver, S = semantic backend.\n33\t\n34\t| Shape | Props come from | Counts | Layer |\n35\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n36\t| `const X = (props: P) => …` plain typed arrow | first parameter annotation | 29 misses (chakra 16, spectrum 7, antd 3, mantine 2, shadcn 1), all genuine | E |\n37\t| `factory`/`polymorphicFactory`/`genericFactory<F>` (Mantine) | `props` member of the payload object at type argument 0 | 184, 26, 14; found 0 | E records, R selects |\n38\t| `withContext`/`withProvider<El, P>` (Chakra) | type argument 1 | 391, 73; found 8 and 1, with empty props | E records, R chooses index |\n39\t| `withRootProvider<P>` (Chakra) | type argument 0 | 16; found 0 | E records, R |\n40\t| `tableElement<F>('th')` | type argument 0, wraps `factory` | 7; found 0 | E and R |\n41\t| react-aria `createLeafComponent`/`createBranchComponent` | typed first parameter of the function at argument 1 | 32; found 0 | E |\n42\t| `createHideableComponent` | typed first parameter at argument 0 | 14; found 14 | works |\n43\t| Opaque factories: `createEdgeComponent`, tiptap `createControl`, `createIconLoader(\"x\")`, antd `generator`/`genPurePanel` | callee body only | about 60 | S |\n44\t| Aliased callee: `polymorphic = createPolymorphicComponent` | type argument 1 | 1 | R follows alias |\n45\t| Callee destructured from another call: Chakra `const { withContext } = createSlotRecipeContext(…)` | the returned object's signature | 74 files | E records, R/S follow |\n46\t| `chakra(\"div\", { recipe })` | overloads and `HTMLChakraProps<T, P>` | 20; found 0 | S |\n47\t| Generators with non-props type argument: `generateCalendar<Dayjs>` | not the type argument (a trap) | 2 to 3 | S |\n48\t| `lazy`, `dynamic` | the target module | 8 spectrum, 13 shadcn | out of scope |\n49\t| Static member assignments, re-export barrels, filename-mangled names | an existing component under another name | the 67 \"no declaration\" rows are RDT naming artifacts, not misses | none |\n50\t| `export default function _3D(…)` | typed parameter | 6 rows, likely fails the PascalCase test (not traced) | small E |\n51\t\n52\tFalse positives the guard must reject: the `createContext` family (427 across the corpora: spectrum 311, antd 51, shadcn 36, mantine 29), array-destructured providers (47), `withPropsProvider` (returns a Provider), SCREAMING_CASE constants (about 30), `Styled*` helpers, 79 lowercase `style<T>` macros, and hooks and string helpers that RDT counts as components.\n53\t\n54\t## 4. Root causes beyond detection\n55\t\n56\t| Cause | Evidence | Structurally fixable? |\n57\t| --- | --- | --- |\n58\t| RC1: indexed access rejected as a props base | `alias.rs:245`; repro gives 0 props plus a warning | Yes, for source-defined bases |\n59\t| RC2: no member selection from an object-literal type argument | `extractor/mod.rs:426-433` stringifies it | Yes |\n60\t| RC3: generic interface type arguments ignored | `chain.rs:199-207` | Yes |\n61\t| RC4: multi-hop barrels fail though single-hop is implemented and tested | mantine `core/index.ts` 51 of 79 unresolved; chakra `styled-system/index.ts` 24 | Probably; cause unestablished, needs a repro |\n62\t| RC5: `HTMLChakraProps<T, P>` second argument not expanded | inferred from the dump | Yes, via a `known.rs` arm (still a library shortcut) |\n63\t| RC6: `ElementProps<'input', …>` helper | `Box.tsx:54-57` | Partly |\n64\t| RC7: identifier-alias detection depends on source order | `component.rs:458-481` | Yes |\n65\t| RC8: no detection in plain `.ts` files | `extractor/mod.rs:140` | Policy |\n66\t\n67\t## 5. Constraints that shape the design\n68\t\n69\t- The extractor is per-file with no cross-file knowledge, so callee-signature lookup cannot live there. It must produce an owned candidate record resolved later.\n70\t- Detection is a first-match-wins chain. `SkippedCandidate` (Info) is the deliberate fallback, but it discards the span, so it has no line or column today.\n71\t- ADR 0006 never says whether the semantic backend may discover components. Changing an ADR needs a new ADR.\n72\t- Nothing can register plugins from the CLI or binding, and plugins cannot see the AST.\n73\t- ADR 0006's backend is designed, not implemented. `crates/tsc-client` is not wired into core, the CLI or NAPI.\n74\t- Watch mode builds `ReverseDeps` once per session, so a promotion that depends on a callee in another file can go stale.\n75\t\n76\t## 6. Prior art\n77\t\n78\t- **react-docgen:** syntactic. Unknown calls go through `resolveHOC`, which looks at the first argument (or the last if the first is a literal). It never reads type arguments, so it cannot read Mantine's `Payload['props']`. `@component` is its escape hatch. Storybook defaults to it (\"much faster but incomplete\").\n79\t- **react-docgen-typescript:** the checker, with no library names and no return-type test. A component is an exported symbol whose call signature has a first parameter named `props` or is the sole parameter. It is dormant (last commit 2025-06-10) and crashes on TypeScript 7 (styleguidist/react-docgen-typescript#538).\n80\t- **Mantine's own docs** run RDT over a hand-listed set of files with manual type-string rewrites.\n81\t- **Implication:** the checker is the only name-free detector for opaque factories, and syntax can cover the type-argument and function-argument cases.\n82\t\n83\t## 7. Contradictions\n84\t\n85\t1. `accuracy.md` (mantine 11%, antd 53%) versus `recall2.py` (29%, 88%): a methodology difference. Use `recall2.py`.\n86\t2. Barrel following is implemented and tested, yet multi-hop barrels fail in the dumps. Unresolved.\n87\t3. `STATUS.md` says the semantic lifecycle \"hasn't started\"; `docs/type-checker-integration.md` says the Rust client exists.\n88\t4. `extractor-ast-visiting.md` is stale against `edge-cases.md`.\n89\t5. `edge-cases.md` says shape gaps are closed, yet plain arrows are missed entirely.\n90\t6. The docs say `typescript/unstable/*`; the installed 7.1 nightly exports `./sync ./async ./proto ./ast/*`. Re-probe 7.1.0-beta.\n91\t7. The task framing said RDT tests `JSX.Element`; its code does not.\n92\t8. Confirmed facts say the checker is exact but opt-in, costly and unshipped; assumed facts say cheap syntactic heuristics suffice. Not resolved by picking a side. The plan is layered and measurement decides.\n93\t\n94\t## 8. Tests and CI\n95\t\n96\t1. One minimal fixture per shape, plus each false positive, with `assert_eq!` on exact prop sets and the exact Info diagnostic. Negative fixtures assert zero components.\n97\t2. A CI harness from `recall2.py`, `accuracy.py`, `final.py` and `patterns.py`, with per-shape classification and thresholds (assumed): no per-project regression, Mantine at least 85%, Chakra at least 80%, new-emission precision at least 95%, wall time within +25%.\n98\t3. Sibling-path parity: `extract()`, `WatchSession::update_file` and `create_session` give identical components, props and diagnostics, including after editing a callee file.\n99\t4. Determinism: repeat and reversed file order give byte-identical output.\n100\t5. Source-only versus dependencies-installed runs.\n101\t6. A cache version bump invalidates old `.d.ts` entries.\n102\t7. The promotion pass runs inside `contain_panic` per item.\n103\t8. Semantic stage: extend the RDT-oracle gate to checker-discovered components.\n104\t\n105\t## 9. Staged plan (sizes and recall movement are inference)\n106\t\n107\t| Stage | Scope | Depends on | Size | Expected movement |\n108\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n109\t| 0 | Harness, fixtures, skip span, barrel repro | none | S to M | measurement |\n110\t| 1 | Typed arrow, source-order fix | 0 | S | +29 components |\n111\t| 2 | Function argument at any position, `@component`, provenance diagnostic | 0 | S | up to 32 (spectrum) |\n112\t| 3 | `WrapperCall`, promotion tier 2, RC1 to RC4, builtin deny list, cache v5 | 0, 1 | L | detection upper bound: mantine about 92%, chakra about 89%; props lag unless RC1 to RC4 land |\n113\t| 4 | Callee-signature tier 1, RC5, RC6 | 3 | M to L | precision, Chakra props |\n114\t| 5 | Optional config list | 3 | M | long tail |\n115\t| 6 | ADR 0007 and semantic discovery | ADR, 7.1 beta re-probe, tsc-client wiring | L | about 60 opaque factories, exact types |\n116\t\n117\tRisks: tier-2 false positives (the `createContext` family); detection without RC1 to RC4 yields components with empty props; a one-time `.d.ts` cache miss; stale `ReverseDeps` in watch; Chakra's destructure-from-call callees may push tier 1 to the checker.\n118\t\n119\t## 10. Decide before speccing\n120\t\n121\t- D1: may tier 2 emit by default, or only with callee-signature confirmation or `@component`?\n122\t- D2: is a declarative config list needed, or is `@component` enough?\n123\t- D3: may the semantic backend discover components (ADR 0007), and is wiring `tsc-client` into core in scope?\n124\t- D4: provenance in `ComponentEntry` JSON, or an Info diagnostic only?\n125\t- D5: acceptance thresholds for component recall, prop recall and new-emission precision.\n126\t- D6: parity target: plausible components (`recall2`) or every RDT entry (`accuracy.md`)?\n127\t- D7: plain `.ts` files and underscore-leading names?\n128\t\n129\t## 11. Risk review (vanguard:risk-assessor; overall risk: high; confidence in ranking: medium)\n130\t\n131\t| # | Risk | Severity / likelihood | Mitigation |\n132\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n133\t| 1 | Tier-2 type-shape heuristic matches the `createContext` family (427 sites), array-destructured providers, `withPropsProvider`, hooks. A name deny list conflicts with \"shapes, not names\" and misses user-land re-exports | critical / high | Tier 2 emits nothing by default. Emit only with callee-signature confirmation, `@component`, or an opt-in flag. Structural discriminators: function-valued callee parameter, component-like return, reject `null`/literal first arguments. Per-family precision, one negative fixture per family |\n134\t| 2 | Detection lands before the prop fixes: components with empty or wrong props (Mantine prop recall 2%; 8 Chakra hits already have empty props). `Factory<P> = P` needs RC3 before RC2 can select `props` | high / high | Order: RC4 repro, RC3, RC2, RC1, then detection. Unresolved props type gives an Info diagnostic and no entry, or a low-confidence entry |\n135\t| 3 | Stage 3 is too large to attribute regressions | high / medium | Split: 3a resolver fixes (valuable on existing components), 3b `WrapperCall` plus tier 1, 3c tier 2 behind a flag. Chakra destructure-from-call (74 files) may move to the checker |\n136\t| 4 | Watch mode: a callee edit or barrel hop doesn't update dependents because `ReverseDeps` has no callee-signature edge; `update_file` can diverge from `extract()` | high / high | Record callee and barrel-hop edges; parity tests including callee-only edits; or re-run promotion globally per update if cheap |\n137\t| 5 | Cache and determinism: a new `DiagnosticCode` variant or `SourceData` field shifts positional msgpack encoding (the enum-index claim is from the ADR, not verified); unordered promotion changes winners and `ComponentKeyCollision` | high / medium | Append fields and variants last; bump `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` in the same commit; test that a v4 blob is rejected; sort candidates by (path, span); define collision precedence |\n138\t| 6 | Output regression for users: hundreds of new components, some wrong, indistinguishable because provenance is only an Info diagnostic (D4); snapshots change; any Warning flips `check --strict` | medium / high | Info only; decide D4 first; hand-review each snapshot diff; changeset note; flag for tier 2 |\n139\t| 7 | Layering: promotion needs resolver machinery (chained wrappers like `tableElement`), tempting a reverse dependency | medium / medium | Pure function (GlobalSourceData, WrapperCall list) to candidates, run before resolution; depth limit; extractor records everything promotion needs; document the direction |\n140\t| 8 | Performance: a cross-file lookup per PascalCase call binding; repeated failed barrel walks | medium / medium | Memoise per (file, symbol); cheap prefilter; bound barrel depth; absolute per-project time budget (about 15ms or 20%) plus peak RSS |\n141\t| 9 | Measurement validity: recall is relative to RDT, which over- and under-reports; source-only mirrors can't exercise tier 1 into `node_modules`; \"outside RDT's set\" counts correct extras as false positives | medium / high | Hand-label about 50 new emissions per project; settle D5 and D6; add a with-dependencies run for Mantine and Chakra |\n142\t| 10 | ADR 0007 rests on an unprobed 7.1 API (`typescript/unstable` versus `./sync ./async ./proto ./ast/*`); `tsc-client` unwired; opaque factories are only about 60 declarations (2 to 3% of misses) | medium / medium | Re-probe 7.1.0-beta first; keep the ADR narrow; defer wiring until stages 3 to 4 are measured |\n143\t| 11 | `@component`: comment attachment edge cases in OXC; a stray annotation forces a prop-less entry | low / medium | Emit with an Info diagnostic when props can't be resolved; test comment placement |\n144\t\n145\tNot verified by the assessor: the enum-index encoding of `DiagnosticCode`, OXC comment attachment, and the counts beyond the reader files.\n146\t\n147\t### Plan changes the risk review implies\n148\t1. Stage 3 splits into 3a (resolver fixes RC4 repro, RC3, RC2, RC1), 3b (`WrapperCall` plus tier 1), 3c (tier 2 behind a flag).\n149\t2. Tier 2 defaults to off (answers D1).\n150\t3. Add a hand-labeled precision sample and a with-dependencies run for Mantine and Chakra to the acceptance gate.\n151\t4. Perf gate is an absolute per-project budget plus peak RSS.\n152\t5. Provenance goes in an Info diagnostic only unless D4 says otherwise.\n153\t6. Re-probe 7.1.0-beta before ADR 0007.\n154\t"}]},"uuid":"97c396da-3cb1-4258-80e9-b6595ff631a3","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:47:41.318Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/research/report.md","content":"# Research report: detecting and resolving wrapper-declared React components\n\nQuestion: how should caliper-docgen detect and resolve components declared through wrapper calls, without hardcoding library names, while preserving the architecture, the semantic models and the TS 7.1 semantic backend (ADR 0006)? Confidence: medium. Sources: four reader reports (architecture docs, code, real library shapes, prior art) and the five-project benchmark. Every claim below is \"confirmed\" unless marked (inferred) or (assumed).\n\n## 1. Recommendation\n\nDetect by declaration shape, in layers. No library names except React builtins.\n\n1. **Extractor** (`visit.rs:229-234`, owned records only, no AST escapes, no cross-file knowledge): add a typed-arrow and function-expression detector, generalize `try_hoc_wrapped` to the first function-valued argument at any position, and record a new owned `WrapperCall` candidate for PascalCase bindings initialized by a call with type arguments or an untyped callback.\n2. **Pipeline promotion pass** after merge (cross-file, per item inside `contain_panic`): tier 1 resolves the callee declaration (aliases, imports, barrels, destructure-from-call) and reads where its type parameters flow into the props position, which gives the type-argument index and payload-versus-props without any name. Tier 2 (no callee declaration) picks the type argument that resolves to a source object type, low confidence. Tier 3 emits nothing and keeps the Info `SkippedCandidate`.\n3. **Resolver fixes** so detected components carry props: accept indexed access as a props base (`resolver/alias.rs:245`), select members from object-literal type arguments, substitute generic interface type arguments (`chain.rs:201`), fix multi-hop barrels after a minimal repro, defer identifier-alias renames to `finish()`.\n4. **Provenance:** a new `non_exhaustive` `DiagnosticCode` (for example `InferredComponent`), Info severity, with line, column and the rule used. No `ComponentEntry` field (it has no schema version). A new `SourceData` or `ComponentMapping` field forces `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` 4 to 5.\n5. **Escape hatch:** a `/** @component */` leading comment first (syntax-only, no options plumbing, react-docgen precedent). A declarative `docgen.config.ts` list only if wanted, since `parse_file(path, source)` takes no options today.\n6. **Semantic backend:** write ADR 0007 allowing the opt-in `tsc --api` backend to discover components (RDT's call-signature rule), handle opaque factories and generics, and keep structural as default and fallback.\n\nFalsifiable claim (inferred from miss counts, not measured): after stages 0 to 3, component recall against RDT's plausible set reaches Mantine at least 85% and Chakra at least 80%, with no regression elsewhere and under 5% of newly emitted components outside RDT's set. If new-emission false positives exceed 5%, or Mantine prop recall stays under 30% after stage 3, the type-shape heuristic is refuted and callee-signature resolution or the checker becomes mandatory.\n\n## 2. Baseline\n\n| Project | RDT components with own props | Caliper found | Component recall | Prop recall |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| mantine | 354 | 103 | 29% | 2% |\n| chakra | 484 | 47 | 9% | 13% |\n| antd | 149 | 132 | 88% | 81% |\n| shadcn | 323 | 317 | 98% | 93% |\n| spectrum | 962 | 947 | 98% | 97% |\n\nCaliper runs in 30 to 141ms and 34 to 78MB, against 0.5 to 2s and 300 to 590MB for react-docgen and react-docgen-typescript (10 to 37 times faster).\n\n## 3. Declaration shapes\n\nLayer: E = extractor, R = pipeline or resolver, S = semantic backend.\n\n| Shape | Props come from | Counts | Layer |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `const X = (props: P) => …` plain typed arrow | first parameter annotation | 29 misses (chakra 16, spectrum 7, antd 3, mantine 2, shadcn 1), all genuine | E |\n| `factory`/`polymorphicFactory`/`genericFactory<F>` (Mantine) | `props` member of the payload object at type argument 0 | 184, 26, 14; found 0 | E records, R selects |\n| `withContext`/`withProvider<El, P>` (Chakra) | type argument 1 | 391, 73; found 8 and 1, with empty props | E records, R chooses index |\n| `withRootProvider<P>` (Chakra) | type argument 0 | 16; found 0 | E records, R |\n| `tableElement<F>('th')` | type argument 0, wraps `factory` | 7; found 0 | E and R |\n| react-aria `createLeafComponent`/`createBranchComponent` | typed first parameter of the function at argument 1 | 32; found 0 | E |\n| `createHideableComponent` | typed first parameter at argument 0 | 14; found 14 | works |\n| Opaque factories: `createEdgeComponent`, tiptap `createControl`, `createIconLoader(\"x\")`, antd `generator`/`genPurePanel` | callee body only | about 60 | S |\n| Aliased callee: `polymorphic = createPolymorphicComponent` | type argument 1 | 1 | R follows alias |\n| Callee destructured from another call: Chakra `const { withContext } = createSlotRecipeContext(…)` | the returned object's signature | 74 files | E records, R/S follow |\n| `chakra(\"div\", { recipe })` | overloads and `HTMLChakraProps<T, P>` | 20; found 0 | S |\n| Generators with non-props type argument: `generateCalendar<Dayjs>` | not the type argument (a trap) | 2 to 3 | S |\n| `lazy`, `dynamic` | the target module | 8 spectrum, 13 shadcn | out of scope |\n| Static member assignments, re-export barrels, filename-mangled names | an existing component under another name | the 67 \"no declaration\" rows are RDT naming artifacts, not misses | none |\n| `export default function _3D(…)` | typed parameter | 6 rows, likely fails the PascalCase test (not traced) | small E |\n\nFalse positives the guard must reject: the `createContext` family (427 across the corpora: spectrum 311, antd 51, shadcn 36, mantine 29), array-destructured providers (47), `withPropsProvider` (returns a Provider), SCREAMING_CASE constants (about 30), `Styled*` helpers, 79 lowercase `style<T>` macros, and hooks and string helpers that RDT counts as components.\n\n## 4. Root causes beyond detection\n\n| Cause | Evidence | Structurally fixable? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| RC1: indexed access rejected as a props base | `alias.rs:245`; repro gives 0 props plus a warning | Yes, for source-defined bases |\n| RC2: no member selection from an object-literal type argument | `extractor/mod.rs:426-433` stringifies it | Yes |\n| RC3: generic interface type arguments ignored | `chain.rs:199-207` | Yes |\n| RC4: multi-hop barrels fail though single-hop is implemented and tested | mantine `core/index.ts` 51 of 79 unresolved; chakra `styled-system/index.ts` 24 | Probably; cause unestablished, needs a repro |\n| RC5: `HTMLChakraProps<T, P>` second argument not expanded | inferred from the dump | Yes, via a `known.rs` arm (still a library shortcut) |\n| RC6: `ElementProps<'input', …>` helper | `Box.tsx:54-57` | Partly |\n| RC7: identifier-alias detection depends on source order | `component.rs:458-481` | Yes |\n| RC8: no detection in plain `.ts` files | `extractor/mod.rs:140` | Policy |\n\n## 5. Constraints that shape the design\n\n- The extractor is per-file with no cross-file knowledge, so callee-signature lookup cannot live there. It must produce an owned candidate record resolved later.\n- Detection is a first-match-wins chain. `SkippedCandidate` (Info) is the deliberate fallback, but it discards the span, so it has no line or column today.\n- ADR 0006 never says whether the semantic backend may discover components. Changing an ADR needs a new ADR.\n- Nothing can register plugins from the CLI or binding, and plugins cannot see the AST.\n- ADR 0006's backend is designed, not implemented. `crates/tsc-client` is not wired into core, the CLI or NAPI.\n- Watch mode builds `ReverseDeps` once per session, so a promotion that depends on a callee in another file can go stale.\n\n## 6. Prior art\n\n- **react-docgen:** syntactic. Unknown calls go through `resolveHOC`, which looks at the first argument (or the last if the first is a literal). It never reads type arguments, so it cannot read Mantine's `Payload['props']`. `@component` is its escape hatch. Storybook defaults to it (\"much faster but incomplete\").\n- **react-docgen-typescript:** the checker, with no library names and no return-type test. A component is an exported symbol whose call signature has a first parameter named `props` or is the sole parameter. It is dormant (last commit 2025-06-10) and crashes on TypeScript 7 (styleguidist/react-docgen-typescript#538).\n- **Mantine's own docs** run RDT over a hand-listed set of files with manual type-string rewrites.\n- **Implication:** the checker is the only name-free detector for opaque factories, and syntax can cover the type-argument and function-argument cases.\n\n## 7. Contradictions\n\n1. `accuracy.md` (mantine 11%, antd 53%) versus `recall2.py` (29%, 88%): a methodology difference. Use `recall2.py`.\n2. Barrel following is implemented and tested, yet multi-hop barrels fail in the dumps. Unresolved.\n3. `STATUS.md` says the semantic lifecycle \"hasn't started\"; `docs/type-checker-integration.md` says the Rust client exists.\n4. `extractor-ast-visiting.md` is stale against `edge-cases.md`.\n5. `edge-cases.md` says shape gaps are closed, yet plain arrows are missed entirely.\n6. The docs say `typescript/unstable/*`; the installed 7.1 nightly exports `./sync ./async ./proto ./ast/*`. Re-probe 7.1.0-beta.\n7. The task framing said RDT tests `JSX.Element`; its code does not.\n8. Confirmed facts say the checker is exact but opt-in, costly and unshipped; assumed facts say cheap syntactic heuristics suffice. Not resolved by picking a side. The plan is layered and measurement decides.\n\n## 8. Tests and CI\n\n1. One minimal fixture per shape, plus each false positive, with `assert_eq!` on exact prop sets and the exact Info diagnostic. Negative fixtures assert zero components.\n2. A CI harness from `recall2.py`, `accuracy.py`, `final.py` and `patterns.py`, with per-shape classification and thresholds (assumed): no per-project regression, Mantine at least 85%, Chakra at least 80%, new-emission precision at least 95%, wall time within +25%.\n3. Sibling-path parity: `extract()`, `WatchSession::update_file` and `create_session` give identical components, props and diagnostics, including after editing a callee file.\n4. Determinism: repeat and reversed file order give byte-identical output.\n5. Source-only versus dependencies-installed runs.\n6. A cache version bump invalidates old `.d.ts` entries.\n7. The promotion pass runs inside `contain_panic` per item.\n8. Semantic stage: extend the RDT-oracle gate to checker-discovered components.\n\n## 9. Staged plan (sizes and recall movement are inference)\n\n| Stage | Scope | Depends on | Size | Expected movement |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 0 | Harness, fixtures, skip span, barrel repro | none | S to M | measurement |\n| 1 | Typed arrow, source-order fix | 0 | S | +29 components |\n| 2 | Function argument at any position, `@component`, provenance diagnostic | 0 | S | up to 32 (spectrum) |\n| 3 | `WrapperCall`, promotion tier 2, RC1 to RC4, builtin deny list, cache v5 | 0, 1 | L | detection upper bound: mantine about 92%, chakra about 89%; props lag unless RC1 to RC4 land |\n| 4 | Callee-signature tier 1, RC5, RC6 | 3 | M to L | precision, Chakra props |\n| 5 | Optional config list | 3 | M | long tail |\n| 6 | ADR 0007 and semantic discovery | ADR, 7.1 beta re-probe, tsc-client wiring | L | about 60 opaque factories, exact types |\n\nRisks: tier-2 false positives (the `createContext` family); detection without RC1 to RC4 yields components with empty props; a one-time `.d.ts` cache miss; stale `ReverseDeps` in watch; Chakra's destructure-from-call callees may push tier 1 to the checker.\n\n## 10. Decide before speccing\n\n- D1: may tier 2 emit by default, or only with callee-signature confirmation or `@component`?\n- D2: is a declarative config list needed, or is `@component` enough?\n- D3: may the semantic backend discover components (ADR 0007), and is wiring `tsc-client` into core in scope?\n- D4: provenance in `ComponentEntry` JSON, or an Info diagnostic only?\n- D5: acceptance thresholds for component recall, prop recall and new-emission precision.\n- D6: parity target: plausible components (`recall2`) or every RDT entry (`accuracy.md`)?\n- D7: plain `.ts` files and underscore-leading names?\n\n## 11. Risk review (vanguard:risk-assessor; overall risk: high; confidence in ranking: medium)\n\n| # | Risk | Severity / likelihood | Mitigation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Tier-2 type-shape heuristic matches the `createContext` family (427 sites), array-destructured providers, `withPropsProvider`, hooks. A name deny list conflicts with \"shapes, not names\" and misses user-land re-exports | critical / high | Tier 2 emits nothing by default. Emit only with callee-signature confirmation, `@component`, or an opt-in flag. Structural discriminators: function-valued callee parameter, component-like return, reject `null`/literal first arguments. Per-family precision, one negative fixture per family |\n| 2 | Detection lands before the prop fixes: components with empty or wrong props (Mantine prop recall 2%; 8 Chakra hits already have empty props). `Factory<P> = P` needs RC3 before RC2 can select `props` | high / high | Order: RC4 repro, RC3, RC2, RC1, then detection. Unresolved props type gives an Info diagnostic and no entry, or a low-confidence entry |\n| 3 | Stage 3 is too large to attribute regressions | high / medium | Split: 3a resolver fixes (valuable on existing components), 3b `WrapperCall` plus tier 1, 3c tier 2 behind a flag. Chakra destructure-from-call (74 files) may move to the checker |\n| 4 | Watch mode: a callee edit or barrel hop doesn't update dependents because `ReverseDeps` has no callee-signature edge; `update_file` can diverge from `extract()` | high / high | Record callee and barrel-hop edges; parity tests including callee-only edits; or re-run promotion globally per update if cheap |\n| 5 | Cache and determinism: a new `DiagnosticCode` variant or `SourceData` field shifts positional msgpack encoding (the enum-index claim is from the ADR, not verified); unordered promotion changes winners and `ComponentKeyCollision` | high / medium | Append fields and variants last; bump `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` in the same commit; test that a v4 blob is rejected; sort candidates by (path, span); define collision precedence |\n| 6 | Output regression for users: hundreds of new components, some wrong, indistinguishable because provenance is only an Info diagnostic (D4); snapshots change; any Warning flips `check --strict` | medium / high | Info only; decide D4 first; hand-review each snapshot diff; changeset note; flag for tier 2 |\n| 7 | Layering: promotion needs resolver machinery (chained wrappers like `tableElement`), tempting a reverse dependency | medium / medium | Pure function (GlobalSourceData, WrapperCall list) to candidates, run before resolution; depth limit; extractor records everything promotion needs; document the direction |\n| 8 | Performance: a cross-file lookup per PascalCase call binding; repeated failed barrel walks | medium / medium | Memoise per (file, symbol); cheap prefilter; bound barrel depth; absolute per-project time budget (about 15ms or 20%) plus peak RSS |\n| 9 | Measurement validity: recall is relative to RDT, which over- and under-reports; source-only mirrors can't exercise tier 1 into `node_modules`; \"outside RDT's set\" counts correct extras as false positives | medium / high | Hand-label about 50 new emissions per project; settle D5 and D6; add a with-dependencies run for Mantine and Chakra |\n| 10 | ADR 0007 rests on an unprobed 7.1 API (`typescript/unstable` versus `./sync ./async ./proto ./ast/*`); `tsc-client` unwired; opaque factories are only about 60 declarations (2 to 3% of misses) | medium / medium | Re-probe 7.1.0-beta first; keep the ADR narrow; defer wiring until stages 3 to 4 are measured |\n| 11 | `@component`: comment attachment edge cases in OXC; a stray annotation forces a prop-less entry | low / medium | Emit with an Info diagnostic when props can't be resolved; test comment placement |\n\nNot verified by the assessor: the enum-index encoding of `DiagnosticCode`, OXC comment attachment, and the counts beyond the reader files.\n\n### Plan changes the risk review implies\n1. Stage 3 splits into 3a (resolver fixes RC4 repro, RC3, RC2, RC1), 3b (`WrapperCall` plus tier 1), 3c (tier 2 behind a flag).\n2. Tier 2 defaults to off (answers D1).\n3. Add a hand-labeled precision sample and a with-dependencies run for Mantine and Chakra to the acceptance gate.\n4. Perf gate is an absolute per-project budget plus peak RSS.\n5. Provenance goes in an Info diagnostic only unless D4 says otherwise.\n6. Re-probe 7.1.0-beta before ADR 0007.\n","numLines":154,"startLine":1,"totalLines":154}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c6a4627d-fb43-449c-8978-8c8856b8b7ac","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"scratch/watch-idle-diag","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
