{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"0af8657a929ca1838f029fc37a5e4d359a074f28425a08193ba4db092e7e362b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sf1Hw6wpuJVxqTqnXU5JNQ","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs","old_string":"            dependencies: None,\n            collapse_inherited_props: options.collapse_inherited_props,\n        }\n    }\n","new_string":"            dependencies: None,\n            react_types: None,\n            collapse_inherited_props: options.collapse_inherited_props,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// This context with React's own declarations indexed apart from the project's, for an HTML layer's attribute\n    /// lookups only (`html::react_attribute`, ADR 0010's amendment). Full mode merges them into `named_types` instead.\n    pub(crate) fn with_react_types(mut self, react_types: Option<Arc<crate::named_type_index::NamedTypeIndex>>) -> Self {\n        self.react_types = react_types;\n        self\n    }\n\n    /// The index holding React's declarations, when this run has them.\n    pub(super) fn react_index(&self) -> &crate::named_type_index::NamedTypeIndex {\n        self.react_types.as_deref().unwrap_or(&self.named_types)\n    }\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012468hJnjxitiEC4Gj1Vqgi","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/core/src/resolver/mod.rs","old_string":"    pub(crate) dependencies: Option<Arc<crate::dependency_types::DependencyLayer>>,\n    pub(crate) collapse_inherited_props: crate::pipeline::CollapseInheritedProps,\n}","new_string":"    pub(crate) dependencies: Option<Arc<crate::dependency_types::DependencyLayer>>,\n    /// React's own declarations in curated mode, which only HTML-attribute lookups read (`react_index`).\n    pub(crate) react_types: Option<Arc<crate::named_type_index::NamedTypeIndex>>,\n    pub(crate) collapse_inherited_props: crate::pipeline::CollapseInheritedProps,\n}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PMLADwf8gBuiguQ4hyZa5d","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/core/src/resolver/html.rs","old_string":"/// `JSX.IntrinsicElements[element]` in React's own types at `react_file`, when this run has them: Full mode merges them;\n/// curated mode and the dependency loader leave them to the HTML layer.\npub(super) fn intrinsic_element<'a>(\n    element: &str,\n    react_file: &Utf8Path,\n    ctx: &'a ResolutionContext,\n) -> Option<&'a CollectedType> {\n    let elements = ctx.named_types.lookup_interface_exact(react_file, \"React.JSX.IntrinsicElements\")?;","new_string":"/// `JSX.IntrinsicElements[element]` in React's own types at `react_file`, when this run has them: Full mode merges them,\n/// curated mode indexes them apart (`ResolutionContext::react_index`), and `none` mode and the dependency loader don't\n/// read them.\npub(super) fn intrinsic_element<'a>(\n    element: &str,\n    react_file: &Utf8Path,\n    ctx: &'a ResolutionContext,\n) -> Option<&'a CollectedType> {\n    let elements = ctx.react_index().lookup_interface_exact(react_file, \"React.JSX.IntrinsicElements\")?;"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TfvkWKoAViDRqo7KrTiq5c","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i '' 's/ctx\\.named_types\\.lookup_interface_exact(react_file, &key)/ctx.react_index().lookup_interface_exact(react_file, \\&key)/; s/let params = ctx\\.named_types\\.lookup_interface_type_params_for(iface);/let params = ctx.react_index().lookup_interface_type_params_for(iface);/; s/ctx\\.named_types\\.lookup_type_alias_exact(react_file, &key)/ctx.react_index().lookup_type_alias_exact(react_file, \\&key)/; s/ctx\\.named_types\\.lookup_type_alias_params(react_file, &key)/ctx.react_index().lookup_type_alias_params(react_file, \\&key)/' crates/core/src/resolver/html.rs && grep -n 'named_types\\|react_index' crates/core/src/resolver/html.rs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"f2aced72c29ca0f0e4f032173452d42942367b1063d30c13db51cb9743a431ff","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/core/src/resolver/html.rs changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. The changes are not shown here; use Read if you need the current content.\n\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n\nHere are the existing tasks:\n\n#1. [completed] Detection precision: render evidence, non-destructive renames, wrapper evidence\n#2. [completed] Type-text P0s: quoted substitution, Infinity/NaN, Required extends, key sets, typeof props, generic alias in prop, cache bump\n#3. [completed] Discovery and small correctness: relative excludes, export-default misses, Required unwrap, PropsWithChildren children\n#4. [completed] Watch revision model shared with cold path, Vite plugin and CLI watch fixes\n#5. [completed] Diagnostics identity and dedup, resolution memoization, cache fingerprint\n#6. [completed] Docs, DX and ADR 0007 amendment; restate #64 figures\n#7. [pending] Replace name-based special cases with structural rules\n#8. [completed] Delta contract: every changed key and diagnostic in IncrementalUpdate\n#9. [completed] Symbol precedence: resolve the binding before builtin or utility names\n#10. [completed] Render evidence: count only returned JSX and resolved element types; precision gate\n#11. [completed] Silent degradations: tsconfig parsing, RenderProps shortcut, cache size bound\n#12. [completed] Interned props: ADR 0009\n#13. [completed] Interned props: Rust serialization\n#14. [completed] Interned props: JS consumers and docs\n#15. [completed] Prove dependency loading: stage 1 loader prototype\n#16. [completed] Prove dependency loading: stage 2 end-to-end on an experimental branch\n#17. [completed] Dependency types 1: resolver groundwork PR\n#18. [completed] Dependency types 2: namespace re-exports\n#19. [completed] Dependency types 3: share resolved props in memory\n#20. [completed] Dependency types 4: type-text fixes\n#21. [completed] Dependency types 5: loader + dependency layer behind a flag, with ADRs\n#22. [completed] Replace trybuild compile_fail test with a doctest pair\n#23. [completed] ComponentProps<typeof X> resolves to X's props\n#24. [completed] Investigate failing Dependabot PR #84\n#25. [completed] Track A: precision and detection PR chain\n#26. [completed] Track B: Storybook integration PR chain\n#27. [completed] Track C: hardening, gates and docs PR chain\n#28. [completed] Fix macOS flake in a_signal_restores_the_terminal_mode_the_session_changed\n#29. [in_progress] Record the agreed decisions (load-deps default plan, collapse default, ADR 0010 amendment, quote style)\n#30. [pending] Wrapper components: props from the callee's result type (Mantine component/renderRoot), recipe variant props, opaque factories\n\n<total_tokens>14906095 tokens left</total_tokens>\n\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."}]}}
