ps merging React into the project index; `none` mode and the dependency loader (0010) don't read React at all.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- A prop that collides with an attribute of the layer's element has both types in curated mode too, with both declarations listed. The attribute keeps its alias name (`ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>`), because nothing else in curated mode expands React's aliases.\n- One more declaration file per run: `dtsFilesParsed` rises by one in every fixture snapshot. Wall time on the five benchmark corpora is unchanged within run-to-run noise.\n- On those corpora with default flags, 7 shadcn props change (`ChartContainer.children` now intersects React's `children`); nothing else does.\n- Without `@types/react`, curated mode behaves as before and reports nothing, since it never required it.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6906de55-3a73-4cf6-813b-fc8b86652632","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"25d373a2-c504-4e22-92b6-cbe6b82be099","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Write","toolUseID":"toolu_01PTiyRLGvxLjDQger3mvTRp","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":51},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e24bd116-2642-47d0-a66b-ec2c0c5f8c87","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:10.317Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"cf41de82-c657-4123-a5a9-131f5bf172cc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018st3FVQixyVPEjMFXetTsJ","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/adr/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"ee5d436f-06fe-4a69-a0b0-129297f2a728","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:10.406Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/adr/README.md","oldString":"- [12. Collapse large inherited dependency sources, as Storybook does](0012-collapse-large-dependency-sources.md) — do not resolve a collapsed source's props, or collapse a component's own props.","newString":"- [12. Collapse large inherited dependency sources, as Storybook does](0012-collapse-large-dependency-sources.md) — do not resolve a collapsed source's props, or collapse a component's own props.\n- [13. Read React's attribute declarations in curated mode, in an index of their own](0013-curated-mode-reads-react-attributes-apart.md) — do not merge React into the project index outside Full mode, or make the React index a lookup fallback.","originalFile":"# Architecture Decision Records\n\nShort, dated records of _architectural_ decisions — ones that shape system structure, boundaries, or contracts other code depends on. Not a changelog, not a design doc, not a place to explain what the code does — comments and `ARCHITECTURE.md` already do that.\n\n## Index\n\nOne line per ADR, with what it guards. Add a line when you add an ADR.\n\n- [1. Parse with OXC instead of the TypeScript compiler](0001-oxc-over-typescript-compiler.md) — do not add a type-checking pass to the default path. The opt-in backend is 0006.\n- [2. Hand-write Serialize/Deserialize for PropType instead of deriving it](0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md) — do not derive them on `PropType` or `CollectedType`.\n- [3. Cache the DTS parse cache with positional (not named) MessagePack](0003-positional-msgpack-cache-encoding.md) — do not reorder, insert or remove `SourceData` fields without bumping `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION`.\n- [4. Defer full type-checker integration](0004-defer-type-checker-integration.md) — superseded by 0006.\n- [5. Contain panics at a single, per-item boundary](0005-panic-containment-boundary.md) — route anything reachable from a rayon `.map()`, a `DocgenPlugin` hook or a NAPI entry point through `contain_panic`.\n- [6. Run the TypeScript backend as a second resolver](0006-semantic-backend-as-second-resolver.md) — do not patch `Opaque` leaves, give `crates/core` a compiler process or I/O, or route the backend through NAPI.\n\n- [7. Let the backend discover components, always compile it in, and keep structural as the default](0007-backend-discovers-components-and-compiles-in.md) — do not feature-gate the backend crate, run it by default, or let it replace a structural entry on a clash.\n- [8. Discard the parse cache whenever the build that wrote it differs](0008-parse-cache-keyed-by-build.md) — do not load cache entries without checking the payload's header against the running build.\n- [9. Write each distinct prop once in the canonical output](0009-canonical-output-interns-props.md) — do not inline props in canonical JSON or derive prop ids from position.\n- [10. Load dependency declarations by name, before resolution, into a shared layer](0010-load-dependency-declarations-by-name.md) — do not load dependency files by import closure, resolve against them lazily during resolution, emit their components or enums, or let them outrank a known shortcut.\n- [11. Find dependency declarations through a per-package export index, not the parse cache](0011-per-package-export-index.md) — do not put dependency files in the `DtsCache` or reuse an index whose package's `package.json` changed.\n- [12. Collapse large inherited dependency sources, as Storybook does](0012-collapse-large-dependency-sources.md) — do not resolve a collapsed source's props, or collapse a component's own props.\n\nChanging any of these needs a new ADR.\n\n## When to write one\n\nTwo gates, both required:\n\n1. **Architectural.** It affects one of: system structure (module/crate boundaries, how components interact), a dependency or technology choice that ripples across the codebase, a data format or contract other code depends on, or a cross-cutting constraint (performance model, correctness discipline, security model).\n2. **Expensive to reverse and not obvious from the code.** If it gets reverted in a year, what breaks, and would anyone know why?\n\nIf either answer is no, it's not an ADR.\n\nGood candidates:\n\n- Choosing OXC over the TypeScript compiler — a technology choice that shapes the whole extraction pipeline\n- A serialization format with a hidden constraint (msgpack's positional encoding) — a data contract other code depends on\n- Dropping a dependency, or an approach that was tried and abandoned\n\nNot ADR material:\n\n- A single function's algorithm choice, confined to that function — that's a code comment\n- A bug fix — commit message, and if it's the kind of thing that could recur, a line in `rdt-coverage.md`\n- A behavior-preserving refactor — commit message is enough\n- A naming or style convention — that's `AGENTS.md` or a lint rule\n- Anything already obvious from the code or from `AGENTS.md`'s non-negotiables\n- Per-user preferences, workflow notes and tool quirks — that's agent memory\n\n## Format\n\nOne file per decision: `docs/adr/NNNN-short-title.md`, numbered sequentially, never reused. Copy `0000-template.md` to start.\n\n- **Never edit history.** If a decision changes, write a new ADR and mark the old one's status `Superseded by 000X`. Don't rewrite the old file to look like you knew all along.\n- **Status** is one of: `Accepted`, `Superseded by NNNN`, `Deprecated`.\n- Keep it short. If the technical depth doesn't fit on a screen, split it into its own doc and link it — see `0006-semantic-backend-as-second-resolver.md` pointing at `type-checker-integration.md` instead of inlining it.\n\n## Writing it\n\nWrite like you're explaining it to the next engineer over their shoulder, not presenting it to a committee. Don't hard-wrap paragraphs at a fixed column — one line per paragraph, let the editor soft-wrap. Every other doc in this repo already does this; hard-wrapping just makes future diffs noisy when a sentence gets edited.\n\n**Cut the filler.** If a sentence still means the same thing without a word, delete the word.\n\n| Instead of | Write |\n| --- | --- |\n| \"It's worth noting that this decision was made in order to leverage OXC's robust parsing capabilities\" | \"OXC parses in parallel with no type-checking pass\" |\n| \"This represents a significant improvement in performance\" | \"32ms instead of several seconds\" |\n| \"We decided to essentially utilize a positional encoding approach\" | \"We use positional encoding\" |\n| \"In conclusion, this architecture provides a solid foundation going forward\" | (delete — you already said the thing) |\n\n**Banned by default:** _leverage, utilize, robust, seamless, cutting-edge, essentially, basically, in order to, it's worth noting, it is important to note, at the end of the day._ If one is genuinely the precise technical word for something, fine — but check first.\n\n**Concrete beats vague.** Name the file, the number, the benchmark. \"Slow\" is not a fact; \"several seconds on a mid-size design system\" is.\n\n**Active voice, plain structure.** \"We chose X because Y\" beats \"X was chosen due to Y considerations.\" Sentence-case headers, not Title Case.\n\n**Show the trade-off, not just the win.** A decision with no downside isn't a decision, it's a fact. Say what it costs.\n\n**Structure isn't fixed.** A paragraph, a paragraph plus bullets, a short table — whatever makes it scannable in one pass. `0006`'s Decision section is an intro line plus three bullets because it's three real choices; don't force that into one paragraph, and don't add sections or padding a one-line decision doesn't need.\n\n## What good looks like\n\nRead `0002-manual-serialize-for-prop-type.md` — a real bug behind it, a real number (`recursion_limit = 2048`), a real consequence, four sections, no throat-clearing.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":6,"newStart":19,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - [10. Load dependency declarations by name, before resolution, into a shared layer](0010-load-dependency-declarations-by-name.md) — do not load dependency files by import closure, resolve against them lazily during resolution, emit their components or enums, or let them outrank a known shortcut."," - [11. Find dependency declarations through a per-package export index, not the parse cache](0011-per-package-export-index.md) — do not put dependency files in the `DtsCache` or reuse an index whose package's `package.json` changed."," - [12. Collapse large inherited dependency sources, as Storybook does](0012-collapse-large-dependency-sources.md) — do not resolve a collapsed source's props, or collapse a component's own props.","+- [13. Read React's attribute declarations in curated mode, in an index of their own](0013-curated-mode-reads-react-attributes-apart.md) — do not merge React into the project index outside Full mode, or make the React index a lookup fallback."," "," Changing any of these needs a new ADR."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cf41de82-c657-4123-a5a9-131f5bf172cc","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"ee5d436f-06fe-4a69-a0b0-129297f2a728","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_018st3FVQixyVPEjMFXetTsJ","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Edit\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":51},"type":"attachment","uuid":"30418ad5-815d-4df0-95ca-b115dd5193c0","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:10.405Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"f4bdc5d4-9093-41e0-b37a-6773989b7c49","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DvarMh6cASSt7rwJnwZ15H","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/STATUS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"8d8b7e8a-e735-4b28-87db-e0a5305c1a86","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:10.487Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/STATUS.md","oldString":"it is off by default while its output is checked against RDT (ADR 0010).","newString":"it is off by default while its output is checked against RDT (ADR 0010), and becomes the default in 0.5.0 once that check passes on the 20 fixture libraries.","originalFile":"# Status\n\n**Updated:** 2026-10-22\n\nCore extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are fully tested. Config file loading, watch mode (including rebuilds on config changes and polling with `ensure_fresh`), plugin architecture, TOON token-optimized output format, JSON schema export, LSP server scaffold, and bounded atomic DTS caching are implemented and verified.\n\n**Types from other packages.** Imports resolve to any file under a source directory, `.d.ts` included, so a monorepo whose packages are all source directories resolves across them. By default, from `node_modules` only `@types/react` and TypeScript's own lib files are read, and a prop whose type comes from any other installed package stays a named reference with an `UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT` warning. `--load-dependencies` (config, NAPI and Vite `loadDependencies`) loads the declarations those names point to; it is off by default while its output is checked against RDT (ADR 0010).\n\n## Numbers\n\n- 745 Rust tests (729 workspace tests under `cargo nextest`, 16 NAPI binding tests) and 46 vitest (41 unit with a mocked binding, 5 integration against the real native binding), all green\n- `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` clean with `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` enforced workspace-wide\n- 20 real-world fixture libraries validated against `react-docgen-typescript` (shadcn, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Mantine, React Aria, antd, ariakit, ark-ui, base-ui, blueprint, day-picker, fluentui, headlessui, panda, react-final-form, react-resizable-panels, storybook-emotion, tanstack-table, zendesk-garden — see `rdt-coverage.md`)\n- **Recall** against `react-docgen-typescript`, own props, five source-only mirrors with no dependencies installed (`docs/projects/architecture-roadmap.md`, after #69): components found Mantine 93%, Chakra 92%, Ant Design 97%, shadcn/ui 98%, react-spectrum 99%; share of RDT's props reported 92%, 85%, 95%, 94%, 97%.\n- **Precision** per detection rule (`docs/precision.md`, 2026-10-21): 1 component that isn't one in 154 sampled, `functionDeclaration` 96% and every other rule 100%. 25 samples per rule can't yet establish the 95% gate.\n- **Speed** on five pinned public corpora (`docs/performance.md`, 2026-10-22): 34 to 81 ms wall time and 66 to 153 MB peak RSS for 41 to 490 kLOC, 17 to 39 times faster than `react-docgen-typescript` on the same files. CI fails on a 10% regression against main or a ratio under 10×.\n\n## Features and improvements\n\n- **Testing Stack** — `cargo-nextest` process runner, `rstest` parameterized spec tables, `insta` snapshots, and `trycmd` executable Markdown CLI specs.\n- **Plugin system** (`DocgenPlugin` / `PluginRegistry`) — Extensible AST and component resolution hooks in `crates/core/src/plugin.rs`.\n- **TOON output format** (`--format toon` / `toon.rs`) — Token-optimized format for LLM agents, cutting context window token usage by ~65-75%.\n- **JSON schema export** (`caliper-docgen schema`) — Machine-readable Draft-07 JSON Schema export for component metadata validation.\n- **Atomic & Bounded DTS cache** (`cache.rs`) — Atomic temp-file swap writes, dirty flag tracking, and 5,000 entry eviction cap.\n- **LSP server scaffold** (`caliper-docgen lsp`) — bounded framing plus initialize/shutdown/exit lifecycle. It currently advertises `hoverProvider: false` and does not serve component prop hovers yet.\n- **Strict Safe Rust** — `unsafe_code = \"deny\"` via `[workspace.lints]`, active across all three crates (`core`, `cli`, `binding`) — none currently use `unsafe`, including the NAPI FFI boundary (napi-rs's `#[napi]` macros generate the glue without user-visible `unsafe`).\n\n## Known gaps that won't get fixed without a type checker\n\nSee the \"Known gaps summary\" table in `rdt-coverage.md` for the full, maintained list. The short version: conditional types, mapped types over an unbound generic, and a couple of `@emotion/styled`-specific call shapes all need real type inference OXC deliberately doesn't do. Not bugs.\n\nAn opt-in TypeScript 7 semantic backend is designed (ADR 0006) but not implemented. Accuracy is verified against real RDT — 0 missing/extra props on 13 hand-picked components, and re-verified against the full 44-file fixture corpus (5,508/5,522 `required` matches, 5,265/5,522 type-string matches; the gap is explained noise, not a resolver bug) — and the RDT oracle that comparison depends on now runs on its own `typescript@6` install, separate from the semantic probe's `typescript@next`. Lifecycle (crash/restart/timeout handling for the `tsc --api` process) hasn't started; see `type-checker-integration.md`'s Gates table.\n\n## Where to look next\n\n- **Edge cases, failure modes, and gaps not yet fixed** → `edge-cases.md` — comprehensive audit of crash/hang risks, silent data loss, and silent correctness bugs across every subsystem, prioritized. Update it as findings get fixed or new ones turn up.\n- **Why those gaps happened, and the plan to fix them** → `root-cause-analysis.md` — the edge-case findings collapsed into 11 mechanism-level root causes with concrete fix proposals, plus a Phase 1 task breakdown.\n- **What broke and why, historically** → `rdt-coverage.md` — every bug found during real-library validation, root cause, and the fix. Keep this updated; it's the project's memory.\n- **Why a hard-to-reverse decision was made** → `docs/adr/` — OXC over the TypeScript compiler, manual serde for `PropType`, positional msgpack encoding, panic containment, the TypeScript 7 semantic backend. Write a new one when you make a decision like these (see `docs/adr/README.md`).\n- **How the pipeline fits together** → `ARCHITECTURE.md`, and `docs/architecture/` for per-subsystem invariants and known gaps (moved from `.claude/semantic-model/` so every coding agent can read it, not just Claude Code — `AGENTS.md` is now this repo's shared instructions file, with per-tool mirrors under `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, `.gemini/`, `.github/`, `.opencode/`).\n- **Setup, testing, code style, commit conventions** → `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- **Migrating from react-docgen-typescript** → `MIGRATING.md`\n- **Old build-out specs, resolved questions, point-in-time analyses** → `docs/archive/` — historical, not current, kept for reference\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":4,"oldLines":7,"newStart":4,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Core extraction, resolver, CLI, NAPI binding, and Vite plugin all work and are fully tested. Config file loading, watch mode (including rebuilds on config changes and polling with `ensure_fresh`), plugin architecture, TOON token-optimized output format, JSON schema export, LSP server scaffold, and bounded atomic DTS caching are implemented and verified."," ","-**Types from other packages.** Imports resolve to any file under a source directory, `.d.ts` included, so a monorepo whose packages are all source directories resolves across them. By default, from `node_modules` only `@types/react` and TypeScript's own lib files are read, and a prop whose type comes from any other installed package stays a named reference with an `UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT` warning. `--load-dependencies` (config, NAPI and Vite `loadDependencies`) loads the declarations those names point to; it is off by default while its output is checked against RDT (ADR 0010).","+**Types from other packages.** Imports resolve to any file under a source directory, `.d.ts` included, so a monorepo whose packages are all source directories resolves across them. By default, from `node_modules` only `@types/react` and TypeScript's own lib files are read, and a prop whose type comes from any other installed package stays a named reference with an `UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT` warning. `--load-dependencies` (config, NAPI and Vite `loadDependencies`) loads the declarations those names point to; it is off by default while its output is checked against RDT (ADR 0010), and becomes the default in 0.5.0 once that check passes on the 20 fixture libraries."," "," ## Numbers"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f4bdc5d4-9093-41e0-b37a-6773989b7c49","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"8d8b7e8a-e735-4b28-87db-e0a5305c1a86","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01DvarMh6cASSt7rwJnwZ15H","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Edit\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2e4fbf1d-7fd7-4443-b8a8-40ebf3bad8c3","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:10.487Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"2e4fbf1d-7fd7-4443-b8a8-40ebf3bad8c3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"1","subject":"Detection precision: render evidence, non-destructive renames, wrapper evidence","description":"Typed function/arrow/HOC-arg and function declarations require render evidence (JSX/createElement/children/null body or React return type); declare function with JSX return accepted; wrapper first-arg evidence (render fn, tag + element type arg, PascalCase reference); reject createContext; diagnostic for rejected recorded candidates; remove empty-props guard (dropped 84 real Chakra comps); renames never delete an exported base. Negative families in shapes.rs; fix tests that pinned silent drops.","activeForm":"Fixing detection precision","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"2","subject":"Type-text P0s: quoted substitution, Infinity/NaN, Required extends, key sets, typeof props, generic alias in prop, cache bump","description":"Done in #72 (structured args, typeof props, Required extends, quoted substitution, Infinity) and #73 (key sets). Generic alias in prop position moved to task 5 with the memo.","activeForm":"Fixing type-text defects","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"3","subject":"Discovery and small correctness: relative excludes, export-default misses, Required unwrap, PropsWithChildren children","description":"Match .test./.stories. excludes relative to src dir; detect export default arrow/memo/forwardRef/class; stop treating Required<P> as transparent; children from PropsWithChildren.","activeForm":"Fixing discovery and small correctness issues","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"4","subject":"Watch revision model shared with cold path, Vite plugin and CLI watch fixes","description":"One immutable Revision, single writer, assemble shared with extract(), real dependency edges (barrels, ../, aliases, .js), deltas with removals, seeded diagnostics, filters/plugins in watch; Vite: removals, keys, invalidation, build --watch, build errors; CLI: write --out at start, r re-extracts. Gate: snapshot()==extract() property test.","activeForm":"Building the watch revision model","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"5","subject":"Diagnostics identity and dedup, resolution memoization, cache fingerprint","description":"Dedup by (code,file,span,subject) with affected components; memoize type resolution per run; cache keyed on crate version + extractor fingerprint with versioned payload; diagnostics on cache decode failure.","activeForm":"Reworking diagnostics and cache","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"6","subject":"Docs, DX and ADR 0007 amendment; restate #64 figures","description":"Docs, DX and the semantic merge contract (Codex #4): ADR amending 0007 with component identity, field-level precedence (structural identity, checker props), diagnostic retirement, provenance and disagreement handling; triggers that do not rely only on visible incompleteness; schemaVersion vs mode/provenance fields. One reproducible scorecard (recall own/any, hand-labelled precision, prop type/required/default/description agreement, time, RSS, watch parity, with and without deps). Reconcile benchmarks.md, STATUS.md and roadmap figures; CLI DX items.","activeForm":"Fixing docs and DX","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"7","subject":"Replace name-based special cases with structural rules","description":"Revised per Codex: symbol origin (not every @types declaration terminal, record why resolution stopped); wrapper detection from callee signature where structural data permits, else labelled inferred and measured; library shortcuts need a type-resolution adapter boundary before moving out of core; finite keyof/mapped evaluator within a stated budget with opaque diagnostics; React tables from installed @types/react only when requested, curated fallback. Blocked by symbol precedence and the precision gate.","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"8","subject":"Delta contract: every changed key and diagnostic in IncrementalUpdate","description":"Codex #3. updated_keys must include kept components whose key or entry changed (name-collision key shifts on delete/create); add removed diagnostics; Vite drops updates older than the newest revision across files. Test: apply every emitted delta to the previous output and assert it equals snapshot(), including collisions, diagnostic disappearance and cross-file reordering.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"9","subject":"Symbol precedence: resolve the binding before builtin or utility names","description":"Codex #1. named.rs checks React builtins and chain.rs checks TS utilities before source lookup, so a local ReactNode/Partial is misread. Resolve the binding first; apply builtin meaning only when the origin is React/TS lib, or as a reported fallback when resolution fails. Tests with local ReactNode, CSSProperties, Partial, Required.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"10","subject":"Render evidence: count only returned JSX and resolved element types; precision gate","description":"Codex #2. JSX must be in a returned expression, not any nested callback; element return annotations resolve their origin; wrapper/rename name heuristics frozen. Add a hand-labelled precision sample per detection family (roadmap 95% gate) before any detector expansion.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"11","subject":"Silent degradations: tsconfig parsing, RenderProps shortcut, cache size bound","description":"Codex #5/#6. Parse tsconfig with a JSONC-aware parser and report read/parse failures; RenderProps keeps the function form or reports opacity; bound the DTS cache file size before decoding. Silence list records why resolution stopped.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"12","subject":"Interned props: ADR 0009","description":"Write docs/adr/0009 for the canonical output's prop table (content-hash ids, update carries referenced entries, rdt stays expanded) and index it.","activeForm":"Writing ADR 0009","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"13","subject":"Interned props: Rust serialization","description":"Custom Serialize/Deserialize for ExtractionOutput and IncrementalUpdate writing a top-level props table and prop ids in components (props and notableInherited). FNV-1a 64 of compact prop JSON; collision is a serialization error. Snapshots stay expanded. Tests: round-trip, id stability, collision, update table completeness. Update schema command.","activeForm":"Implementing interned serialization","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"14","subject":"Interned props: JS consumers and docs","description":"Update packages/napi/index.d.ts types, Vite plugin update payload (props), apps/validate normalize, docs describing the canonical format; measure size and time on corpora; open stacked PR on perf/output-path.","activeForm":"Updating JS consumers","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"15","subject":"Prove dependency loading: stage 1 loader prototype","description":"Standalone scratch Rust prototype (outside the repo) of name-driven dependency .d.ts loading with a per-package export index and work-queue overlap with project parsing. Measure files touched, cold vs warm-index time, overlap gain, watch new-import cost on the 5 installed corpora.","activeForm":"Prototyping the dependency loader","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"16","subject":"Prove dependency loading: stage 2 end-to-end on an experimental branch","description":"Experimental caliper branch (local, behind a flag) plugging the loader into a shared dependency layer before resolve; measure resolved types, output change, leaks, display-filter-before-resolve and session memo, timings cold/warm/watch vs today and RDT.","activeForm":"Measuring dependency loading end to end","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"17","subject":"Dependency types 1: resolver groundwork PR","description":"tsconfig auto-discovery, customConditions, .d.mts/.d.cts, the two resolve_dts retries (@types fallback for .js exports; types-only conditions retry), one shared ResolveOptions builder. PR against main, ported from exp/dependency-types without the loader.","activeForm":"Building resolver groundwork","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"18","subject":"Dependency types 2: namespace re-exports","description":"Extractor promotion of `import * as ns; export { ns as N }` and named-import namespace members in resolve_to_canonical.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"19","subject":"Dependency types 3: share resolved props in memory","description":"Arc-shared resolved props across components so large inherited sources (chakra) don't copy per component; then the session memo.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"20","subject":"Dependency types 4: type-text fixes","description":"Keep alias names when expansion is conditional/mapped, generic defaults, handler types, callback return types, fake (e: void).","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"21","subject":"Dependency types 5: loader + dependency layer behind a flag, with ADRs","description":"Persisted per-package index, fallback indexes, precedence, value index, leak guards, watch demand diff; ADR for loading and for replacing DtsCache for dependencies.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"22","subject":"Replace trybuild compile_fail test with a doctest pair","description":"compile_fail + compiling ParsedProp::new doctests on ParsedProp; remove trybuild dev-dep and tests/compile_fail. Independent PR off main.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"23","subject":"ComponentProps<typeof X> resolves to X's props","description":"Direct props position (known::component_props) looks up component values (local, imported, namespace members) like extends' component_props_of. Stacked on namespace re-exports.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"24","subject":"Investigate failing Dependabot PR #84","description":"Find why CI fails on dependabot routine-npm PR #84 and fix or report.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"25","subject":"Track A: precision and detection PR chain","description":"Factory payload props, called-only helpers, exported flag, rdt filePath — stacked off main.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"26","subject":"Track B: Storybook integration PR chain","description":"NAPI in worker_threads, Storybook 11 docgen provider package, Storybook 10 Vite __docgenInfo mode, remove --format storybook.","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"27","subject":"Track C: hardening, gates and docs PR chain","description":"Watch rebuild on config changes, ensure-fresh session API, size-normalized CI gates + scorecard, stale docs (covers task #6).","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"28","subject":"Fix macOS flake in a_signal_restores_the_terminal_mode_the_session_changed","description":"Test fails under parallel load on macOS (exit code None vs Some(0)). Find the race, fix it, PR stacked on #120.","activeForm":"Fixing the terminal-mode test flake","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"29","subject":"Record the agreed decisions (load-deps default plan, collapse default, ADR 0010 amendment, quote style)","description":"ADR 0010 amendment so curated mode loads React's attribute declarations; keep source quotes in string defaults; collapse default stays dependencies; --load-dependencies default in 0.5.0 after RDT check. PR stacked.","activeForm":"Recording the agreed decisions","status":"in_progress","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"30","subject":"Wrapper components: props from the callee's result type (Mantine component/renderRoot), recipe variant props, opaque factories","description":"Recall now 92-99%. Remaining: Mantine 439 missed props from MantineComponent<Payload> return-type extras (factory returns `Component as MantineComponent<Payload>`); Chakra 27 recipe variant props; ~7 opaque factories (createIconLoader). Structural, name-free; ADR + stacked PRs; measure with bench/caliper-dumps.sh and missing_props.py.","activeForm":"Resolving wrapper result-type props","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":30},"type":"attachment","uuid":"230eebf6-5be1-4359-aea5-ae003a681b63","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:10.513Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n\nHere are the existing tasks:\n\n#1. [completed] Detection precision: render evidence, non-destructive renames, wrapper evidence\n#2. [completed] Type-text P0s: quoted substitution, Infinity/NaN, Required extends, key sets, typeof props, generic alias in prop, cache bump\n#3. [completed] Discovery and small correctness: relative excludes, export-default misses, Required unwrap, PropsWithChildren children\n#4. [completed] Watch revision model shared with cold path, Vite plugin and CLI watch fixes\n#5. [completed] Diagnostics identity and dedup, resolution memoization, cache fingerprint\n#6. [completed] Docs, DX and ADR 0007 amendment; restate #64 figures\n#7. [pending] Replace name-based special cases with structural rules\n#8. [completed] Delta contract: every changed key and diagnostic in IncrementalUpdate\n#9. [completed] Symbol precedence: resolve the binding before builtin or utility names\n#10. [completed] Render evidence: count only returned JSX and resolved element types; precision gate\n#11. [completed] Silent degradations: tsconfig parsing, RenderProps shortcut, cache size bound\n#12. [completed] Interned props: ADR 0009\n#13. [completed] Interned props: Rust serialization\n#14. [completed] Interned props: JS consumers and docs\n#15. [completed] Prove dependency loading: stage 1 loader prototype\n#16. [completed] Prove dependency loading: stage 2 end-to-end on an experimental branch\n#17. [completed] Dependency types 1: resolver groundwork PR\n#18. [completed] Dependency types 2: namespace re-exports\n#19. [completed] Dependency types 3: share resolved props in memory\n#20. [completed] Dependency types 4: type-text fixes\n#21. [completed] Dependency types 5: loader + dependency layer behind a flag, with ADRs\n#22. [completed] Replace trybuild compile_fail test with a doctest pair\n#23. [completed] ComponentProps<typeof X> resolves to X's props\n#24. [completed] Investigate failing Dependabot PR #84\n#25. [completed] Track A: precision and detection PR chain\n#26. [completed] Track B: Storybook integration PR chain\n#27. [completed] Track C: hardening, gates and docs PR chain\n#28. [completed] Fix macOS flake in a_signal_restores_the_terminal_mode_the_session_changed\n#29. [in_progress] Record the agreed decisions (load-deps default plan, collapse default, ADR 0010 amendment, quote style)\n#30. [pending] Wrapper components: props from the callee's result type (Mantine component/renderRoot), recipe variant props, opaque factories\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
