{"parentUuid":"9985cedb-d6a7-4e09-859f-6685734a0836","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016HcsTgx61Ravxa5LiiCRPB","type":"tool_result","content":"---\ncargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-vite-plugin: patch\n---\n\n- **A prop two intersection members declare has both types:** `A & B` used to keep whichever member declared a prop first, dropping the other declaration. As in TypeScript, the prop now has the intersection of both types (literal unions reduce to their common values, so `(\"default\" | \"destructive\") & (\"default\" | \"info\")` is `\"default\"`), is required when either member requires it, and lists both declarations. An interface's own declaration still replaces the one it extends.\n- **In Full mode, a prop beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` also has the element attribute's type:** recharts' `onTimeUpdate` next to a div's attributes is `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>` intersected with recharts' handler. Curated mode does not read React's declarations, so there the prop keeps the other member's type.\nalias-display.md  642B\ncalled-helpers.md  668B\ncollapse-inherited-props.md  955B\ncomponent-props-of-typeof.md  774B\nexported-flag.md  1021B\nfactory-payload-props.md  659B\nfunction-types.md  1.1K\nintersection-props-intersect.md  1000B\njsdoc-attaches-to-next-declaration.md  730B\nload-dependency-types.md  1.1K\nnamespace-reexports.md  550B\nrdt-file-path.md  296B\nremove-storybook-format.md  320B\nresolve-like-typescript.md  964B\nsession-docgen-info.md  581B\nsession-ensure-fresh.md  614B\nshared-props.md  759B\nstorybook-provider.md  563B\nunevaluable-indexed-access-keeps-alias-name.md  902B\nvite-inject-docgen-info.md  427B\nwatch-rebuild-on-config.md  861B\nzero-argument-callback-text.md  370B","is_error"