{"parentUuid":"d368f315-10bc-492e-b739-2f54f59cd88a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TiSC5ArLqKBZgvdKqU45EM","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.changeset/intersection-props-intersect.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"b070f0e9-1626-45f8-a701-228138c29eb1","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:25.422Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.changeset/intersection-props-intersect.md","oldString":"- **In Full mode, a prop beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` also has the element attribute's type:** recharts' `onTimeUpdate` next to a div's attributes is `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>` intersected with recharts' handler. Curated mode does not read React's declarations, so there the prop keeps the other member's type.","newString":"- **A prop beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` also has the element attribute's type:** recharts' `onTimeUpdate` next to a div's attributes is `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>` intersected with recharts' handler, in Full and curated mode alike. Curated mode reads React's declarations for this lookup only (ADR 0013), so nothing else in its output changes.","originalFile":"---\ncargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-vite-plugin: patch\n---\n\n- **A prop two intersection members declare has both types:** `A & B` used to keep whichever member declared a prop first, dropping the other declaration. As in TypeScript, the prop now has the intersection of both types (literal unions reduce to their common values, so `(\"default\" | \"destructive\") & (\"default\" | \"info\")` is `\"default\"`), is required when either member requires it, and lists both declarations. An interface's own declaration still replaces the one it extends.\n- **In Full mode, a prop beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` also has the element attribute's type:** recharts' `onTimeUpdate` next to a div's attributes is `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>` intersected with recharts' handler. Curated mode does not read React's declarations, so there the prop keeps the other member's type.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":4,"newStart":8,"newLines":4,"lines":[" ---"," "," - **A prop two intersection members declare has both types:** `A & B` used to keep whichever member declared a prop first, dropping the other declaration. As in TypeScript, the prop now has the intersection of both types (literal unions reduce to their common values, so `(\"default\" | \"destructive\") & (\"default\" | \"info\")` is `\"default\"`), is required when either member requires it, and lists both declarations. An interface's own declaration still replaces the one it extends.","-- **In Full mode, a prop beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` also has the element attribute's type:** recharts' `onTimeUpdate` next to a div's attributes is `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>` intersected with recharts' handler. Curated mode does not read React's declarations, so there the prop keeps the other member's type.","+- **A prop beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` also has the element attribute's type:** recharts' `onTimeUpdate` next to a div's attributes is `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>` intersected with recharts' handler, in Full and curated mode alike. Curated mode reads React's declarations for this lookup only (ADR 0013), so nothing else in its output changes."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d368f315-10bc-492e-b739-2f54f59cd88a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Project