{"parentUuid":"e901b56d-ddc6-4298-aab1-e7dee20a166a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HiYDzMQtKKa8kVCCGGRxGz","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nnpm/caliper-docgen-storybook: minor\n---\n\n- **New package `caliper-docgen-storybook`:** a Storybook 11 addon whose docgen provider answers argTypes from a caliper-docgen session. It resolves `meta.component` and `meta.subcomponents`, converts with `@storybook/react`'s own converter, applies saved edits before each answer, and hands a component it can't find, or one whose extraction reported a warning or error, to React's docgen. On a four-component example its first answer took 43 ms against React's 504 ms, and later answers 0.4 ms against 0.7–1.5 ms.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"037831cd-7c43-469d-8bd8-89f64b40d08f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:33.565Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nnpm/caliper-docgen-storybook: minor\n---\n\n- **New package `caliper-docgen-storybook`:** a Storybook 11 addon whose docgen provider answers argTypes from a caliper-docgen session. It resolves `meta.component` and `meta.subcomponents`, converts with `@storybook/react`'s own converter, applies saved edits before each answer, and hands a component it can't find, or one whose extraction reported a warning or error, to React's docgen. On a four-component example its first answer took 43 ms against React's 504 ms, and later answers 0.4 ms against 0.7–1.5 ms.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"6c5619f7-66dc-4261-a576-bd24175058a4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"feat/decisions-0.4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":17,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":10},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e901b56d-ddc6-4298-aab1-e7dee20a166a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"037831cd-7c43-469d-8bd8-89f64b40d08f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01HiYDzMQtKKa8kVCCGGRxGz","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":50},"type":"attachment","uuid":"41f55112-68f8-4258-830c-1aa111c2174e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:33.564Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"41f55112-68f8-4258-830c-1aa111c2174e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.changeset/intersection-props-intersect.md","snippet":"3\tcargo/caliper-docgen: patch\n4\tcargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\n5\tnpm/caliper-docgen: patch\n6\tnpm/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\n7\tnpm/caliper-docgen-vite-plugin: patch\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t- **A prop two intersection members declare has both types:** `A & B` used to keep whichever member declared a prop first, dropping the other declaration. As in TypeScript, the prop now has the intersection of both types (literal unions reduce to their common values, so `(\"default\" | \"destructive\") & (\"default\" | \"info\")` is `\"default\"`), is required when either member requires it, and lists both declarations. An interface's own declaration still replaces the one it extends.\n11\t- **In Full mode, a prop beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` also has the element attribute's type:** recharts' `onTimeUpdate` next to a div's attributes is `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>` intersected with recharts' handler. Curated mode does not read React's declarations, so there the prop keeps the other member's type."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"652e29f1-9eec-4d2b-9ee8-5e7586b6827b","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:33.592Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.changeset/intersection-props-intersect.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n3\tcargo/caliper-docgen: patch\n4\tcargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\n5\tnpm/caliper-docgen: patch\n6\tnpm/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\n7\tnpm/caliper-docgen-vite-plugin: patch\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t- **A prop two intersection members declare has both types:** `A & B` used to keep whichever member declared a prop first, dropping the other declaration. As in TypeScript, the prop now has the intersection of both types (literal unions reduce to their common values, so `(\"default\" | \"destructive\") & (\"default\" | \"info\")` is `\"default\"`), is required when either member requires it, and lists both declarations. An interface's own declaration still replaces the one it extends.\n11\t- **In Full mode, a prop beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` also has the element attribute's type:** recharts' `onTimeUpdate` next to a div's attributes is `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>` intersected with recharts' handler. Curated mode does not read React's declarations, so there the prop keeps the other member's type.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
