{"parentUuid":"76aa07ae-c7a9-4177-83d2-c262bb742bb3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ba9ae519-62e2-4faf-a305-57eaf7b43c38","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:00:33.595Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/decisions-0.4","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"a51b84971102d2563174d3dfdf84b6b5e668da47c13b7e5f1154d3bee24d8b19","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Note: /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.changeset/intersection-props-intersect.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n3\tcargo/caliper-docgen: patch\n4\tcargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\n5\tnpm/caliper-docgen: patch\n6\tnpm/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\n7\tnpm/caliper-docgen-vite-plugin: patch\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t- **A prop two intersection members declare has both types:** `A & B` used to keep whichever member declared a prop first, dropping the other declaration. As in TypeScript, the prop now has the intersection of both types (literal unions reduce to their common values, so `(\"default\" | \"destructive\") & (\"default\" | \"info\")` is `\"default\"`), is required when either member requires it, and lists both declarations. An interface's own declaration still replaces the one it extends.\n11\t- **In Full mode, a prop beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` also has the element attribute's type:** recharts' `onTimeUpdate` next to a div's attributes is `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement>` intersected with recharts' handler. Curated mode does not read React's declarations, so there the prop keeps the other member's type.\n\n<total_tokens>14872451 tokens left</total_tokens>\n\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."}]}}
