{"parentUuid":"d5dc8dfd-b5c8-46c2-a770-988d4e2b9e65","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKmTnM3F85a6fA4hhyAQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both branches are pushed. Opening the two PRs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2062,"cache_read_input_tokens":427439,"output_tokens":1670,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2062,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1670,"cache_read_input_tokens":427439,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2062},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a25878f-d01f-4da9-9333-b7a2206c5512","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgKmTmwUvxNA57MRVZ15z","requestRef":"4f19df8a-36e3-4d5f-85c3-bbb942fd45fc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"adr","type":"assistant","uuid":"232d8e74-1515-41d0-95a6-08ff903bca25","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:03:38.920Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/curated-react-attributes","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"232d8e74-1515-41d0-95a6-08ff903bca25","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKmTnM3F85a6fA4hhyAQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WpNJPoBEjV4cnZJRedMwvq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr-quotes.md","content":"## Why\n\nStorybook's React docgen and react-docgen-typescript print a string default as its source text (`'md'`). We rewrote every string default with double quotes, which was the main remaining argTypes mismatch with React's docgen in the Storybook comparison (5 of the 7 differences).\n\n## What\n\n- A string-literal default keeps its source text, quotes included, like array and object literals already did. `\"neutral\"` and `` `Go` `` keep theirs too.\n- Every output format changes, so the changeset is `minor`.\n- No `.d.ts` cache bump: parameter defaults only exist in runtime source, which the cache never holds.\n\n## Effect (five corpora with dependencies installed, before = main)\n\n| Corpus | Defaults changed |\n| --- | ---: |\n| mantine | 18 |\n| spectrum | 12 |\n| chakra, shadcn, antd | 0 (they write double quotes) |\n\nProp names and types unchanged. The `rdt_compat` snapshot changes in its three single-quoted defaults only.\n\n## Verify\n\n- `extractor::tests::string_defaults_keep_their_source_quotes`: exact `'md'`, `\"neutral\"` and `` `Go` `` (computed).\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace` (771 pass), `just test-ts`, `just test-integration` (the Vite plugin and Storybook provider now expect `'primary'`), `just lint doc-check typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2062,"cache_read_input_tokens":427439,"output_tokens":1670,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2062,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1670,"cache_read_input_tokens":427439,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2062},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WpNJPoBEjV4cnZJRedMwvq":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr-quotes.md","content":"## Why\n\nStorybook's React docgen and react-docgen-typescript print a string default as its source text (`'md'`). We rewrote every string default with double quotes, which was the main remaining argTypes mismatch with React's docgen in the Storybook comparison (5 of the 7 differences).\n\n## What\n\n- A string-literal default keeps its source text, quotes included, like array and object literals already did. `\"neutral\"` and `` `Go` `` keep theirs too.\n- Every output format changes, so the changeset is `minor`.\n- No `.d.ts` cache bump: parameter defaults only exist in runtime source, which the cache never holds.\n\n## Effect (five corpora with dependencies installed, before = main)\n\n| Corpus | Defaults changed |\n| --- | ---: |\n| mantine | 18 |\n| spectrum | 12 |\n| chakra, shadcn, antd | 0 (they write double quotes) |\n\nProp names and types unchanged. The `rdt_compat` snapshot changes in its three single-quoted defaults only.\n\n## Verify\n\n- `extractor::tests::string_defaults_keep_their_source_quotes`: exact `'md'`, `\"neutral\"` and `` `Go` `` (computed).\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace` (771 pass), `just test-ts`, `just test-integration` (the Vite plugin and Storybook provider now expect `'primary'`), `just lint doc-check typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a25878f-d01f-4da9-9333-b7a2206c5512","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_01