{"parentUuid":"bb0b87b3-e6f7-4f14-b649-e90451877310","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Write","toolUseID":"toolu_01WpNJPoBEjV4cnZJRedMwvq","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":53},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bddd79f4-b0ed-4cf4-b42b-a9318963ea4f","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:03:44.413Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/curated-react-attributes","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"bddd79f4-b0ed-4cf4-b42b-a9318963ea4f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKmTnM3F85a6fA4hhyAQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018A9jZZ6qofP3kRiskaGeC8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr-curated.md","content":"Stacked on #127.\n\n## Why\n\n#122 made a prop that two intersection members declare have both types, including an HTML layer's attribute: recharts' `onTimeUpdate` beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` is the DOM handler intersected with recharts' handler. That only worked in Full mode, the one that merges `@types/react`. Curated mode, the default for the CLI, the Vite plugin and Storybook, still showed recharts' type alone.\n\n## What\n\n- **ADR 0013:** in curated mode the cold run parses `@types/react` (through the parse cache) into its own `NamedTypeIndex`. Only the HTML-layer attribute lookup (`resolver/html.rs`, through `ResolutionContext::react_index`) reads it; it is not a lookup fallback, so no other name resolves against React's declarations. Full mode is unchanged, and `none` mode and the dependency loader don't read React.\n- The index is built once per session and carried into every watch revision.\n- In curated mode the attribute keeps its alias name: `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement> & ((data: unknown, index: number) => void)`.\n- `docs/STATUS.md`: `--load-dependencies` becomes the default in 0.5.0 once checked against RDT on the 20 fixture libraries (agreed in review).\n\n## Effect (five corpora with dependencies installed, before = #127)\n\n| Corpus | Props changed | Wall time (best of 5) |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| shadcn | 7 (`ChartContainer.children` now also has React's `children`) | 72 → 69 ms |\n| mantine, chakra, antd, spectrum | 0 | within noise |\n\nFixture snapshots change only in `dtsFilesParsed` (+1, React's declaration file).\n\n## Verify\n\n- `pipeline::tests::a_prop_beside_an_html_layer_also_has_the_elements_attribute_type_in_full_and_curated_mode`: exact type text and declaration list for `Legend`, `Flipped` and `Omitted` in both modes.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace` (771 pass), `just test-ts`, `just test-integration`, `just lint doc-check typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2062,"cache_read_input_tokens":427439,"output_tokens":1670,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2062,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1670,"cache_read_input_tokens":427439,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2062},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018A9jZZ6qofP3kRiskaGeC8":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr-curated.md","content":"Stacked on #127.\n\n## Why\n\n#122 made a prop that two intersection members declare have both types, including an HTML layer's attribute: recharts' `onTimeUpdate` beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` is the DOM handler intersected with recharts' handler. That only worked in Full mode, the one that merges `@types/react`. Curated mode, the default for the CLI, the Vite plugin and Storybook, still showed recharts' type alone.\n\n## What\n\n- **ADR 0013:** in curated mode the cold run parses `@types/react` (through the parse cache) into its own `NamedTypeIndex`. Only the HTML-layer attribute lookup (`resolver/html.rs`, through `ResolutionContext::react_index`) reads it; it is not a lookup fallback, so no other name resolves against React's declarations. Full mode is unchanged, and `none` mode and the dependency loader don't read React.\n- The index is built once per session and carried into every watch revision.\n- In curated mode the attribute keeps its alias name: `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement> & ((data: unknown, index: number) => void)`.\n- `docs/STATUS.md`: `--load-dependencies` becomes the default in 0.5.0 once checked against RDT on the 20 fixture libraries (agreed in review).\n\n## Effect (five corpora with dependencies installed, before = #127)\n\n| Corpus | Props changed | Wall time (best of 5) |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| shadcn | 7 (`ChartContainer.children` now also has React's `children`) | 72 → 69 ms |\n| mantine, chakra, antd, spectrum | 0 | within noise |\n\nFixture snapshots change only in `dtsFilesParsed` (+1, React's declaration file).\n\n## Verify\n\n- `pipeline::tests::a_prop_beside_an_html_layer_also_has_the_elements_attribute_type_in_full_and_curated_mode`: exact type text and declaration list for `Legend`, `Flipped` and `Omitted` in both modes.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace` (771 pass), `just test-ts`, `just test-integration`, `just lint doc-check typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7a25878f-d01f-4da9-9333-b7a2206c5512","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgKmTmwUvxNA57MRVZ15z","requestRef":"4f19df8a-36e3-4d5f-85c3-bbb942fd45fc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"adr","type":"assistant","uuid":"f5c6c9d2-0dd3-4274-915d-54f9cab38605","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:03:51.541Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/curated-react-attributes","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
