{"parentUuid":"9547ddc4-4b7a-4017-a2fc-8d2fc9fe097c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14852526 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4a6e9a96-ab92-48fb-8704-1dfc6ccb49a2","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:03:57.119Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14852526 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/curated-react-attributes","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"4a6e9a96-ab92-48fb-8704-1dfc6ccb49a2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Concise","turnReminder":"Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"805d1755-253b-438e-8d20-03d0c025952d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:03:57.121Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/curated-react-attributes","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"81f14576217e1526bfec297c896a69622687e71d556db19b3f44e7290b30ff1c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both branches are pushed. Opening the two PRs."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WpNJPoBEjV4cnZJRedMwvq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr-quotes.md","content":"## Why\n\nStorybook's React docgen and react-docgen-typescript print a string default as its source text (`'md'`). We rewrote every string default with double quotes, which was the main remaining argTypes mismatch with React's docgen in the Storybook comparison (5 of the 7 differences).\n\n## What\n\n- A string-literal default keeps its source text, quotes included, like array and object literals already did. `\"neutral\"` and `` `Go` `` keep theirs too.\n- Every output format changes, so the changeset is `minor`.\n- No `.d.ts` cache bump: parameter defaults only exist in runtime source, which the cache never holds.\n\n## Effect (five corpora with dependencies installed, before = main)\n\n| Corpus | Defaults changed |\n| --- | ---: |\n| mantine | 18 |\n| spectrum | 12 |\n| chakra, shadcn, antd | 0 (they write double quotes) |\n\nProp names and types unchanged. The `rdt_compat` snapshot changes in its three single-quoted defaults only.\n\n## Verify\n\n- `extractor::tests::string_defaults_keep_their_source_quotes`: exact `'md'`, `\"neutral\"` and `` `Go` `` (computed).\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace` (771 pass), `just test-ts`, `just test-integration` (the Vite plugin and Storybook provider now expect `'primary'`), `just lint doc-check typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018A9jZZ6qofP3kRiskaGeC8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr-curated.md","content":"Stacked on #127.\n\n## Why\n\n#122 made a prop that two intersection members declare have both types, including an HTML layer's attribute: recharts' `onTimeUpdate` beside `ComponentProps<\"div\">` is the DOM handler intersected with recharts' handler. That only worked in Full mode, the one that merges `@types/react`. Curated mode, the default for the CLI, the Vite plugin and Storybook, still showed recharts' type alone.\n\n## What\n\n- **ADR 0013:** in curated mode the cold run parses `@types/react` (through the parse cache) into its own `NamedTypeIndex`. Only the HTML-layer attribute lookup (`resolver/html.rs`, through `ResolutionContext::react_index`) reads it; it is not a lookup fallback, so no other name resolves against React's declarations. Full mode is unchanged, and `none` mode and the dependency loader don't read React.\n- The index is built once per session and carried into every watch revision.\n- In curated mode the attribute keeps its alias name: `ReactEventHandler<HTMLDivElement> & ((data: unknown, index: number) => void)`.\n- `docs/STATUS.md`: `--load-dependencies` becomes the default in 0.5.0 once checked against RDT on the 20 fixture libraries (agreed in review).\n\n## Effect (five corpora with dependencies installed, before = #127)\n\n| Corpus | Props changed | Wall time (best of 5) |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| shadcn | 7 (`ChartContainer.children` now also has React's `children`) | 72 → 69 ms |\n| mantine, chakra, antd, spectrum | 0 | within noise |\n\nFixture snapshots change only in `dtsFilesParsed` (+1, React's declaration file).\n\n## Verify\n\n- `pipeline::tests::a_prop_beside_an_html_layer_also_has_the_elements_attribute_type_in_full_and_curated_mode`: exact type text and declaration list for `Legend`, `Flipped` and `Omitted` in both modes.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace` (771 pass), `just test-ts`, `just test-integration`, `just lint doc-check typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015CdhCpfXgmdUuyHaJu9fB9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr create --base main --head feat/string-defaults-keep-quotes --title \"feat: keep string defaults' source quotes\" --body-file /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr-quotes.md","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
