{"parentUuid":"107bbe95-e32d-4124-be7b-d4294c4b0512","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B3fVi6pxtWxmU5B1aXmYP4","type":"tool_result","content":"14\tuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n15\tuse std::hash::Hasher;\n16\t\n17\tuse crate::types::{Diagnostic, DiagnosticCode, DiagnosticSeverity, SourceData};\n18\t\n19\t/// Bump this whenever `SourceData`'s field list or field order changes.\n20\t/// Serialization is via plain `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice` — MessagePack's\n21\t/// *positional* (not named-map) struct encoding — so inserting a field\n22\t/// anywhere but the very end shifts every subsequent field's decode position\n23\t/// for any cache entry written before the change. A same-shaped field\n24\t/// addition (e.g. another `FxHashMap<String, Vec<X>>`) wouldn't even fail\n25\t/// loudly; it would decode as plausible-looking but wrong data. `const_arrays`\n26\t/// (added mid-struct, not appended) is exactly this case — this bump covers it.\n27\t/// Also bumped for the mtime+size -> content-hash key change (P0-2 fix):\n28\t/// `SerializableCacheKey`'s own shape changed, so pre-existing on-disk cache\n29\t/// files must be discarded rather than misread under the new field layout.\n30\t/// Extractor changes that keep the shape are covered by `CacheHeader::fingerprint` instead.\n31\t/// 16: `LexedExport::LocalDeclaration` gained `declared_as`.\n32\t/// 17: component mappings record whether they are exported.\n33\tconst CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION: u32 = 17;\n34\t\n35\tconst DATA_FILE: &str = \"dts.msgpack\";"}]},"uuid":"d20c809f-4d2d-46a1-b044-c7788e76dd89","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:07:03.398Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/core/src/cache.rs","content":"use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse std::hash::Hasher;\n\nuse crate::types::{Diagnostic, DiagnosticCode, DiagnosticSeverity, SourceData};\n\n/// Bump this whenever `SourceData`'s field list or field order changes.\n/// Serialization is via plain `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice` — MessagePack's\n/// *positional* (not named-map) struct encoding — so inserting a field\n/// anywhere but the very end shifts every subsequent field's decode position\n/// for any cache entry written before the change. A same-shaped field\n/// addition (e.g. another `FxHashMap<String, Vec<X>>`) wouldn't even fail\n/// loudly; it would decode as plausible-looking but wrong data. `const_arrays`\n/// (added mid-struct, not appended) is exactly this case — this bump covers it.\n/// Also bumped for the mtime+size -> content-hash key change (P0-2 fix):\n/// `SerializableCacheKey`'s own shape changed, so pre-existing on-disk cache\n/// files must be discarded rather than misread under the new field layout.\n/// Extractor changes that keep the shape are covered by `CacheHeader::fingerprint` instead.\n/// 16: `LexedExport::LocalDeclaration` gained `declared_as`.\n/// 17: component mappings record whether they are exported.\nconst CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION: u32 = 17;\n\nconst DATA_FILE: &str = \"dts.msgpack\";","numLines":22,"startLine":14,"totalLines":697}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"107bbe95-e32d-4124-be7b-d4294c4b0512","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"test/signal-after-watcher-ready","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
