{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"361101ce3eba66f5115a11f6cc910e10426c854fec489a2ffa531f51f8f5a71c","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QrPHgh2LgQWNnfuE6WTu1g","type":"tool_result","content":"770\t    /// `const Button = (props: Props) => ...` or `const Button = function (props: Props) {}`: a PascalCase binding\n771\t    /// whose initializer is a synchronous function with a props-typed first parameter.\n772\t    TypedFunctionExpression,\n773\t    /// `const Button = wrapper<ButtonFactory>(...)` or `wrapper<El, ButtonProps>(...)`: a generic call whose type\n774\t    /// arguments carry the props type, chosen by shape from declarations in the same file.\n775\t    WrapperTypeArgument,\n776\t}\n777\t\n778\t/// A component → prop type mapping.\n779\t#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]\n780\tpub struct ComponentMapping {\n781\t    pub component_name: std::string::String,\n782\t    pub props_type_name: TypeName,\n783\t    pub props_type_args: Vec<CollectedType>,\n784\t    pub file_path: Utf8PathBuf,\n785\t    pub description: std::string::String,\n786\t    pub tags: BTreeMap<std::string::String, std::string::String>,\n787\t    /// Byte span for diagnostics\n788\t    pub span_start: u32,\n789\t    pub span_end: u32,\n790\t    /// Default values extracted from parameter destructuring or defaultProps.\n791\t    /// Key = prop name. Populated only for implementation files (.tsx/.ts), not .d.ts.\n792\t    pub param_defaults: FxHashMap<std::string::String, RawDefault>,\n793\t    /// Which extractor rule matched.\n794\t    pub rule: DetectionRule,\n795\t    /// Whether its module exports it, directly or as a sub-component attached to an exported component.\n796\t    pub exported: bool,\n797\t}\n798\t\n799\timpl ComponentMapping {\n800\t    /// A mapping with no type arguments, documentation or parameter defaults; add them with the `with_*` methods.\n801\t    pub fn new(\n802\t        component_name: std::string::String,\n803\t        props_type_name: TypeName,\n804\t        file_path: Utf8PathBuf,\n805\t        span_start: u32,\n806\t        span_end: u32,\n807\t        rule: DetectionRule,\n808\t    ) -> Self {\n809\t        Self {\n810\t            component_name,\n811\t            props_type_name,\n812\t            props_type_args: Vec::new(),\n813\t            file_path,\n814\t            description: std::string::String::new(),\n815\t            tags: BTreeMap::new(),\n816\t            span_start,\n817\t            span_end,\n818\t            param_defaults: FxHashMap::default(),\n819\t            rule,\n820\t            exported: false,\n821\t        }\n822\t    }\n823\t\n824\t    #[must_use]\n825\t    pub fn with_props_type_args(mut self, props_type_args: Vec<CollectedType>) -> Self {\n826\t        self.props_type_args = props_type_args;\n827\t        self\n828\t    }\n829\t\n830\t    #[must_use]\n831\t    pub fn with_doc(\n832\t        mut self,\n833\t        description: std::string::String,\n834\t        tags: BTreeMap<std::string::String, std::string::String>,\n835\t    ) -> Self {\n836\t        self.description = description;\n837\t        self.tags = tags;\n838\t        self\n839\t    }\n840\t\n841\t    #[must_use]\n842\t    pub fn with_param_defaults(mut self, param_defaults: FxHashMap<std::string::String, RawDefault>) -> Self {\n843\t        self.param_defaults = param_defaults;\n844\t        self\n845\t    }\n846\t}\n847\t\n848\t// ─── Import/Export Types ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n849\t"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TfKzu5kxRMvsg67DXGF3WH","type":"tool_result","content":"576\t    pub const_arrays: FxHashMap<std::string::String, Vec<EnumValue>>,\n577\t\n578\t    /// Component → prop type mappings found in this file.\n579\t    /// Only populated for .tsx files.\n580\t    pub component_mappings: Vec<ComponentMapping>,\n581\t\n582\t    /// Import bindings in this file — local name → source\n583\t    pub imports: Vec<ImportBinding>,\n584\t\n585\t    /// Re-exports from this file\n586\t    pub exports: Vec<LexedExport>,\n587\t\n588\t    /// Non-fatal issues discovered while parsing this file (e.g. excessive nesting,\n589\t    /// TypeScript syntax errors). Drained into the pipeline's top-level diagnostics\n590\t    /// during `GlobalSourceData` merge — never dropped silently.\n591\t    pub diagnostics: Vec<Diagnostic>,\n592\t}\n593\t\n594\t/// A collected interface declaration.\n595\t#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]"},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B3fVi6pxtWxmU5B1aXmYP4","type":"tool_result","content":"14\tuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n15\tuse std::hash::Hasher;\n16\t\n17\tuse crate::types::{Diagnostic, DiagnosticCode, DiagnosticSeverity, SourceData};\n18\t\n19\t/// Bump this whenever `SourceData`'s field list or field order changes.\n20\t/// Serialization is via plain `rmp_serde::to_vec`/`from_slice` — MessagePack's\n21\t/// *positional* (not named-map) struct encoding — so inserting a field\n22\t/// anywhere but the very end shifts every subsequent field's decode position\n23\t/// for any cache entry written before the change. A same-shaped field\n24\t/// addition (e.g. another `FxHashMap<String, Vec<X>>`) wouldn't even fail\n25\t/// loudly; it would decode as plausible-looking but wrong data. `const_arrays`\n26\t/// (added mid-struct, not appended) is exactly this case — this bump covers it.\n27\t/// Also bumped for the mtime+size -> content-hash key change (P0-2 fix):\n28\t/// `SerializableCacheKey`'s own shape changed, so pre-existing on-disk cache\n29\t/// files must be discarded rather than misread under the new field layout.\n30\t/// Extractor changes that keep the shape are covered by `CacheHeader::fingerprint` instead.\n31\t/// 16: `LexedExport::LocalDeclaration` gained `declared_as`.\n32\t/// 17: component mappings record whether they are exported.\n33\tconst CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION: u32 = 17;\n34\t\n35\tconst DATA_FILE: &str = \"dts.msgpack\";"}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"7730ba1d0a476c9a6c5dd7a689db539d351574a96696b62792fb62fe83041e16","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable.\n\n\nHere are the existing tasks:\n\n#1. [completed] Detection precision: render evidence, non-destructive renames, wrapper evidence\n#2. [completed] Type-text P0s: quoted substitution, Infinity/NaN, Required extends, key sets, typeof props, generic alias in prop, cache bump\n#3. [completed] Discovery and small correctness: relative excludes, export-default misses, Required unwrap, PropsWithChildren children\n#4. [completed] Watch revision model shared with cold path, Vite plugin and CLI watch fixes\n#5. [completed] Diagnostics identity and dedup, resolution memoization, cache fingerprint\n#6. [completed] Docs, DX and ADR 0007 amendment; restate #64 figures\n#7. [pending] Replace name-based special cases with structural rules\n#8. [completed] Delta contract: every changed key and diagnostic in IncrementalUpdate\n#9. [completed] Symbol precedence: resolve the binding before builtin or utility names\n#10. [completed] Render evidence: count only returned JSX and resolved element types; precision gate\n#11. [completed] Silent degradations: tsconfig parsing, RenderProps shortcut, cache size bound\n#12. [completed] Interned props: ADR 0009\n#13. [completed] Interned props: Rust serialization\n#14. [completed] Interned props: JS consumers and docs\n#15. [completed] Prove dependency loading: stage 1 loader prototype\n#16. [completed] Prove dependency loading: stage 2 end-to-end on an experimental branch\n#17. [completed] Dependency types 1: resolver groundwork PR\n#18. [completed] Dependency types 2: namespace re-exports\n#19. [completed] Dependency types 3: share resolved props in memory\n#20. [completed] Dependency types 4: type-text fixes\n#21. [completed] Dependency types 5: loader + dependency layer behind a flag, with ADRs\n#22. [completed] Replace trybuild compile_fail test with a doctest pair\n#23. [completed] ComponentProps<typeof X> resolves to X's props\n#24. [completed] Investigate failing Dependabot PR #84\n#25. [completed] Track A: precision and detection PR chain\n#26. [completed] Track B: Storybook integration PR chain\n#27. [completed] Track C: hardening, gates and docs PR chain\n#28. [completed] Fix macOS flake in a_signal_restores_the_terminal_mode_the_session_changed\n#29. [completed] Record the agreed decisions (load-deps default plan, collapse default, ADR 0010 amendment, quote style)\n#30. [in_progress] Wrapper components: props from the callee's result type (Mantine component/renderRoot), recipe variant props, opaque factories\n\n<total_tokens>14816873 tokens left</total_tokens>\n\nConcise output style is active. Be concise: lead with the result, skip preamble and narration, keep only what the user needs."}]}}
