{"parentUuid":"866ccaf1-51df-4314-9a71-f7e5bb9e2d45","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dhaagkmhi5gebkWvVWLLP9","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/architecture/extractor-ast-visiting.md:62:- **`try_rename_identifier_wrapped_component` matches two distinct real-world shapes with one function**, not two: a call-wrapped rename (`export let X = someLibraryWrapper(InnerFn) as Y` — Headless UI's `forwardRefWithAs`) and a bare passthrough (`const Button = InternalButton;` — antd's pattern). Both reduce to \"an identifier reference to an already-collected mapping, optionally wrapped in a recognized-but-uninterpreted call.\" Splitting these into separate functions was considered unnecessary since the resolution logic (clone-and-rename, track `aliased_away`) is identical either way.\ndocs/architecture/types-and-output-contract.md:234:`detected_by` (`detectedBy` in JSON) is the extractor rule that recognized the component, so a consumer can tell an explicit declaration form (`functionDeclaration`, `forwardRef`, `fcAnnotation`, `classComponent`, ...) from an inference (`typedFunctionExpression`, `wrapperTypeArgument`). It is the grouping the per-rule precision sample uses (`docs/precision.md`).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f345cce4-4dbd-42f0-b44b-e87240ddf774","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:19:42.535Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/architecture/extractor-ast-visiting.md:62:- **`try_rename_identifier_wrapped_component` matches two distinct real-world shapes with one function**, not two: a call-wrapped rename (`export let X = someLibraryWrapper(InnerFn) as Y` — Headless UI's `forwardRefWithAs`) and a bare passthrough (`const Button = InternalButton;` — antd's pattern). Both reduce to \"an identifier reference to an already-collected mapping, optionally wrapped in a recognized-but-uninterpreted call.\" Splitting these into separate functions was considered unnecessary since