{"parentUuid":"2b9a4c3d-ad7a-4273-a773-46f766f19a23","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKnhBwaZqiAfUjs4as9Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VHuf8PKKUQzKD5GmnZ3nHJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md","offset":29,"limit":16},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425,"cache_read_input_tokens":569505,"output_tokens":142,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":425,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":142,"cache_read_input_tokens":569505,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":425},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VHuf8PKKUQzKD5GmnZ3nHJ":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md","offset":29,"limit":16}},"serverClassifierRequest":"33c8b722-8261-4a01-a458-cbc71f8dbb82","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgKnhBVoZZ93ttimyqGuu","requestRef":"5322e2f1-9b23-4b2e-8e15-2494548acf11","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"adr","type":"assistant","uuid":"b70a834e-18ce-4ad2-8154-46266c6bc059","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:19:48.638Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/wrapper-callee-result","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"b70a834e-18ce-4ad2-8154-46266c6bc059","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VHuf8PKKUQzKD5GmnZ3nHJ","type":"tool_result","content":"29\t## Dependency declarations (`load_dependencies`, ADR 0010)\n30\t\n31\tWith `PipelineOptions::load_dependencies`, `ResolutionContext::with_dependencies` attaches the run's `DependencyLayer` (`dependency_types.rs`). The resolver reads it only through fallbacks, so every lookup the project's own data answers is unchanged:\n32\t\n33\t- **Import map and named-type index:** a file the project's maps don't hold is looked up in the layer's (`ImportResolutionMap::fallback`, `NamedTypeIndex::fallback`).\n34\t- **Re-exports:** `follow_reexports` takes the loader's answer for a `(module, name)` it walked, instead of walking the package's stubs again; a module with no answer is walked as before.\n35\t- **Precedence:** a project declaration, then a known shortcut, then the dependency's own declaration, then a builtin. `resolve_source_defined_or_known` checks `resolve_known` first for a name declared in a dependency file, because the shortcuts (cva's `VariantProps`, MUI's `SxProps`) stand in for conditional or mapped types this resolver can't expand.\n36\t- **Value index:** `ComponentProps<typeof X>` and `typeof X` in `extends` find a dependency component through `DependencyLayer::component`. Dependency components and enums live only in the layer's `GlobalSourceData`, so they never reach output or the bare-name indexes.\n37\t- **Diagnostics:** a type the loader could not find says why in the help of \"Cannot resolve type\" (`unresolved_type_help`): the module did not resolve, resolved to JavaScript without types, or does not export the name.\n38\t\n39\t- **Collapse** (`collapse_inherited_props`, ADR 0012): `ctx.collapses` records an inherited source declaring more than 30 props as an `InheritedLayer` (no `html_element`, `total_props` = its declared count) and resolves only its notable members (`notable_html_attrs`' element-independent list) into `notable_inherited`. Sources are an interface's own members and an object-literal alias; an interface's parents are sources of their own. Never at depth 0 (the component's own props type), and never while `ResolveState::expand_all` is set: `Pick`'s base and `keyof` operands select or count props by name. `Dependencies` (default) collapses loaded dependency files only; `All` adds every file outside `node_modules`, so React's and TypeScript's declarations stay with `html_attributes`. Interface-chain recordings are keyed on `expand_all` too.\n40\t\n41\t**Invariant:** never merge layer data into the project's `GlobalSourceData`; that would emit dependency components and enums and let dependency names shadow project names in bare-name lookups.\n42\t\n43\t## The three-tier data model this resolver operates on\n44\t"}]},"uuid":"117dddeb-34b2-4758-a146-098e88ba9754","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:19:48.722Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md","content":"## Dependency declarations (`load_dependencies`, ADR 0010)\n\nWith `PipelineOptions::load_dependencies`, `ResolutionContext::with_dependencies` attaches the run's `DependencyLayer` (`dependency_types.rs`). The resolver reads it only through fallbacks, so every lookup the project's own data answers is unchanged:\n\n- **Import map and named-type index:** a file the project's maps don't hold is looked up in the layer's (`ImportResolutionMap::fallback`, `NamedTypeIndex::fallback`).\n- **Re-exports:** `follow_reexports` takes the loader's answer for a `(module, name)` it walked, instead of walking the package's stubs again; a module with no answer is walked as before.\n- **Precedence:** a project declaration, then a known shortcut, then the dependency's own declaration, then a builtin. `resolve_source_defined_or_known` checks `resolve_known` first for a name declared in a dependency file, because the shortcuts (cva's `VariantProps`, MUI's `SxProps`) stand in for conditional or mapped types this resolver can't expand.\n- **Value index:** `ComponentProps<typeof X>` and `typeof X` in `extends` find a dependency component through `DependencyLayer::component`. Dependency components and enums live only in the layer's `GlobalSourceData`, so they never reach output or the bare-name indexes.\n- **Diagnostics:** a type the loader could not find says why in the help of \"Cannot resolve type\" (`unresolved_type_help`): the module did not resolve, resolved to JavaScript without types, or does not export the name.\n\n- **Collapse** (`collapse_inherited_props`, ADR 0012): `ctx.collapses` records an inherited source declaring more than 30 props as an `InheritedLayer` (no `html_element`, `total_props` = its declared count) and resolves only its notable members (`notable_html_attrs`' element-independent list) into `notable_inherited`. Sources are an interface's own members and an object-literal alias; an interface's parents are sources of their own. Never at depth 0 (the component's own props type), and never while `ResolveState::expand_all` is set: `Pick`'s base and `keyof` operands select or count props by name. `Dependencies` (default) collapses loaded dependency files only; `All` adds every file outside `node_modules`, so React's and TypeScript's declarations stay with `html_attributes`. Interface-chain recordings are keyed on `expand_all` too.\n\n**Invariant:** never merge layer data into the project's `GlobalSourceData`; that would emit dependency components and enums and let dependency names shadow project names in bare-name lookups.\n\n## The three-tier data model this resolver operates on\n","numLines":16,"startLine":29,"totalLines":129}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b70a834e-18ce-4ad2-8154-46266c6bc059","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/wrapper-callee-result","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
