{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"bf20a66c-881d-4e7b-8502-492f7228ac5c","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:19:48.827Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"0b6896854d006f4d8f425f18d704c237f040ff80238d5f9ef57b18ed3f82cd87","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"5322e2f1-9b23-4b2e-8e15-2494548acf11","keep":866,"tail":["dd78255cecb6ef9595ec0f987635576e668b466c7af5bec29545053f15d4850a","c04f66ecb4e7a5c7010706bc11222974fecb75b39b6b32849286d74a3d3eb425","abd07f13a90bb293aae238ed9ab00f686a3c7749dca95c4be164722d47f8af10"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",868,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"be3181d459ff52680d52d406995487a04f0fe48f71c5501bb915e683c52deb1a"}
{"parentUuid":"1adfc836-0243-415d-836e-1b035074cbd7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKnhM7FHEvWX2GMnfoUq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QCpBZgek5cnMMVJG7VxfZE","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md","old_string":"## The three-tier data model this resolver operates on\n","new_string":"## Wrapper callees (`resolver/callee.rs`)\n\nA `wrapperTypeArgument` component's props come from the type argument the extractor selected (`extractor/wrapper.rs`), plus what its callee's result type adds. The extractor records every generic function's result in `SourceData::function_results`: the return annotation, or the type its only top-level `return … as T` asserts. `callee::result_props` binds the callee's type parameters to the call's type arguments, follows aliases to the first React component type (`NamedExoticComponent<P>`, `FC<P>`, a call signature, …) and adds P's inline object members (`{ component?: any; renderRoot?: … }`) that the component doesn't already have. Other members of P (`Payload['props']`, `RefAttributes<…>`) are left to the selection, so this never warns. The callee's file is a recorded dependency, so editing the factory re-resolves the components it builds; `follow_reexports` treats a recorded function as a declaration, so `export *` barrels reach it.\n\n**Gap:** a result type asserted through an alias declared inside the function body (Mantine's `polymorphicFactory`) is not reachable.\n\n## The three-tier data model this resolver operates on\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_read_input_tokens":569930,"output_tokens":1122,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1161,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1122,"cache_read_input_tokens":569930,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1161},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QCpBZgek5cnMMVJG7VxfZE":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md","old_string":"## The three-tier data model this resolver operates on\n","new_string":"## Wrapper callees (`resolver/callee.rs`)\n\nA `wrapperTypeArgument` component's props come from the type argument the extractor selected (`extractor/wrapper.rs`), plus what its callee's result type adds. The extractor records every generic function's result in `SourceData::function_results`: the return annotation, or the type its only top-level `return … as T` asserts. `callee::result_props` binds the callee's type parameters to the call's type arguments, follows aliases to the first React component type (`NamedExoticComponent<P>`, `FC<P>`, a call signature, …) and adds P's inline object members (`{ component?: any; renderRoot?: … }`) that the component doesn't already have. Other members of P (`Payload['props']`, `RefAttributes<…>`) are left to the selection, so this never warns. The callee's file is a recorded dependency, so editing the factory re-resolves the components it builds; `follow_reexports` treats a recorded function as a declaration, so `export *` barrels reach it.\n\n**Gap:** a result type asserted through an alias declared inside the function body (Mantine's `polymorphicFactory`) is not reachable.\n\n## The three-tier data model this resolver operates on\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c2cdb7f0-9ca3-4a27-adae-856acc0fbca9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgKnhLfhiwqdXjEmwSjWz","requestRef":"bf20a66c-881d-4e7b-8502-492f7228ac5c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"adr","type":"assistant","uuid":"c56ee074-e080-4d0a-9b67-aa7030f40558","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:19:54.578Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/wrapper-callee-result","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"c56ee074-e080-4d0a-9b67-aa7030f40558","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKnhM7FHEvWX2GMnfoUq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q5ig7UPrDEhj5f7kQHkaoc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.changeset/wrapper-callee-result-props.md","content":"---\ncargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-vite-plugin: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-storybook: patch\n---\n\n**A wrapper-built component gets the props its factory's result type adds:** `const Button = factory<ButtonFactory>(…)` now also lists the props the type `factory` returns declares beyond the payload, such as Mantine's `component` and `renderRoot`, as react-docgen-typescript does. The factory may be reached through `export *` barrels, and editing it updates the components it builds in watch mode. On Mantine's core package, 360 missing props are now reported.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_read_input_tokens":569930,"output_tokens":1122,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1161,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1122,"cache_read_input_tokens":569930,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1161,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1161},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Q5ig7UPrDEhj5f7kQHkaoc":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.changeset/wrapper-callee-result-props.md","content":"---\ncargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-vite-plugin: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-storybook: patch\n---\n\n**A wrapper-built component gets the props its factory's result type adds:** `const Button = factory<ButtonFactory>(…)` now also lists the props the type `factory` returns declares beyond the payload, such as Mantine's `component` and `renderRoot`, as react-docgen-typescript does. The factory may be reached through `export *` barrels, and editing it updates the components it builds in watch mode. On Mantine's core package, 360 missing props are now reported.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c2cdb7f0-9ca3-4a27-adae-856acc0fbca9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgKnhLfhiwqdXjEmwSjWz","requestRef":"bf20a66c-881d-4e7b-8502-492f7228ac5c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"adr","type":"assistant","uuid":"fdf60ec0-d9c2-4d4e-94b4-1e82cb671494","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:19:57.537Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/wrapper-callee-result","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
