sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/wrapper-callee-result","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"c56ee074-e080-4d0a-9b67-aa7030f40558","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d29d37d1-42a9-4a91-986a-e0277a3cbad8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QCpBZgek5cnMMVJG7VxfZE","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"2a8edc8a-d78c-4853-8d67-0f1eb393c0ee","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:19:58.875Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md","oldString":"## The three-tier data model this resolver operates on\n","newString":"## Wrapper callees (`resolver/callee.rs`)\n\nA `wrapperTypeArgument` component's props come from the type argument the extractor selected (`extractor/wrapper.rs`), plus what its callee's result type adds. The extractor records every generic function's result in `SourceData::function_results`: the return annotation, or the type its only top-level `return … as T` asserts. `callee::result_props` binds the callee's type parameters to the call's type arguments, follows aliases to the first React component type (`NamedExoticComponent<P>`, `FC<P>`, a call signature, …) and adds P's inline object members (`{ component?: any; renderRoot?: … }`) that the component doesn't already have. Other members of P (`Payload['props']`, `RefAttributes<…>`) are left to the selection, so this never warns. The callee's file is a recorded dependency, so editing the factory re-resolves the components it builds; `follow_reexports` treats a recorded function as a declaration, so `export *` barrels reach it.\n\n**Gap:** a result type asserted through an alias declared inside the function body (Mantine's `polymorphicFactory`) is not reachable.\n\n## The three-tier data model this resolver operates on\n","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":40,"oldLines":6,"newStart":40,"newLines":12,"lines":[" "," **Invariant:** never merge layer data into the project's `GlobalSourceData`; that would emit dependency components and enums and let dependency names shadow project names in bare-name lookups."," ","+## Wrapper callees (`resolver/callee.rs`)","+","+A `wrapperTypeArgument` component's props come from the type argument the extractor selected (`extractor/wrapper.rs`), plus what its callee's result type adds. The extractor records every generic function's result in `SourceData::function_results`: the return annotation, or the type its only top-level `return … as T` asserts. `callee::result_props` binds the callee's type parameters to the call's type arguments, follows aliases to the first React component type (`NamedExoticComponent<P>`, `FC<P>`, a call signature, …) and adds P's inline object members (`{ component?: any; renderRoot?: … }`) that the component doesn't already have. Other members of P (`Payload['props']`, `RefAttributes<…>`) are left to the selection, so this never warns. The callee's file is a recorded dependency, so editing the factory re-resolves the components it builds; `follow_reexports` treats a recorded function as a declaration, so `export *` barrels reach it.","+","+**Gap:** a result type asserted through an alias declared inside the function body (Mantine's `polymorphicFactory`) is not reachable.","+"," ## The three-tier data model this resolver operates on"," "," - `CollectedType` / `CollectedTypeAlias` — what the extractor produced: structural, not yet resolved, may reference cross-file names."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c56ee074-e080-4d0a-9b67-aa7030f40558","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/wrapper-callee-result","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
