ype":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/wrapper-callee-result","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"96bcbea2-4a27-4a5d-a97b-493e837b8b4a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKniNnUnHbrVzNsqGwi2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LFkaNVS7APdmHXWzdFPsEg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"/usr/bin/git push -q -u origin feat/wrapper-callee-result","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1406,"cache_read_input_tokens":571091,"output_tokens":1710,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1406,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1710,"cache_read_input_tokens":571091,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1406},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LFkaNVS7APdmHXWzdFPsEg":{"command":"/usr/bin/git push -q -u origin feat/wrapper-callee-result","dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0a3fd256-a111-4839-9595-b09185d27866","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgKniNLgbnqhspXCAyNat","requestRef":"0a7fda17-6b4b-4486-98f5-0f0638f47992","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"adr","type":"assistant","uuid":"54a36734-386d-4c0d-b263-5714845a578e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:20:06.645Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/wrapper-callee-result","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"54a36734-386d-4c0d-b263-5714845a578e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKniNnUnHbrVzNsqGwi2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G2YP5G6HKQpigHH6X66uDN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr-callee.md","content":"Stacked on #128.\n\n## Why\n\nreact-docgen-typescript reads a component's props from its type, so for `const Button = factory<ButtonFactory>(render)` it reports what `factory` returns. Mantine's `factory` returns `MantineComponent<Payload>`, whose props add `component` and `renderRoot` to the payload's props. We only read the payload, so every Mantine factory component missed those two props: 379 of the 443 own props we missed on Mantine core.\n\n## What\n\n- **Extractor:** every generic function records its result type in `SourceData::function_results`: its return annotation, or the type its only top-level `return … as T` asserts. A `wrapperTypeArgument` mapping records its callee and the call's type arguments. `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` 17 → 18.\n- **Resolver (`resolver/callee.rs`):** binds the callee's type parameters to the call's type arguments, follows aliases to the first React component type (`NamedExoticComponent<P>`, `FC<P>`, a call signature, …) and adds P's inline object members the component doesn't already have. Its own props win a clash. Other members of P (`Payload['props']`, `RefAttributes`) are left to the existing selection, so nothing new warns. No library names.\n- **Barrels:** `follow_reexports` only accepted a wildcard hop to a file declaring the name as a type, so `export * from './factory'` never reached a function. It now counts a recorded function too.\n- **Watch:** the callee's file is a recorded dependency, so editing the factory re-resolves the components it builds.\n\n## Effect (five corpora with dependencies installed, before = #128)\n\n| Corpus | Prop sets changed | Wall time (hyperfine, mean of 40) |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| mantine | 182 components gain `component` and `renderRoot` | 64.2 → 64.9 ms |\n| chakra, shadcn, antd, spectrum | 0 | chakra 38.6 → 39.1 ms |\n\nAgainst react-docgen-typescript on the source-only Mantine mirror, missed own props fall from 443 to 83. What remains: 60 from `polymorphicFactory`, whose asserted result is an alias declared inside the function body (documented as a gap), and 19 from a few components built another way. Fixture snapshots are unchanged.\n\n## Verify\n\n- `pipeline::tests::a_wrapper_built_component_gets_the_props_its_callees_result_type_adds`: through two barrels, exact props (type, required, description) for a factory component, one whose own `component` prop wins, and one built by a callee with no known result; no warnings.\n- `watch::tests::editing_a_wrapper_callees_result_type_updates_the_components_it_builds`: editing only the factory updates `Button` and matches a cold `extract()`.\n- `extractor::tests::a_generic_functions_result_is_its_return_annotation_or_its_one_asserted_return`: exact recorded results; none for a non-generic function, an unasserted return or two returns.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace` (774 pass), `just lint doc-check typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1406,"cache_read_input_tokens":571091,"output_tokens":1710,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1406,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1710,"cache_read_input_tokens":571091,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1406},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01G2YP5G6HKQpigHH6X66uDN":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/pr-callee.md","content":"Stacked on #128.\n\n## Why\n\nreact-docgen-typescript reads a component's props from its type, so for `const Button = factory<ButtonFactory>(render)` it reports what `factory` returns. Mantine's `factory` returns `MantineComponent<Payload>`, whose props add `component` and `renderRoot` to the payload's props. We only read the payload, so every Mantine factory component missed those two props: 379 of the 443 own props we missed on Mantine core.\n\n## What\n\n- **Extractor:** every generic function records its result type in `SourceData::function_results`: its return annotation, or the type its only top-level `return … as T` asserts. A `wrapperTypeArgument` mapping records its callee and the call's type arguments. `CACHE_SCHEMA_VERSION` 17 → 18.\n- **Resolver (`resolver/callee.rs`):** binds the callee's type parameters to the call's type arguments, follows aliases to the first React component type (`NamedExoticComponent<P>`, `FC<P>`, a call signature, …) and adds P's inline object members the component doesn't already have. Its own props win a clash. Other members of P (`Payload['props']`, `RefAttributes`) are left to the existing selection, so nothing new warns. No library names.\n- **Barrels:** `follow_reexports` only accepted a wildcard hop to a file declaring the name as a type, so `export * from './factory'` never reached a function. It now counts a recorded function too.\n- **Watch:** the callee's file is a recorded dependency, so editing the factory re-resolves the components it builds.\n\n## Effect (five corpora with dependencies installed, before = #128)\n\n| Corpus | Prop sets changed | Wall time (hyperfine, mean of 40) |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| mantine | 182 components gain `component` and `renderRoot` | 64.2 → 64.9 ms |\n| chakra, shadcn, antd, spectrum | 0 | chakra 38.6 → 39.1 ms |\n\nAgainst react-docgen-typescript on the source-only Mantine mirror, missed own props fall from 443 to 83. What remains: 60 from `polymorphicFactory`, whose asserted result is an alias declared inside the function body (documented as a gap), and 19 from a few components built another way. Fixture snapshots are unchanged.\n\n## Verify\n\n- `pipeline::tests::a_wrapper_built_component_gets_the_props_its_callees_result_type_adds`: through two barrels, exact props (type, required, description) for a factory component, one whose own `component` prop wins, and one built by a callee with no known result; no warnings.\n- `watch::tests::editing_a_wrapper_callees_result_type_updates_the_components_it_builds`: editing only the factory updates `Button` and matches a cold `extract()`.\n- `extractor::tests::a_generic_functions_result_is_its_return_annotation_or_its_one_asserted_return`: exact recorded results; none for a non-generic function, an unasserted return or two returns.\n- `cargo nextest run --workspace` (774 pass), `just lint doc-check typos`.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0a3fd256-a111-4839-9595-b09185d27866","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgKniNLgbnqhspXCAyNat","requestRef":"0a7fda17-6b4b-4486-98f5-0f0638f47992","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"adr","type":"assistant","uuid":"a41da9b5-8ceb-4d2a-b2cc-75eca374f026","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:20:16.436Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"feat/wrapper-callee-result","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
